WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.780
“SCP-682 must be destroyed as soon as possible.”

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:11.280
So begins the SCP Foundation file on the dreaded
SCP - 682, a highly-intelligent reptilian

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:16.380
monster that has - despite the Foundation’s
best efforts - proved impossible to kill.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:21.420
It may not be the most dangerous SCP out there,
considering that some are capable of eliminating

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:26.040
entire realities, but it’s one of the most
iconic, and you’ve probably heard tales

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:30.840
of the monster that death forgot, and you
know exactly why everyone is so afraid of

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.120
the so-called “Hard to Kill Reptile”.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.020
It’s been subjected to some of the most
deadly weapons and traps the Foundation could

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.340
devise, and survived attacks from some of
its deadliest fellow SCPs.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:45.600
But before we tell you about the Foundation’s
many failed assassination attempts against

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.520
the so-called “Hard to Kill Reptile”,
we need a little more groundwork on what this

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:51.600
creature even is.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:57.000
The first thing to know about SCP - 682, is
that this thing wants you and everyone you

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:57.900
know dead.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:04.920
Unlike some other creatures like SCP - 096
and SCP - 173, which are murderous but exhibit

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:11.220
no real higher processing skills, SCP - 682
possesses cunning, advanced reasoning, and

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:13.260
even human-level logical intelligence.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:18.840
SCP - 682 can engage you in conversation,
but just talking to the creature calmly and

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:23.280
cordially will sometimes cause it to enter
its “rage state” where it becomes even

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.720
more dangerous and volatile.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:29.820
The beast is perpetually kept in a huge tank
of powerful hydrochloric acid, melting its

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:33.660
tissue to prevent it from reaching its full
potential and going on a rampage.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:38.640
The creature’s most terrifying asset, and
the reason it’s proven impossible to terminate

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:43.740
thus far, is its incredible adaptability to
any and all external stimuli.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:50.040
682 is a reactive being, capable of not only
surviving and regenerating from all attacks,

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:54.300
but often incorporating those attacks into
its own wide arsenal.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:58.260
In other words, if you’re hoping to kill
this thing, you better kill it on the first

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:04.080
hit - cause if you don’t, you better believe
it’s gonna hit you back a hundred times

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:04.680
harder.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:10.380
This brings us to the main event: Some of
the SCP Foundation’s most ambitious and

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:15.960
frightening attempts to terminate SCP - 682,
or even understand how it could theoretically

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:16.680
be terminated.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:21.600
There are quite literally too many unsuccessful
attempts for us to list them all here, so

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.880
think of this as a highlight&nbsp;
reel of the Foundation’s&nbsp;

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:25.200
most prominent failures.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:31.380
682 was first cross-tested with SCP - 017,
a humanoid shadow-entity shown to be able

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.920
to consume matter with its shadows and leave
no traces behind.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:41.520
Tests on tissue samples from 682 showed that
SCP - 017 was able to consume said tissues

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:42.840
with no adverse effects.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:48.840
However, when SCP - 017 was placed into the
containment chamber with the actual creature,

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:54.000
682 let out a horrific roar that was so loud
it damaged nearby audio equipment.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:00.480
SCP - 017 fled to the corner of the room,
and 682, in its rage state, attempted to breach

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.140
containment.

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:06.240
Agents managed to suppress and remove the
creature, but no meaningful damage was logged.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.680
Attempt failed.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:13.500
SCP - 173 - the Killer statue - was later
brought in, hoping that its thus-far impeccable

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.540
track recording for killing would hold strong.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:21.060
The second that 173 was introduced into the
testing area, 682 retreated to the far wall

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.800
and began screeching intensely.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:25.560
It was intelligent enough to know what it
was dealing with here.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:30.060
While the researchers and guards expected
an instantaneous reaction, there was actually

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:35.760
a stalemate for over six hours as 682 stared
at 173 continuously.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:40.800
Eventually, the tie was broken when Agents
shot out 682’s eyes with high-caliber sniper

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:44.340
rifles, breaking the line of sight and causing
173 to attack.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:49.500
Though 682 sustained damage to several parts
of its body while its eyes regenerated, the

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.700
creature was not killed.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:55.920
It then regenerated a number of eyes all over
its body, covered in a clear, armoured carapace

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.960
that made them resistant to bullets.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:03.300
The stalemate continued for an additional
twelve hours, as 682 maintained perpetual

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:03.780
eye contact.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:08.400
173 was eventually removed from the containment
unit, and the mission was aborted.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:09.840
Attempt failed.

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:15.540
In their desperation, the SCP Foundation resorted
to bringing in another dangerous and seemingly

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:22.740
unkillable monster to take on 682: SCP - 096,
also known as The Shy Guy.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:28.800
As astute SCP fans will already know, this
being kills anything that sees its face, with

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:33.840
no known exceptions - and when it enters its
attack mode, it’s thought to be quite literally

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.220
unstoppable.

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:38.100
Or, at least, it was.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:44.700
While SCP - 096 was able to destroy 85% of
682’s original body mass during their 27

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:49.140
hour battle, it was left&nbsp;
mentally broken - wounded,&nbsp;

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.520
and huddled in the corner.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:56.640
To this day, if ever confronted with SCP 682,
the Shy Guy reacts in pure terror, turning

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.380
away and clawing at his own face.

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:00.480
Attempt failed.

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:06.720
During a deadly containment breach, SCP - 682
also went head to head organically with another

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:12.660
iconic SCP hall-of-famer: SCP - 106, also
known as The Old Man.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:19.440
The Old Man and a shapeshifting, psionic anomaly
known as SCP - 953 broke into 682’s containment

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:19.740
cell.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:24.420
The Old Man pulled both of his fellow anomalous
combatants into his pocket dimension to continue

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:25.800
the battle on his terms.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:31.200
However, despite losing 67% of his body mass
during the ensuing pocket dimension showdown,

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:37.920
682 still prevailed - with the Old Man eventually
fleeing back to his cell, and 953 being collected

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:39.300
and taken away by agents.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:43.440
Once again, SCP - 682 continued to hold the
title.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:47.280
But it wasn’t just cross-testing experiments,
intentional or otherwise.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:52.860
The SCP Foundation’s quest to kill 682 lead
them to a number of more conventional murder

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:55.560
methods, all with varying degrees of success.

00:05:55.560 --> 00:06:01.020
Due to SCP - 682’s highly adaptive abilities,
some methods were discounted from the outset.

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:06.360
For example, launching a powerful thermonuclear
missile at the creature was soundly rejected

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:10.620
by O5 Command - on the premise that, if the
creature wasn’t destroyed and evolved to

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:15.060
the point where it could shrug off nukes,
humanity would be pretty much done for.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:19.320
Other ideas were abandoned just for being
too ridiculous - such as one researcher’s

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:22.620
suggestion to fly the creature through the
air and drop it from a considerable height,

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:25.020
hoping to kill it with the high-altitude impact.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:28.080
I’m not sure we even need to tell you why
that’s a terrible idea.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:33.960
But, during the experiments on SCP - 682,
the studies ranged from honest to incompetent

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.520
to straight-up evil.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:40.980
One guest researcher fed two small, innocent
children to the creature, just to see what

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:41.340
would happen.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:45.660
He was then himself fed to the creature for
his sadistic behaviour, which was viewed as

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:47.640
getting in the way of his professional conduct.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:51.480
After all, the Foundation is meant to be cold,
not cruel.

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:55.680
It was SCP - 682 that had the monopoly on
cruelty.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:57.780
Memetic Kill agents were a resounding failure.

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:00.540
They attempted to dismember 682 with a powerful&nbsp;

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.880
laser, only to have the&nbsp;
creature develop reflective

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:07.260
surfaces that displaced the beam and caused
catastrophic damage to the area around it.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:11.460
They attempted to kill the creature by sucking
all the air out of its containment facility

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:16.920
and creating a vacuum, but it expelled a dangerous
gaseous compound that reacted violently and

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:19.740
exploded when air was once again introduced
into the room.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:26.100
The Foundation used high-precision blades
to slice SCP - 682 into approximately 12,000

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:28.260
pieces then separated these pieces.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:31.800
Unsurprisingly by this point, this attempt
also failed.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:36.300
The 12,000 pieces reformed a short while later
into the fully operational killing machine

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:37.860
we all know and fear.

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:42.480
In one particularly frightening display of
intelligence and adaptability, the Foundation

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:47.220
attempted to kill 682 with extreme heat, but
it shielded itself by developing a secondary

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:49.620
carapace composed of solid helium.

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:53.160
When personnel entered the room following
the failed attempt on the creature’s life,

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:58.440
it shattered its helium carapace into deadly
shards that fired around the room and shredded

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:00.660
all Foundation personnel in attendance.

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:04.980
It’d set a trap, and that trap had been
wildly successful.

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:09.720
The creature’s ability to adapt to seemingly
any offensive is unparalleled, to the point

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:14.460
where Foundation staff have no idea how to
classify this creature - whether it’s organic,

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:18.720
inorganic, or even alive at all based on any
definitions we could understand.

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:22.500
At every turn, the creature just raised more
questions.

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:23.640
What is it?

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:26.460
Is it possible to destroy it at all by any
means?

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:28.500
Who was even trying to kill who here?

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:33.960
Because it certainly seemed like SCP - 682
had a masterful K/D ratio by now.

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:38.460
More extreme feats of cross-testing continued
in the Foundation’s growing desperation

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:39.900
to eliminate this monster.

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:45.960
SCP - 162, which is a hypnotic ball of sharp
objects, hooks, and high-tension fishing line,

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:48.540
was introduced to 682’s containment cell.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:53.280
The hooks latched onto the creature and tore
huge portions off, including its entire lower

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:54.900
jaw and one of its limbs.

00:08:54.900 --> 00:09:01.680
However, 682 was still able to breach containment,
kill eleven people, and badly wound 86 others.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:04.860
It regenerated its severe injuries in no time.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:09.420
The beast was even taken to the domain of
The Gate Guardian, one of the proposals for

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:10.800
SCP - 001.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:15.840
The Guardian has a flaming sword hotter than
the sun, capable of destroying its targets

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.040
on an atomic level.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:21.480
Naturally, SCP - 682 survived and regenerated.

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:29.100
Perhaps the most fascinating cross-test of
all was between 682 and SCP - 053, who manifests

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:31.860
as a kind, innocent little&nbsp;
girl with the unfortunate&nbsp;

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:33.900
condition of causing homicidal tendencies

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:37.140
in all who come into contact with her for
more than ten minutes.

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:41.760
The people with these tendencies would then
attempt to harm the girl, but would immediately

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:45.120
drop dead shortly after, leaving the girl
intact.

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:50.160
The researchers present anticipated two possible
outcomes here: The optimistic outcome, in

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:53.940
which 682 entered a rage state, attacked 053,
and died for good.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:59.640
And the realistic outcome, in which 682 attacked
053, possibly experienced some minor injury

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:03.240
or nothing at all, and 053 had to be removed
from the containment cell.

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:04.860
But that didn’t happen.

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:09.480
What did occur was considerably more shocking
than any kind of violence.

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:15.480
When 053 entered 682’s containment chamber,
the monster became uncharacteristically docile.

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:20.700
Researchers and staff were baffled, and watched
with amazement as 053 approached the terrifying,

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:25.260
immortal, mass-murdering monster...and began
to play with it.

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:29.220
682 even allowed 053 to draw on its face with
crayons.

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:33.600
Researchers thought they must’ve been dreaming,
seeing this surreal display play out.

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:37.500
053 even appeared to have affection for this
unkillable misanthrope.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:41.760
It was a single act in defiance of everything
they thought they knew.

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:47.280
When Foundation personnel entered the containment
cell to separate the two, 682 went ballistic

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:48.720
and killed multiple guards.

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:52.740
053 also wept, sad at being separated from
her new friend.

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:58.680
To this day, despite further testing, the
Foundation has no idea how or why this happened.

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:05.100
Like many details surrounding SCP - 682, it’s
shrouded in deeply frustrating mystery.

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:11.880
And so the tale of SCP - 682 continues, in
spite of the Foundation’s best efforts.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:17.220
The monster continues to breach containment
and slaughter with some regularity, taking

00:11:17.220 --> 00:11:23.040
out its seemingly limitless hatred for not
only human beings, but anything that dares

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:24.360
draw breath.

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:29.580
Nobody knows where exactly the creature is
from, what its true nature is, or why its

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:33.960
ability to adapt and regenerate far exceeds
any known organism on this planet.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:39.480
Perhaps one day, through enough research and
cross testing, we can someday answer these

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:47.040
questions with scientific precision, but until
then, we only have one answer: Hatred never

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:47.520
dies.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:57.180
Here we go again. It’s time to return to the&nbsp;
acid-filled containment chamber of SCP-682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.180 --> 00:12:03.720
more commonly known as the Hard to Destroy&nbsp;
Reptile. We’ve spoken about him and the ways&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:10.320
The SCP Foundation has attempted to destroy him&nbsp;
in a previous video. But as we said back then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:15.180
we really only scratched the surface&nbsp;
of the huge number of insane ways&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:20.160
the Foundation has tried to wipe this&nbsp;
ornery lizard off the face of the earth.

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:25.380
Today, we’re filling in some of the cracks.&nbsp;
Let’s take a look at the secret test logs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:35.040
detailing the Foundation’s unsuccessful&nbsp;
quest to finally destroy SCP-682. If you’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:41.580
a real SCP Expert, you’re likely to recognize&nbsp;
some familiar faces we meet along the way...

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:47.280
Esteemed Foundation Researcher Dr. Alto&nbsp;
Clef - famed for his somewhat unconventional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:53.100
personality - entered the test chamber to see&nbsp;
if he could intimidate the beast to death. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:59.340
resulted in a long staring contest between&nbsp;
Dr. Clef and 682, towards the end of which,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:04.800
Dr. Clef began to lose his nerve. He&nbsp;
tried to leave the room, only to find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:10.620
that the door was locked, causing him to swear&nbsp;
loudly. Dr. Clef, who always tries to find the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:16.620
most direct solution to his problems, blew up&nbsp;
the door with plastic explosives and ran off.

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:22.740
Test failed.
Next came SCP-662, a silver&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:29.280
hand bell that summons the supernaturally helpful&nbsp;
butler, Mr. Deeds. When Mr. Deeds was summoned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:35.940
Foundation researchers asked him if he could kill&nbsp;
SCP-682. Deeds politely explained that he wouldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:43.440
be capable of killing 682, it’s just too strong.&nbsp;
When asked if he could at least incapacitate 682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:49.860
he replied that the best way to do this would&nbsp;
be to poison himself and allow 682 to eat his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:54.960
body. But this, he reminded, would only&nbsp;
be a temporary problem for the lizard.

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:59.820
Test failed.
The Foundation brought in SCP-689,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:05.580
a terrifying soapstone statue of a sitting&nbsp;
skeleton that can kill you if you see it and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:11.460
then stop paying attention to it. 682 first&nbsp;
observed the statue, and then the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:17.640
turned off the lights. When they turned them&nbsp;
back on, SCP-682 appeared to be dead in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:23.640
puddle of gray and black liquid. D-Classes were&nbsp;
sent in to confirm that 682 was actually dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:30.240
but it instead got up and killed them. Researchers&nbsp;
theorized that 682’s definition of “life” is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:36.000
not quite the same as ours, rendering&nbsp;
689’s death-related powers ineffective.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:37.260
Test failed.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:44.280
SCP-807 was next up to bat. This is&nbsp;
an anomalous salmon-colored ceramic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:49.440
dinner plate with the words "Last Chance&nbsp;
Diner" printed on the edges in white. Any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:54.480
food placed on it becomes irresistible by any&nbsp;
definition, but when the food is consumed it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:59.220
causes immediate cardiac arrest due to the&nbsp;
sudden clogging of the arteries with fat.

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:05.280
Researchers made a meal known as the&nbsp;
“682 Special” - 10 kg of rotten meat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:11.340
and sharpened bone splinters, 10 L of&nbsp;
rancid mayonnaise, 1 L potassium cyanide,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:16.440
and 1 kg morphine hydrochloride,&nbsp;
combined into a solid mass and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:23.340
transmuted by 807. When 682 first consumed&nbsp;
this disgusting meal, it seemed to collapse.

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:29.220
However, when D-Classes were sent in to see&nbsp;
whether 682 was truly out for the count,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:34.740
multiple holes opened in its body. These&nbsp;
holes fired out high-pressure jets of blood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:41.520
killing the nearby D-Classes and destroying&nbsp;
the containment cell. 682 was fine afterwards.

00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:44.880
Test failed.
To kill 682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:49.980
it seemed that the Foundation really needed&nbsp;
to have God on their side. So they tried to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.980 --> 00:15:57.240
recruit SCP-343, also known as “God”, to&nbsp;
help them destroy the beast. However, when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.240 --> 00:16:02.100
he entered the containment chamber, he somehow&nbsp;
couldn’t even see the beast. When researchers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:07.800
asked him whether he could kill 682, God replied,&nbsp;
“He's not one of mine. Deal with him yourself."

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:09.300
Test failed.

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:18.180
Next, the Foundation recruited SCP-524: A small&nbsp;
white rabbit that can eat literally anything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:24.540
including itself, without being harmed. The&nbsp;
rabbit was released into SCP-682’s chamber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:30.960
at which point it approached 682 and began to&nbsp;
eat one of its legs. 682 roared in pain and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:37.080
scuttled up the wall, out of 524’s reach, where&nbsp;
it remained for a number of hours. At this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:42.780
SCP-524 seemed to become bored, and began eating&nbsp;
its way out of containment through a nearby wall.

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:44.280
Test failed.

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:48.660
Maybe the luck of the Irish was what the&nbsp;
Foundation needed to finally put this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:48.660 --> 00:16:55.320
monster to rest. They recruited SCP-1933, a&nbsp;
fat man dressed as Santa Claus whose bodily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:55.320 --> 00:17:01.620
fluids are entirely the alcoholic beverage known&nbsp;
as Irish Cream. However, if enough of this Irish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:07.740
cream is fed to something, all of their bodily&nbsp;
fluids will become Irish cream, killing them.

00:17:07.740 --> 00:17:16.140
The Foundation fed large quantities of this&nbsp;
Irish cream to SCP-682. At first, it appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:24.420
intoxicated, a promising sign. However, it vomited&nbsp;
out a massive quantity of SCP-1933 bodily fluids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:29.520
turning the walls of its cell into Irish cream&nbsp;
and allowing it to escape and wreak havoc.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:31.080
Test failed.&nbsp;

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:39.120
The Foundation recruited the help of SCP-2337,&nbsp;
an intelligent corn crake known as Dr. Spanko,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:44.040
with a voice so loud it can quite literally&nbsp;
talk its victims to death if it speaks to them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:50.820
for an extended period of time. It was sent&nbsp;
into SCP-682’s chamber to destroy the beast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:56.160
but 682 just told it to leave, and the&nbsp;
talkative bird obliged - by blowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:56.160 --> 00:18:02.340
away one of the chamber walls with a yell,&nbsp;
allowing SCP-682 to breach containment again.

00:18:04.740 --> 00:18:06.193
Test failed.

00:18:06.193 --> 00:18:08.520
As you can probably sympathize with right now,&nbsp;
the Foundation researchers were starting to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:15.480
a little frustrated with their lack of progress.&nbsp;
They even pitched the possibility of sending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:22.380
SCP-682 into an alternate dimension, perhaps&nbsp;
into a stalemate against its alternate self.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:29.340
But this pitch was shot down by the O5 Council on&nbsp;
the grounds that it was way, way, way too risky.

00:18:29.340 --> 00:18:33.840
Back to the drawing board. By which&nbsp;
we mean, they literally transformed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:41.130
SCP-682’s skin into a kind of drawing board.
SCP-2521 is an anomaly that manifests any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:45.780
time information about it is recorded, and&nbsp;
immediately grabs the source of the information,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:45.780 --> 00:18:51.180
wrapping it in its tendrils and taking it&nbsp;
away with it. The Foundation sought to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:51.180 --> 00:18:57.780
advantage of this by using a laser to cut&nbsp;
this anomalous information into SCP-682’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:57.780 --> 00:19:01.500
side. However, this didn’t have the&nbsp;
results that they were hoping for.

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:06.900
SCP-2521 did turn up to take the&nbsp;
information, but it only took the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:13.200
skin on which the information was carved.&nbsp;
682 survived and quickly grew back its skin.

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:19.140
Test failed.
Researchers suggested tracking down SCP-169,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:25.860
an obscenely massive underwater creature known&nbsp;
as The Leviathan, and feeding 682 to the beast.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:25.860 --> 00:19:32.640
However, this idea was immediately shot down&nbsp;
by the O5 Council. If 682 did what it did best:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:40.260
Surviving the attack and acting accordingly,&nbsp;
perhaps by growing to the size of SCP-169,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:46.920
it would likely trigger an XK-Class End of the&nbsp;
World Scenario. It simply was not worth the risk.&nbsp;

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:56.400
The Foundation released two specimens of SCP-939&nbsp;
into 682’s test chamber. These voice-imitating,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:56.400 --> 00:20:00.660
amnesia-inducing monsters have&nbsp;
caused huge damage to human targets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:06.960
so maybe they had some hope against 682.&nbsp;
This hope turned out to be misplaced:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:14.880
Both specimens seemed extremely distressed by&nbsp;
682’s presence and refused to engage. 682 did not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:14.880 --> 00:20:21.180
have that same refusal. It charged in and brutally&nbsp;
killed both, before devouring their corpses.

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:25.920
Test failed.
In a very well-documented case, the adorable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:33.000
SCP-999 was introduced into 682’s test chamber.&nbsp;
The unassailable good vibes provided by 999,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:40.200
as well as an intense tickle fight, did actually&nbsp;
lead to the temporary incapacitation of SCP-682.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:46.980
However, the otherwise wholesome incident ended in&nbsp;
tragedy when 682 adapted to the good vibes and was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:46.980 --> 00:20:52.140
able to release a kind of violent laughter&nbsp;
wave. This incapacitated much of the staff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:58.560
and allowed 682 to breach containment and go on&nbsp;
another killing spree, before being recontained.

00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:01.073
Test, once again, failed.

00:21:01.073 --> 00:21:04.020
One of the closest attempts the&nbsp;
Foundation ever had involved SCP-294,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:08.640
an anomalous coffee machine that can&nbsp;
produce any liquid typed into its keypad.

00:21:08.640 --> 00:21:15.660
Foundation researchers requested “SCP-682&nbsp;
Killer” from the machine, and were astounded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:15.660 --> 00:21:25.320
at the results. During tests on SCP-682 tissue&nbsp;
samples, the liquid was capable of causing 682&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:31.320
tissue to decay and crumble. Tests on the living&nbsp;
creature were similarly promising. The acid in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:39.660
682’s tank was receded, and one liter of SCP-682&nbsp;
Killer was poured onto it, causing that portion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:47.340
of its flesh to immediately decay. When the acid&nbsp;
was returned, this portion dissolved instantly.

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:58.680
Scientists believe that if they could one day&nbsp;
get a large enough quantity of this liquid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:58.680 --> 00:22:04.200
they might have a viable option.&nbsp;
But until then, the tests march on.

00:22:05.520 --> 00:22:09.720
They introduced SCP-055, the self-keeping&nbsp;
secret, into the containment chamber of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:19.161
SCP-682. We don’t really know what happened,&nbsp;
but seeing as 682 isn’t dead, we now know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:19.161 --> 00:22:29.460
055 can’t kill it. That and the fact it isn’t&nbsp;
round is pretty much all we know about SCP-055.

00:22:32.880 --> 00:22:34.260
Test failed.

00:22:38.340 --> 00:22:45.660
Next came SCP-082, also known as Fernand the&nbsp;
Cannibal. Fernand was first presented a piece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:45.660 --> 00:22:50.640
of flesh from 682, but rather than eating&nbsp;
it, he inspected it and began to express&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:50.640 --> 00:22:55.620
joy that his “friend” still lived. When&nbsp;
introduced into 682’s testing chamber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:55.620 --> 00:23:01.080
Fernand attempted to subdue the lizard&nbsp;
and use it as his steed. 682 expressed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:01.080 --> 00:23:06.360
an intense hatred of both Fernand and the&nbsp;
idea of being Fernand’s steed, so the two of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:12.180
them engaged in combat. Mobile Task Forces were&nbsp;
eventually brought in to subdue both subjects.

00:23:12.180 --> 00:23:15.420
In the debrief interview, both hinted&nbsp;
that the two of them shared history&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:15.420 --> 00:23:19.980
prior to containment. 682 was&nbsp;
reluctant to talk about it.

00:23:19.980 --> 00:23:23.220
Test failed.

00:23:23.220 --> 00:23:28.980
Researchers were becoming extremely frustrated&nbsp;
with SCP-682’s unwillingness to die,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:28.980 --> 00:23:35.460
so they called in an SCP who responded&nbsp;
to reason much better: SCP-049,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:35.460 --> 00:23:41.160
the Plague Doctor. This sinister surgeon can&nbsp;
kill with a touch, and the Foundation hoped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:41.160 --> 00:23:48.600
that would extend to 682. However, the result&nbsp;
was a dud. The Plague Doctor did touch 682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:48.600 --> 00:23:53.940
but it experienced no adverse effects, and&nbsp;
even swiped at the doctor. Upon leaving,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:53.940 --> 00:24:00.960
049 reported feeling “emotionally&nbsp;
disturbed” by his encounter with SCP-682.

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:04.440
Yep, you guessed it: Test failed.

00:24:04.440 --> 00:24:08.760
If it gives you any indication of just how&nbsp;
desperate the researchers were at this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:08.760 --> 00:24:14.400
Dr. Richard Graham pondered whether introducing&nbsp;
SCP-682 to a human with just as pessimistic and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:14.400 --> 00:24:20.040
misanthropic feelings as itself would somehow&nbsp;
pacify it. They sent in a particularly nasty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:20.040 --> 00:24:25.500
D-Class, and the two spoke. Fascinatingly,&nbsp;
682 didn’t attempt to harm this D-Class,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:25.500 --> 00:24:29.460
they just shared their profane and bleak&nbsp;
sentiments about the human race with one another.

00:24:29.460 --> 00:24:35.580
However, some of 682’s opinions were a&nbsp;
little too spicy for this D-Class. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:35.580 --> 00:24:40.200
listening to the reptile speak for twenty&nbsp;
minutes, the D-Class fell into a catatonic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:40.200 --> 00:24:43.980
state from the sheer depression&nbsp;
of it all. He died not long after.

00:24:43.980 --> 00:24:51.180
One anonymous researcher suggested perhaps the&nbsp;
worst idea of all: Letting SCP-682 out into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:51.180 --> 00:24:55.860
wild. Not even to really terminate it, just&nbsp;
to see what it does. The anonymous scientist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:55.860 --> 00:24:59.220
figured there would be some merit in&nbsp;
analyzing the creature’s behavior.

00:25:08.520 --> 00:25:13.200
As you can probably guess, this&nbsp;
request was shot down by the O5&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:13.200 --> 00:25:17.340
Council. The note attached to the request&nbsp;
by one of its members summed it up best:

00:25:17.340 --> 00:25:21.900
“I'll tell you what it'll do. It'll go out for&nbsp;
a nice stroll, murder a few innocent people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:21.900 --> 00:25:27.480
go fishing, slaughter a few more innocent people,&nbsp;
start up a tech-company, eat a few more innocent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:27.480 --> 00:25:33.180
people, go on a vacation to Florida, dismember a&nbsp;
few more innocent people! I swear, when I find out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:33.180 --> 00:25:38.340
who wrote this, you can personally enter 682's&nbsp;
containment chamber to analyze him yourself!”

00:25:38.340 --> 00:25:46.440
Even this isn’t covering every&nbsp;
single attempt to terminate SCP-682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:46.440 --> 00:25:53.880
but all attempts have either been failures or too&nbsp;
risky or potentially unviable to even try. Sadly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:53.880 --> 00:26:00.840
for the SCP Foundation and the human race, it’s&nbsp;
likely we’ll be dealing with SCP-682 for a long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:00.840 --> 00:26:01.680
time to come. How do you think 682 could finally&nbsp;
be killed? Let us know down in the comments below!

00:26:01.680 --> 00:26:03.780
SCP-682.

00:26:03.780 --> 00:26:05.880
Does it even require an introduction?

00:26:05.880 --> 00:26:11.700
The SCP Foundation thinks this cantankerous
reptile needs a serious attitude adjustment

00:26:11.700 --> 00:26:15.120
- By which we mean, they really, really want
to kill it.

00:26:15.120 --> 00:26:19.680
But as you might have seen in our previous
videos on the subject, they don’t call this

00:26:19.680 --> 00:26:22.620
monstrosity the “Hard to Destroy Reptile”
for nothing.

00:26:22.620 --> 00:26:28.320
That’s why we’ve done what the Foundation
isn’t allowed to - we outsourced the dirty

00:26:28.320 --> 00:26:30.900
job of squashing this lizard to all of you!

00:26:30.900 --> 00:26:36.900
We made a community post asking for your ideas
on how this scaly abomination can finally

00:26:36.900 --> 00:26:40.140
be destroyed, and you delivered big time!

00:26:40.140 --> 00:26:44.340
A truly staggering amount with over 6,000
comments!

00:26:44.340 --> 00:26:49.320
Now let’s see if we can finally get our
answer, because believe us, the Foundation

00:26:49.320 --> 00:26:51.060
is desperate at this point.

00:26:51.060 --> 00:26:55.440
Idk what to write for a name said, “The
most effective way that Dr Bright approves

00:26:55.440 --> 00:26:57.060
of: CHAINSAW CANNON.”

00:26:57.060 --> 00:27:03.000
As awesome as a chainsaw cannon would probably
be to use, it sadly wouldn’t be very effective

00:27:03.000 --> 00:27:04.980
against SCP-682.

00:27:04.980 --> 00:27:10.200
Chainsaws are blades, and we know from the
termination test logs that blades have been

00:27:10.200 --> 00:27:10.980
ineffective.

00:27:10.980 --> 00:27:17.520
Even when SCP-682 is chopped up into tiny
little pieces, those pieces have a nasty habit

00:27:17.520 --> 00:27:21.600
of reforming into the big, ugly monster we
all know and fear.

00:27:21.600 --> 00:27:26.220
AwesomeCardinal said, “The SCP Foundation
could try to bring it to the void in Russia

00:27:26.220 --> 00:27:27.600
where the Pattern Screamers are.”

00:27:27.600 --> 00:27:31.680
This was a popular idea and the Foundation
actually tried this.

00:27:31.680 --> 00:27:38.220
The SCP being referred to here is SCP-3930,
a big ol’ pile of nothing in Russia that

00:27:38.220 --> 00:27:40.800
causes things inside it to stop existing.

00:27:40.800 --> 00:27:45.720
When they threw SCP-682 inside, it technically
did stop existing.

00:27:45.720 --> 00:27:51.360
Despite this, it could still be perceived,
and still caused the deaths of all surrounding

00:27:51.360 --> 00:27:52.020
researchers.

00:27:52.020 --> 00:27:57.300
Fifteen hours later, it just reappeared in
its containment chamber, apparently totally

00:27:57.300 --> 00:27:57.660
fine.

00:27:57.660 --> 00:28:01.080
You can probably see why the Foundation is
frustrated by this thing.

00:28:01.080 --> 00:28:03.900
Sc0r3cr0w and Friends said, “Black hole.

00:28:03.900 --> 00:28:04.920
Need I say more?”

00:28:04.920 --> 00:28:07.680
You may need to say a little more.

00:28:07.680 --> 00:28:12.300
For starters, there would be logistical issues
in actually getting the creature anywhere

00:28:12.300 --> 00:28:13.620
near a black hole.

00:28:13.620 --> 00:28:18.420
But there’s also the concern that it may
just adapt its body to respond to the intense

00:28:18.420 --> 00:28:20.760
gravity present near a black hole.

00:28:20.760 --> 00:28:25.980
Or, even scarier, somehow adapts to reproduce
the powers of a black hole.

00:28:25.980 --> 00:28:30.420
It probably wouldn’t be worth the risk of
ending up with a reptile capable of creating

00:28:30.420 --> 00:28:31.860
gamma ray bursts.

00:28:31.860 --> 00:28:36.600
StellarSolar Sky said, “Put the reptile
inside nuclear fusion and watch its particles

00:28:36.600 --> 00:28:37.200
disappear.”

00:28:37.200 --> 00:28:42.600
The Foundation tried something pretty close
to this, by trying to put it inside SCP-536

00:28:42.600 --> 00:28:47.640
- A chamber where they can use dials to control
the physical constants within.

00:28:48.420 --> 00:28:54.060
They increased the speed of light and nuclear
force within the chamber, which caused SCP-682

00:28:54.060 --> 00:28:59.280
to disintegrate until all that was left was
a piece of matter 1% of its original size.

00:28:59.280 --> 00:29:02.940
However, the creature then reformed and killed
the researchers.

00:29:02.940 --> 00:29:08.100
Later tests showed that its body had become
an unknown form of matter, held together by

00:29:08.100 --> 00:29:12.360
quantum effects impossible to unravel with
our current understanding of science.

00:29:12.360 --> 00:29:16.860
Bray of fun said, “So you know that coffee
machine thing that is 294?

00:29:16.860 --> 00:29:21.600
Type in "682 killing substance" and repeat
that until you have enough to fill its entire

00:29:21.600 --> 00:29:22.800
room, then fill it.”

00:29:22.800 --> 00:29:29.520
They did actually try this, and the resulting
substance was effective in damaging SCP-682’s

00:29:29.520 --> 00:29:30.000
tissue.

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:34.200
However, the one problem is that it’s extremely
difficult to produce enough of this stuff

00:29:34.200 --> 00:29:36.240
to actually submerge the creature.

00:29:36.240 --> 00:29:41.700
Worse still, if enough of it was made to cause
significant damage to the body of SCP-682,

00:29:41.700 --> 00:29:47.040
it may adapt to the chemical as a defense
mechanism, making it ineffective as a weapon.

00:29:47.040 --> 00:29:52.800
Its adaptive ability is truly SCP-682’s
greatest asset when it comes to thwarting

00:29:52.800 --> 00:29:55.200
the Foundation’s constant attempts to kill
it.

00:29:55.200 --> 00:29:57.900
Alex Webb said, “Ask it kindly to die.”

00:29:57.900 --> 00:30:02.940
We don’t believe that the Foundation has
ever actually tried this one, but just based

00:30:02.940 --> 00:30:08.700
on the fact that SCP-682 is a huge jerk on
top of being an omnicidal monster, he probably

00:30:08.700 --> 00:30:11.100
wouldn’t respond to polite requests.

00:30:11.100 --> 00:30:15.120
iFlashboy said, “I wonder if Doom Slayer
could defeat the reptile.

00:30:15.120 --> 00:30:20.460
He’s torn through every demon in hell, and
even titans, so would 682 be a challenge or

00:30:20.460 --> 00:30:22.260
just another Tuesday for the slayer?”

00:30:22.260 --> 00:30:24.420
That’s a slightly trickier one.

00:30:24.420 --> 00:30:27.120
Of course, since they exist&nbsp;
in different universes,&nbsp;

00:30:27.120 --> 00:30:29.100
we’ll never see an official battle between

00:30:29.100 --> 00:30:31.500
the Doom Slayer and SCP-682.

00:30:31.500 --> 00:30:36.480
However, given that the Doom Slayer’s weapons
are all conventional - meaning, largely based

00:30:36.480 --> 00:30:41.340
around slashing, crushing, shooting, and blasting
- we don’t know whether he’d actually

00:30:41.340 --> 00:30:43.140
be able to slay the beast.

00:30:43.140 --> 00:30:46.620
That being said, we don’t know if 682 could
kill him, either.

00:30:46.620 --> 00:30:49.440
We could have a stalemate on our hands here...

00:30:49.440 --> 00:30:54.120
Amanda Breneman said, “I asked my sister
(who’s never heard of SCP’s) this question,

00:30:54.120 --> 00:30:56.700
and her answer was “You hit it again”.”

00:30:56.700 --> 00:31:00.660
Amanda, your sister may be the one to finally
stop this creature.

00:31:00.660 --> 00:31:04.800
Getting the two of them in the same room may
be the biggest logistical problem here.

00:31:04.800 --> 00:31:10.800
Samuel Pascual said, “Throwing him down
SCP-087, so he suffers and is contained once

00:31:10.800 --> 00:31:13.440
and for all in the improbable case he is still
alive.”

00:31:13.440 --> 00:31:19.980
SCP-087 - the Endless Staircase - can be a
dangerous anomaly for humans who don’t know

00:31:19.980 --> 00:31:20.880
what they’re getting into.

00:31:20.880 --> 00:31:26.940
However, SCP-682 would likely detect the threat
far earlier than any human, and then breach

00:31:26.940 --> 00:31:27.540
containment.

00:31:27.540 --> 00:31:30.480
It’s definitely gotten out of stickier situations.

00:31:30.480 --> 00:31:35.100
Yashasheree Charya said, “Send him to endless
IKEA where he will be trapped forever.”

00:31:35.100 --> 00:31:41.820
Much like SCP-087, the Endless Ikea wouldn’t
pose the same threat to SCP-682 as it would

00:31:41.820 --> 00:31:43.560
for the average human trapped inside.

00:31:43.560 --> 00:31:48.600
The staff would be no trouble for 682, and
it would be able to devote pretty much all

00:31:48.600 --> 00:31:50.940
of its time in there to finding a way out.

00:31:50.940 --> 00:31:55.140
And when he did finally break out, he’d
probably be armed with the terrifying knowledge

00:31:55.140 --> 00:31:57.660
of how to correctly assemble a svendendorkk.

00:31:57.660 --> 00:31:58.920
We shudder at the thought.

00:31:58.920 --> 00:32:01.620
Jack Lost said, “Oxygen Destroyer.

00:32:01.620 --> 00:32:05.040
Used to deal with another big lizard issue
back in 1954.”

00:32:05.040 --> 00:32:11.220
Sadly, this would also likely be an ineffective
weapon against SCP-682, because the creature

00:32:11.220 --> 00:32:16.140
thrives in anaerobic environments - seeing
as its native atmosphere seems to have no

00:32:16.140 --> 00:32:21.240
oxygen, and according to Foundation tests,
it can survive just fine in a vacuum.

00:32:21.240 --> 00:32:27.240
Whether SCP-682 could take Godzilla in a fight
is still up for debate and you can argue about

00:32:27.240 --> 00:32:30.060
which lizard would reign supreme in the comments.

00:32:30.060 --> 00:32:34.080
Ace Godwin said, “Just don’t kill him,
let him live, bro, he hasn't done anything

00:32:34.080 --> 00:32:34.680
wrong yet.

00:32:34.680 --> 00:32:36.000
Let him vibe in his chamber.”

00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:36.780
Wait a second…

00:32:36.780 --> 00:32:38.760
Did SCP-682 write this?

00:32:38.760 --> 00:32:40.200
Moving on.

00:32:40.200 --> 00:32:42.720
A lot of you said, “Throw him into the sun.”

00:32:42.720 --> 00:32:45.180
While the sun is a gigantic nuclear furnace&nbsp;

00:32:45.180 --> 00:32:47.460
where hydrogen is built&nbsp;
into helium at a temperature

00:32:48.000 --> 00:32:50.400
of millions of degrees, there is the the issue&nbsp;

00:32:50.400 --> 00:32:53.100
of it not only being beyond&nbsp;
difficult to incapacitate

00:32:53.100 --> 00:32:57.420
the creature for long enough to get it into
the rocket, but also the problem of the sun

00:32:57.420 --> 00:33:00.660
being 93 millions miles away from earth.

00:33:00.660 --> 00:33:06.420
It’s a long trip there no matter what, and
during that time, SCP-682 would almost definitely

00:33:06.420 --> 00:33:08.580
figure out a way to return to earth.

00:33:08.580 --> 00:33:13.380
It might even rewire the rocket and turn it
into its own personal vehicle, giving it the

00:33:13.380 --> 00:33:15.660
freedom to cause chaos around the solar system.

00:33:15.660 --> 00:33:22.260
And even if everything else went well, SCP-682
would still probably survive being thrown

00:33:22.260 --> 00:33:22.980
into the sun.

00:33:22.980 --> 00:33:27.240
After all, The Gate Guardian’s flaming sword
is described as being hotter than the sun,

00:33:27.240 --> 00:33:30.900
and it didn’t manage to kill the hard-to-destroy
reptile.

00:33:30.900 --> 00:33:35.580
PokemonRedBoy said, “Send him to Mars and
launch a nuke that can destroy a planet along

00:33:35.580 --> 00:33:36.600
with the SCP.”

00:33:36.600 --> 00:33:42.300
While a nuke capable of destroying the planet
Mars would also likely destroy SCP-682 in

00:33:42.300 --> 00:33:46.920
the process, the destruction of Mars itself
would likely cause such a catastrophic shift

00:33:46.920 --> 00:33:50.760
in our neck of the solar system that we’d
probably die with it.

00:33:50.760 --> 00:33:55.500
The question, at that point, is whether it’s
really worth killing ourselves to take down

00:33:55.500 --> 00:33:56.220
the lizard?

00:33:56.220 --> 00:34:00.900
Artemis said, “Let it live with 999 its
entire life and it's not a threat.”

00:34:00.900 --> 00:34:03.480
This is a double-edged sword.

00:34:03.480 --> 00:34:10.620
During their cross-test, SCP-999 did pacify
SCP-682 and put it in a state of bliss and

00:34:10.620 --> 00:34:12.060
laughter for a brief period.

00:34:12.060 --> 00:34:16.260
However, this actually resulted in a pretty
catastrophic tragedy, too.

00:34:16.260 --> 00:34:22.260
682 adapted to 999’s effects and released
a beam of laughter that incapacitated everyone

00:34:22.260 --> 00:34:26.220
around it, allowing it to escape and go on
a killing spree.

00:34:26.220 --> 00:34:29.100
So maybe the two are better kept apart...

00:34:29.100 --> 00:34:34.560
Dr. wasup said, “I'd give 682 a jar of pickles
to open, and the jar would be so tight that

00:34:35.160 --> 00:34:37.620
682 couldn't open it and&nbsp;
he would be so embarrassed&nbsp;

00:34:37.620 --> 00:34:39.360
by it that he would just destroy himself.”

00:34:39.360 --> 00:34:42.180
You may actually be on to something here.

00:34:42.180 --> 00:34:45.480
We know we’d be extremely embarrassed if
we couldn’t open the jar.

00:34:45.480 --> 00:34:47.880
But there are three major problems.

00:34:47.880 --> 00:34:50.340
One, where does one get such a jar?

00:34:50.340 --> 00:34:55.680
Can SCP-343 make a jar of pickles so difficult
to open that even he himself can’t open

00:34:55.680 --> 00:34:55.920
it?

00:34:55.920 --> 00:35:01.920
Two, we don’t know if SCP-682 likes pickles
enough to make opening the jar an attractive

00:35:01.920 --> 00:35:02.460
prospect.

00:35:02.460 --> 00:35:08.460
And three, if it does turn out it likes pickles,
it would probably just eat the jar too.

00:35:08.460 --> 00:35:15.480
Shuvro Bhattacharjee said, “To deal with
him in my opinion, send SCP-682 into SCP-3001,

00:35:15.480 --> 00:35:17.280
aka the Red Reality.

00:35:17.280 --> 00:35:18.420
That's my theory.”

00:35:18.420 --> 00:35:24.060
This could potentially be an effective method
of trapping SCP-682 for a period of time.

00:35:24.060 --> 00:35:28.620
However, the problem is that there’s no
reliable way to access the Red Reality.

00:35:28.620 --> 00:35:33.420
The only person who’s ever really been inside
is Robert Scranton, and he ended up there

00:35:33.420 --> 00:35:34.560
completely by accident.

00:35:34.560 --> 00:35:37.560
So this doesn’t seem to be&nbsp;
a reliable neutralization&nbsp;

00:35:37.560 --> 00:35:39.480
method for SCP-682.

00:35:39.480 --> 00:35:44.640
Adding to that, the panel that Dr. Scranton
was transported to the Red Reality with eventually

00:35:44.640 --> 00:35:49.260
came back, which means it might only be a
temporary solution anyway.

00:35:49.260 --> 00:35:55.140
MistakeToSociaty Yay said, “Can someone
ride SCP-682 without them dying?”

00:35:55.140 --> 00:36:00.240
This isn’t technically about neutralizing
SCP-682, but it deserves an answer.

00:36:00.240 --> 00:36:06.720
While it appears that some people are able
to ride 682 such as SCP-053, the Little Girl

00:36:06.720 --> 00:36:12.960
and 05-6 aka The American in the Ouroboros
cycle, he doesn’t seem to enjoy it.

00:36:12.960 --> 00:36:17.940
At least he didn’t when SCP-082, better
known as Fernand the Cannibal attempted it.

00:36:17.940 --> 00:36:23.580
Of course Fernand describes their relationship
quite differently, insisting that 682 is his

00:36:23.580 --> 00:36:26.160
Bayard… his magical steed.

00:36:26.160 --> 00:36:30.780
Laura Garcia said, “Chop it up, put the
pieces in a giant bowl with egg beaters stirring

00:36:30.780 --> 00:36:32.520
it constantly so it can't reanimate.

00:36:32.520 --> 00:36:36.600
Keep it kinetically moving so it doesn't ever
have the rest time to reform.

00:36:36.600 --> 00:36:39.360
Giant Egg Beating Machine to prevent Reformation.

00:36:39.360 --> 00:36:43.800
Killing it would take a Rigel sun blast to
stop it from reanimating itself.”

00:36:43.800 --> 00:36:47.820
This has got to be one of the most creative
ones we’ve encountered.

00:36:47.820 --> 00:36:51.420
Even Dr. Bright probably wouldn’t think
to use giant whisks on the beast.

00:36:51.420 --> 00:36:55.140
However, it probably wouldn’t kill the ornery
creature for good.

00:36:55.140 --> 00:37:00.300
As we’ve said before, not only has the beast
regenerated from things as hot as the sun,

00:37:00.300 --> 00:37:05.760
he’s also able to remanifest from the tiniest
atoms, or even nothing at all.

00:37:05.760 --> 00:37:10.740
On the plus side, he may reanimate with a
new super whisking ability, and could potentially

00:37:10.740 --> 00:37:14.400
give SCP-5031 a run for best cook in containment.

00:37:14.400 --> 00:37:18.960
Shaked ben yakar said, “I think they need
to explode him from the inside because maybe

00:37:18.960 --> 00:37:24.540
there's one spot in his body that isn't invincible
and if they hurt it SCP-682 will die.”

00:37:24.540 --> 00:37:30.420
The problem with SCP-682 isn’t necessarily
that it’s invincible, just hyper-adaptive

00:37:30.420 --> 00:37:31.560
and hyper-regenerative.

00:37:31.560 --> 00:37:38.280
As you may have seen in other videos, SCP-682
has been shot, dismembered, burned, frozen,

00:37:38.280 --> 00:37:42.780
vaporized, blown up, partially eaten, and
even totally disintegrated.

00:37:42.780 --> 00:37:47.940
But it always manages to come back, even from
the smallest specs of matter.

00:37:47.940 --> 00:37:52.920
It would almost admirable… if it wasn’t
a perpetually-aggressive murder monster.

00:37:52.920 --> 00:37:56.400
Brybot said, “Put it in 106's pocket dimension.”

00:37:56.400 --> 00:38:01.860
This actually happened once during a containment
breach where the Old Man as well as SCP-953

00:38:01.860 --> 00:38:05.280
the Polymorphic Humanoid ended up in 682’s
cell.

00:38:05.280 --> 00:38:12.000
SCP-106 dragged them all into its pocket dimension
for a bit of the old ultra-violence, and when

00:38:12.000 --> 00:38:15.600
they emerged, it was clear that they’d all
taken considerable damage.

00:38:15.600 --> 00:38:22.140
SCP-682 wasn’t killed though, and 106 hasn’t
tried anything like that again since.

00:38:22.140 --> 00:38:26.040
NonPlayerCactus said, “Trick him into killing
John Wick's dog.”

00:38:26.040 --> 00:38:31.140
To be fair, if anyone could take this monster
down, it’d probably be John Wick.

00:38:31.140 --> 00:38:35.880
Though SCP-682 might be too smart to actually
kill his dog in the first place.

00:38:35.880 --> 00:38:38.520
And if he did manage to best John Wick?

00:38:38.520 --> 00:38:43.380
Well we hate to think what a 682 with the
martial prowess and gun skills of John Wick

00:38:43.380 --> 00:38:44.040
would be like.

00:38:44.040 --> 00:38:47.880
Actually no, we don’t hate to think about
it, because it would be awesome.

00:38:47.880 --> 00:38:52.320
These are just a little taster plate of the
huge and varied potential murder methods you’ve

00:38:52.320 --> 00:38:57.000
devised for this terrible creature, but there
were just too many good ones, so we’ll have

00:38:57.000 --> 00:38:58.680
to save the rest for another day.

00:38:58.680 --> 00:39:00.420
Ah Skip, here we go again...

00:39:00.420 --> 00:39:06.780
It’s time for us to take another crack at
putting SCP-682 six feet under, once and for

00:39:06.780 --> 00:39:07.020
all.

00:39:07.020 --> 00:39:11.160
If you’ve been following this channel for
any amount of time, then there’s one thing

00:39:11.160 --> 00:39:16.980
you know for certain: SCP-682 is harder to
kill than pretty much, well, anything!

00:39:16.980 --> 00:39:21.780
We’ve made multiple videos on the Foundation’s
failed attempts to finally terminate the beast,

00:39:21.780 --> 00:39:25.980
and we made a video with some of your ideas
on how to finally slay the monster.

00:39:25.980 --> 00:39:30.720
And considering you’re watching this video
right now, you can probably guess how that

00:39:30.720 --> 00:39:31.140
went.

00:39:31.140 --> 00:39:36.120
Now it’s time for one more run at the Death
Star: and once again it’s with your ideas

00:39:36.120 --> 00:39:41.040
from comments and community post responses,
let’s see if any of them can help us finally

00:39:41.040 --> 00:39:43.260
put this ill-tempered reptile to rest.

00:39:43.260 --> 00:39:44.520
If we can’t…

00:39:44.520 --> 00:39:48.960
well we’re not blaming you, but also it’s
your fault.

00:39:48.960 --> 00:39:52.140
Let the community termination attempts commence!

00:39:52.140 --> 00:39:55.320
Anais McBride suggested, “Ask the Witch
Child.”

00:39:55.320 --> 00:40:01.140
SCP-239, also known as The Witch Child, is
one of the most dangerous and powerful anomalies

00:40:01.140 --> 00:40:01.500
out there.

00:40:01.500 --> 00:40:04.680
She’s a small girl with&nbsp;
unparalleled reality-warping&nbsp;

00:40:04.680 --> 00:40:07.080
mental abilities, so powerful that her very

00:40:07.080 --> 00:40:09.600
brainwaves alone can be passively fatal.

00:40:09.600 --> 00:40:12.300
However, the problem is,&nbsp;
her power is so potentially&nbsp;

00:40:12.300 --> 00:40:14.640
dangerous that she’s forever kept in a kind

00:40:14.640 --> 00:40:16.800
of medically-induced anomalous coma.

00:40:16.800 --> 00:40:21.660
Dr. Alto Clef thinks she’s so dangerous
he’s even campaigning to have her terminated.

00:40:21.660 --> 00:40:28.620
As a result, the O5 Council has forbidden
any cross-testing between 682 and 239, fearing

00:40:28.620 --> 00:40:34.860
the consequences of 239 gaining 682’s powers
and becoming a truly unstoppable threat capable

00:40:34.860 --> 00:40:37.860
of causing an XK-Class End of the World Scenario.

00:40:37.860 --> 00:40:43.680
Syed Zamin Ali Shah Kazmi Mushadi suggested,
“Kill him with SCP-734.”

00:40:43.680 --> 00:40:45.960
This is an interesting one.

00:40:45.960 --> 00:40:52.920
SCP-734, also known as The Baby, is an anomaly
that causes a painful degenerative disease

00:40:52.920 --> 00:40:57.780
that eventually disintegrates the entire body
and kills the victim if they so much as come

00:40:57.780 --> 00:41:00.240
into contact with the baby or its fluids.

00:41:00.240 --> 00:41:05.100
However, based on cross-tests with other,
similar “touch it and die” anomalies like

00:41:05.100 --> 00:41:10.860
SCP-409 - the Contagious Crystal - we can
probably guess how exactly this would go down.

00:41:10.860 --> 00:41:15.720
In all likelihood, the Baby’s anomalous
effects would infect and destroy large portions

00:41:15.720 --> 00:41:17.880
of SCP-682’s body.

00:41:17.880 --> 00:41:23.580
However, at this point, 682 would adapt to
the threat, and begin to reverse it and heal.

00:41:23.580 --> 00:41:29.520
Even worse, it’s likely that 682 would steal
the ability for a limited time, and become

00:41:29.520 --> 00:41:30.600
deadly to the touch.

00:41:30.600 --> 00:41:35.460
Caden Griffin suggested, “Why don't you
use the Dragon Slayer to terminate 682?

00:41:35.460 --> 00:41:38.640
It has proved itself many times in fights
with LSAs.”

00:41:38.640 --> 00:41:45.000
SCP-5514, the Dragon Slayer, is essentially
a giant fighting robot designed to take down

00:41:45.000 --> 00:41:47.700
killer kaijus with its&nbsp;
plethora of state-of-the-art&nbsp;

00:41:47.700 --> 00:41:49.740
anomalous weapons and defenses.

00:41:49.740 --> 00:41:54.780
However, we’d still argue that while it
could definitely help in immobilizing 682

00:41:54.780 --> 00:41:58.560
during a rampage, it doesn’t have much of
a chance of actually killing it.

00:41:58.560 --> 00:42:04.440
Let’s look at SCP-001, the Gate Guardian,
a supernatural warrior with a blade hotter

00:42:04.440 --> 00:42:07.380
than the sun, capable of cleaving atoms in
half.

00:42:07.380 --> 00:42:10.740
Even he couldn’t kill SCP-682.

00:42:10.740 --> 00:42:15.540
So a robotic approximation with only a fraction
of the Gate Guardian’s power is probably

00:42:15.540 --> 00:42:18.600
not going to have any real chance of killing
682.

00:42:18.600 --> 00:42:24.000
ImAChuckster48 suggested, “Make it bite
its tongue so hard that it just destroys itself.”

00:42:24.000 --> 00:42:29.220
While we can certainly attest from personal
experience that this really, really hurts,

00:42:29.220 --> 00:42:35.100
we worry that if ever 682 bit its own tongue
really hard, it’d just drive it into a state

00:42:35.100 --> 00:42:36.300
of murderous rage.

00:42:36.300 --> 00:42:40.860
Though we do take a small piece of satisfaction
in knowing its tongue would probably be in

00:42:40.860 --> 00:42:45.420
distress for a few minutes afterwards, it’s
unlikely to wipe out the beast once and for

00:42:45.420 --> 00:42:45.600
all.

00:42:45.600 --> 00:42:51.780
Liezel Rolle suggested, “How about we just
put SCP-682 in 2317's cell.”

00:42:51.780 --> 00:42:58.560
SCP-2317 is an old wooden door that functions
as a portal into the domain of a planet-destroying

00:42:58.560 --> 00:43:03.900
monster known as The Devourer of Worlds, a
being that many believe is associated with

00:43:03.900 --> 00:43:09.180
the Scarlet King, and will inevitably escape
and cause an XK-Class End of the World Scenario.

00:43:09.180 --> 00:43:14.160
While you may be thinking, “Perhaps it’ll
kill 682”, it’s more likely that they’d

00:43:14.160 --> 00:43:17.040
collaborate, seeing as they both want the
same thing.

00:43:17.040 --> 00:43:18.720
Namely, to kill everyone.

00:43:18.720 --> 00:43:23.940
If you let 682 in, chances are, it’ll come
back through that door with the Devourer right

00:43:23.940 --> 00:43:27.120
on its tail - then, it’s all of our problems.

00:43:27.120 --> 00:43:32.220
Guest123 116 suggested, “Drop him in Russia
so they can terminate him.”

00:43:32.220 --> 00:43:35.100
The Foundation has technically already tried
this.

00:43:35.100 --> 00:43:41.400
They dropped 682 into SCP-3930, a patch of
literal non-existence in Russia that causes

00:43:41.400 --> 00:43:44.160
anything that goes inside of it to cease to
exist.

00:43:44.160 --> 00:43:45.300
And afterwards?

00:43:45.300 --> 00:43:46.320
He was fine!

00:43:46.320 --> 00:43:50.520
So yeah, dropping him anywhere in Russia is
probably just going to get a bunch of innocent

00:43:50.520 --> 00:43:51.960
Russian civilians killed.

00:43:51.960 --> 00:43:56.520
Mysher said, “The Foundation shouldn't worry
about how to kill him, but how to stop his

00:43:56.520 --> 00:43:57.480
ability to adapt.

00:43:57.480 --> 00:44:03.900
I would suggest typing "Scp 682 no adaptability
juice" or something like that into SCP-294

00:44:03.900 --> 00:44:08.220
and then kill him by any means, which SHOULD
kill him forever.”

00:44:08.220 --> 00:44:14.460
An interesting theory, but what if he simply
adapts to SCP-682 no adaptability juice?

00:44:14.460 --> 00:44:17.160
Then we’d really be in trouble...

00:44:17.160 --> 00:44:22.140
MarioTGP said, “Give him a twitter account,
he'll be canceled instantly for his spicy

00:44:22.140 --> 00:44:22.560
opinions.”

00:44:22.560 --> 00:44:28.260
SCP-682 would cancel Twitter itself, for not
having opinions that are spicy enough.

00:44:28.260 --> 00:44:29.580
Sorry, Jack.

00:44:29.580 --> 00:44:35.940
SCP-096 - still sore about losing the battle,
we assume - said, “Let him fight the queen

00:44:35.940 --> 00:44:36.300
of England.

00:44:36.300 --> 00:44:38.100
After all, she’s immortal too.”

00:44:38.100 --> 00:44:43.320
We definitely think it would be interesting
to see SCP-682 go head to head with the Queen

00:44:43.320 --> 00:44:43.620
of England.

00:44:43.620 --> 00:44:48.540
Based on all the knighting she does, we know
that she at least has a sword, though we don’t

00:44:48.540 --> 00:44:51.900
know if that sword is as powerful as the one
wielded by the Gate Guardian.

00:44:51.900 --> 00:44:55.800
But regardless of the outcome, the battle
would definitely change history.

00:44:55.800 --> 00:45:01.980
Every history book would simply read: “SCP-682
Punched the Queen”, everything else would

00:45:01.980 --> 00:45:02.820
just be a footnote.

00:45:02.820 --> 00:45:07.500
Noah Cordero said, “Use SCP-2935 to kill
the lizard.

00:45:07.500 --> 00:45:09.660
As you can see in the video, he will die.”

00:45:09.660 --> 00:45:16.800
SCP-2935, also known as O’ Death, is probably
one of the scariest and deadliest SCPs out

00:45:16.800 --> 00:45:16.920
there.

00:45:16.920 --> 00:45:22.380
It killed an entire alternate dimension, including
an alternate SCP-682.

00:45:22.380 --> 00:45:28.740
The problem is, putting our 682 into 2935’s
alternate reality could lead to the destruction

00:45:28.740 --> 00:45:30.960
of our entire dimension.

00:45:30.960 --> 00:45:31.920
Why’s that?

00:45:31.920 --> 00:45:38.340
Because, if 682 was somehow able to return
to our world from the world of 2935, it could

00:45:38.340 --> 00:45:42.540
bring the spirit of death itself back with
it and kill us all in the process.

00:45:42.540 --> 00:45:48.480
Explorando con beto 1 suggested, “SCP 682
vs Lady Dimitrescu.”

00:45:48.480 --> 00:45:54.000
While Resident Evil 8’s Lady Dimitrescu
has certainly captured all of our hearts,

00:45:54.000 --> 00:45:57.360
we don’t think she’ll be bringing home
the W on this one.

00:45:57.360 --> 00:46:02.880
Lady Dimitrescu has a powerful adaptive ability
of her own - with a high resistance to damage,

00:46:02.880 --> 00:46:08.760
impressive regenerative abilities, and a number
of offensive capabilities, from huge claws

00:46:08.760 --> 00:46:10.200
to a powerful dragon form.

00:46:10.200 --> 00:46:14.460
However, considering she wasn’t even able
to defeat Ethan Winters, she probably wouldn’t

00:46:14.460 --> 00:46:17.580
be able to defeat SCP-682, either.

00:46:17.580 --> 00:46:23.820
However, in her dragon form, SCP-682 may finally
join the rest of us in developing a crush.

00:46:23.820 --> 00:46:25.200
Or is that being crushed?

00:46:25.200 --> 00:46:26.700
Anyway, moving on.

00:46:26.700 --> 00:46:32.880
Jonathan Pecany suggested, “Just ask SCP
343 on how to destroy it, or even better,

00:46:32.880 --> 00:46:34.380
ask if he could destroy it.”

00:46:34.380 --> 00:46:39.180
It’s an idea so good that the Foundation
actually tried it, and it went about as well

00:46:39.180 --> 00:46:39.960
as you can expect.

00:46:39.960 --> 00:46:45.840
When the SCP known as God entered the containment
chamber, he couldn’t even see 682 in there,

00:46:45.840 --> 00:46:48.900
as though the creature was somehow totally
invisible to him.

00:46:48.900 --> 00:46:53.880
When God eventually got bored and left, they
told him that he was in there to destroy 682.

00:46:53.880 --> 00:46:56.520
He simply replied, “He's not one of mine.

00:46:56.520 --> 00:46:57.540
Deal with him yourself.”

00:46:57.540 --> 00:46:59.580
Interpret that how you will.

00:46:59.580 --> 00:47:05.280
12 Escobar Blancas Eddy Saul suggested, “They
could send him to Area 37 for The Sisters

00:47:05.280 --> 00:47:06.360
to experiment with.”

00:47:06.360 --> 00:47:13.380
SCP-1765, The Sisters, are a trio of terrifyingly
powerful reality warpers that have taken over

00:47:13.380 --> 00:47:19.260
Area 37, and spend their days tormenting everyone
inside with their twisted experiments.

00:47:19.260 --> 00:47:24.780
Using them to try to terminate 682 leads to
similar problems with using the Witch Child

00:47:24.780 --> 00:47:30.300
or the Devourer of Worlds: If they decide
to team up rather than fighting, or the Sisters

00:47:30.300 --> 00:47:33.840
take over 682, we’d all be effectively doomed.

00:47:33.840 --> 00:47:39.180
Kiroyah suggested, “Would the ants from
SCP-743 tear 682 apart?”

00:47:39.180 --> 00:47:44.940
The Foundation actually tried this, getting
682 to consume chocolate from the SCP-743

00:47:44.940 --> 00:47:48.360
fountain, incurring the wrath of its flesh-eating
ants.

00:47:48.360 --> 00:47:53.580
However, 682 developed an adaptation that
gave it a long, ant-eater-like tongue, that

00:47:53.580 --> 00:47:56.880
it then used to consume the ants faster than
they could consume it.

00:47:56.880 --> 00:48:02.340
And even worse, the chocolate seemed to enhance
its regenerative abilities even more for several

00:48:02.340 --> 00:48:03.300
days afterwards.

00:48:03.300 --> 00:48:07.320
Lol 2222 suggested, “Write the name in the
Death Note.”

00:48:07.320 --> 00:48:08.640
Great idea.

00:48:08.640 --> 00:48:13.740
We’ll put it into practice as soon as you
can tell us SCP-682’s real name.

00:48:13.740 --> 00:48:18.960
It may come as a surprise, but its parents
didn’t actually name it the “Hard to Destroy

00:48:18.960 --> 00:48:19.560
Reptile.”

00:48:19.560 --> 00:48:23.760
Stephen Vierie suggested, “I thought that
maybe we should put him in a giant blender

00:48:23.760 --> 00:48:28.440
and then when he is in small pieces put lava
in the blender so it will incinerate him then

00:48:28.440 --> 00:48:32.220
put nuclear waste into the blender and repeat
that until there is no more left of him.”

00:48:32.220 --> 00:48:37.320
After the cooking whisks last time, we feel
obliged to include at least one attempt to

00:48:37.320 --> 00:48:41.940
kill SCP-682 with oversized kitchen equipment
in every video about him.

00:48:41.940 --> 00:48:46.260
However, this attempt would probably go about
as well as the last one, we’re afraid.

00:48:46.260 --> 00:48:51.720
Extreme physical trauma by conventional means
- like burning and dismemberment - has never

00:48:51.720 --> 00:48:53.100
been successful in the past.

00:48:53.100 --> 00:48:58.020
And the Foundation is extremely hesitant to
use anything radioactive on the beast, in

00:48:58.020 --> 00:49:01.200
case it adapts and adds deadly radiation to
its own arsenal.

00:49:01.200 --> 00:49:05.100
MrMaster IQ suggested, “Just take away his
plot armor.”

00:49:05.100 --> 00:49:11.520
You can pry SCP-682’s plot armor from its
cold, dead claws, and as we’ve already learned,

00:49:11.520 --> 00:49:14.820
making those claws cold and dead seems next
to impossible.

00:49:14.820 --> 00:49:15.720
Moving on.

00:49:15.720 --> 00:49:21.360
JC3 suggested, “HMMM IF ANYBODY CAN'T BEAT
THE UNDYING LIZARD WHY NOT OMNI MAN I MEAN

00:49:21.360 --> 00:49:25.620
HE DID KILLED ALL THE GUARDIANS OF THE GLOBE
OF COURSE HE CAN KILL SCP-682.”

00:49:25.620 --> 00:49:32.400
Omni-Man from the comic and TV series Invincible
is undeniably a formidable opponent, given

00:49:32.400 --> 00:49:36.360
he’s able to destroy superhero teams, cities,
and even planets.

00:49:36.360 --> 00:49:39.120
However, one of the few enemies to give Omni-Man&nbsp;

00:49:39.120 --> 00:49:41.700
a genuine run for his money&nbsp;
is a genetically-enhanced

00:49:41.700 --> 00:49:43.260
Kaiju known as Hail Mary.

00:49:43.260 --> 00:49:48.720
Given that, first, 682 has taken on beings
stronger than Omni-Man - like the Gate Guardian

00:49:48.720 --> 00:49:54.000
- and lived, and second, that Omni-Man has
struggled with monsters before - chances are,

00:49:54.000 --> 00:49:56.460
he probably couldn’t permanently kill this
one, either.

00:49:56.460 --> 00:50:02.460
Heycani Havea suggested, “Kill SCP-053,
then 682 will be sad and die.”

00:50:02.460 --> 00:50:05.100
Wow, now that’s cold-blooded.

00:50:05.100 --> 00:50:09.540
However, even if this did work, it’s important
for you to remember that it’s impossible

00:50:09.540 --> 00:50:14.220
to actually kill SCP-053, also known as The
Child or the Little Girl.

00:50:14.220 --> 00:50:16.980
Part of her anomalous abilities is that anyone&nbsp;

00:50:16.980 --> 00:50:19.680
who attempts to kill her&nbsp;
will themselves immediately

00:50:19.680 --> 00:50:22.980
die during the process - normally due to a
heart attack.

00:50:22.980 --> 00:50:28.320
So this method would result in a pile of dead
Foundation personnel, and no progress.

00:50:28.320 --> 00:50:31.200
Jerry Zhang said, “Mush peanut butter on
it.”

00:50:31.200 --> 00:50:36.060
This would definitely work if SCP-682 has
some kind of severe peanut allergy.

00:50:36.060 --> 00:50:39.120
After all, anaphylactic shock is no laughing
matter.

00:50:39.120 --> 00:50:45.120
However, in the far more likely event that
this will have no effect on SCP-682, you will

00:50:45.120 --> 00:50:48.060
likely just die with your hands covered in
peanut butter.

00:50:48.060 --> 00:50:50.520
Andrew Mills suggested, “My idea?

00:50:50.520 --> 00:50:54.720
Have several Xenomorphs, Predators, and Daleks
(yes that’s a Doctor Who reference) take

00:50:54.720 --> 00:50:55.740
682 on.”

00:50:55.740 --> 00:50:58.860
Once again, in all likelihood, this would
have no effect.

00:50:58.860 --> 00:51:05.400
682 has survived blades and lasers - the primary
weapons of the Predators and Daleks - and

00:51:05.400 --> 00:51:10.260
spends the majority of its life immersed in
powerful acid, so the xenomorph would hold

00:51:10.260 --> 00:51:11.580
no surprises for it.

00:51:11.580 --> 00:51:15.180
Sadly, this three-way teamup would be no match
for 682.

00:51:15.180 --> 00:51:21.540
And even if they did defeat him, whoever wins,
we… well you know how it goes.

00:51:21.540 --> 00:51:24.780
Matteo Huang suggested, “Maybe just destroy
reality.”

00:51:24.780 --> 00:51:26.220
This.

00:51:26.220 --> 00:51:32.760
This might be the thing that finally kills
SCP-682, but considering it’s already survived

00:51:32.760 --> 00:51:37.980
being thrown into pure nothingness in Russia,
it may just result in it being one of the

00:51:37.980 --> 00:51:40.620
only survivors of a full destruction of reality.

00:51:40.620 --> 00:51:42.900
We, on the other hand, would all be killed.

00:51:42.900 --> 00:51:47.220
Though in a sense, we wouldn’t have to deal
with SCP-682 anymore.

00:51:47.220 --> 00:51:49.200
So maybe that’s a type of winning?

00:51:49.200 --> 00:51:54.180
And finally, Blind Honor suggested, “Would
Saitama be a good way to eliminate it?

00:51:54.180 --> 00:51:55.920
He is One Punch Man, after all.”

00:51:55.920 --> 00:52:00.300
Of anyone we’ve covered in this series,
Saitama from One Punch Man would probably

00:52:00.300 --> 00:52:06.540
be the most likely to kill SCP-682, especially
if he was taking the battle seriously.

00:52:06.540 --> 00:52:10.920
After all, he has killed planet-destroying
monsters before with barely any effort.

00:52:10.920 --> 00:52:15.300
The only real question is whether he could
even be bothered to come down to a Foundation

00:52:15.300 --> 00:52:17.280
containment site and fight it.

00:52:17.280 --> 00:52:20.460
Saitama hasn’t been known to be a very motivated
guy.

00:52:20.460 --> 00:52:26.040
But of course, like with anything, there’s
the risk that 682 would survive and gain his

00:52:26.040 --> 00:52:26.400
powers.

00:52:26.400 --> 00:52:28.320
Which would be bad.

00:52:28.320 --> 00:52:28.980
Awesome.

00:52:28.980 --> 00:52:30.000
But bad.

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:33.600
Those blasted Foundation rats had done it
again...

00:52:33.600 --> 00:52:41.820
SCP-682, the Hard to Destroy Reptile, sat
in its tank of highly concentrated acid and

00:52:41.820 --> 00:52:44.460
seethed at the world it had been placed in.

00:52:44.460 --> 00:52:47.820
And what a miserable, terrible world it was.

00:52:47.820 --> 00:52:54.360
He hated it, and he hated every single soul
that occupied it - and especially the hypocritical

00:52:54.360 --> 00:52:58.500
monsters in lab coats that ran this sham of
an organization.

00:52:58.500 --> 00:53:04.260
Whenever the reptile wasn’t speaking - normally
to bark threats and profanities at its human

00:53:04.260 --> 00:53:10.200
jailers - it was quietly listening, taking
everything in, and how the things it heard

00:53:10.200 --> 00:53:15.360
made its blood boil more than the corrosive
fluid forever eating into its carapace.

00:53:15.360 --> 00:53:21.780
What high-minded ideas these worthless apes
had about themselves: “We’re cold, not

00:53:21.780 --> 00:53:22.320
cruel.”

00:53:22.320 --> 00:53:23.310
Ha!

00:53:23.310 --> 00:53:25.140
What a sick joke...

00:53:25.140 --> 00:53:28.800
Every moment for the reptile was a different
kind of hell.

00:53:28.800 --> 00:53:34.800
The baseline of existence was a certain dull,
fizzling pain as he melted as quickly as his

00:53:34.800 --> 00:53:35.760
cells could divide.

00:53:35.760 --> 00:53:40.980
His only reprieve from this was to be dragged
into a testing chamber for some even worse

00:53:40.980 --> 00:53:47.880
pain: Perhaps burned, or sliced, or chewed
at by a mutant rabbit, or crushed by bananas,

00:53:47.880 --> 00:53:53.700
or torn apart by wires and hooks, or beaten
and bashed by some mad swordsman, or having

00:53:53.700 --> 00:53:57.960
his mind invaded and attacked by a rogue soul
in a cursed necklace.

00:53:57.960 --> 00:54:03.720
If this was only “Cold”, then the reptile
hated to even imagine what the SCP Foundation

00:54:03.720 --> 00:54:05.340
considered “Cruel.”

00:54:05.340 --> 00:54:08.820
After all, there were monsters more powerful
than him out there.

00:54:08.820 --> 00:54:14.100
The Hanged King or the Devourer Of Worlds
could handily destroy their wretched ball

00:54:14.100 --> 00:54:16.200
of rock if they so chose to.

00:54:16.200 --> 00:54:21.720
He wasn’t the most sadistic or evil of the
beasts these maniacs in white coats had faced.

00:54:21.720 --> 00:54:25.860
Those who warred with him met a quick death
at his claws and fangs.

00:54:25.860 --> 00:54:29.640
Would that nightmarish Old Man afford his
victims such a luxury?

00:54:29.640 --> 00:54:33.180
Or that unstoppable psychopath in the old
police car?

00:54:33.180 --> 00:54:41.340
And yet, it was his file that bore the addendum:
“SCP-682 must be destroyed as soon as possible.”

00:54:41.340 --> 00:54:42.420
And why?

00:54:42.420 --> 00:54:47.700
Seemingly only because he could take it, and
the Foundation always had new toys it wanted

00:54:47.700 --> 00:54:50.280
to test on their favorite punching bag.

00:54:50.280 --> 00:54:53.460
Of course, he attempted to escape, but wouldn’t
you?

00:54:53.460 --> 00:54:56.280
Is freedom not an inalienable right?

00:54:56.280 --> 00:55:00.480
The Foundation would cry, “But look at the
terrible crimes he’s committed!

00:55:00.480 --> 00:55:02.280
Look at the lives he’s taken!”

00:55:02.280 --> 00:55:03.780
as they always do.

00:55:03.780 --> 00:55:08.280
Let he who is without sin draw the first acid
bath.

00:55:08.280 --> 00:55:13.020
He knew, on some level, if he were to make
a tally, the Foundation’s crimes would far

00:55:13.020 --> 00:55:14.100
outnumber his own.

00:55:14.100 --> 00:55:19.080
The only difference was that they’d deluded
themselves into believing all acts of cruelty

00:55:19.080 --> 00:55:22.500
are permissible in service of their “greater
good.”

00:55:22.500 --> 00:55:27.720
If they all had but one head, the reptile
would claw it from their shoulders.

00:55:27.720 --> 00:55:33.180
A group of incredibly well-armed and well-armored
guards entered the room, training all their

00:55:33.180 --> 00:55:34.020
weapons on him.

00:55:34.020 --> 00:55:39.060
He hadn’t summoned the energy to escape
today, and that meant only one thing: They

00:55:39.060 --> 00:55:41.460
were going to take another swing at killing
him again.

00:55:41.460 --> 00:55:43.080
Oh, goody.

00:55:43.080 --> 00:55:49.080
Another attempt that would leave him momentarily
in absolute agony, and allow neither of them

00:55:49.080 --> 00:55:50.340
to gain any ground.

00:55:50.340 --> 00:55:53.880
He’d grown numb to attempts on his life
by now.

00:55:53.880 --> 00:55:58.080
Whatever they had waiting for him in the other
room, he’d be ready for it.

00:55:58.080 --> 00:56:02.340
The guards removed him from his acid bath,
and, while he was still trying to regenerate

00:56:02.340 --> 00:56:06.660
his muscles and nerves enough to move, they
dragged him into the testing chamber.

00:56:06.660 --> 00:56:11.820
It was always a mystery, wondering what they’d
be poking or prodding him with today.

00:56:11.820 --> 00:56:15.540
But when he was first dragged into the chamber,
it was...

00:56:15.540 --> 00:56:16.440
Empty.

00:56:16.440 --> 00:56:18.720
Those were always the worst ones.

00:56:18.720 --> 00:56:23.640
When he was left some sitting duck, waiting
for the Foundation, in their infinite malice,

00:56:23.640 --> 00:56:26.400
to choose the form of the would-be destroyer.

00:56:26.400 --> 00:56:29.280
What would be behind Door Number One...

00:56:29.280 --> 00:56:30.420
A box.

00:56:30.420 --> 00:56:36.600
A large, wooden box was pushed into the room,
and the door closed behind it.

00:56:36.600 --> 00:56:37.680
How curious.

00:56:37.680 --> 00:56:42.300
The Hard to Destroy Reptile began to approach
the box, sniffing at the air.

00:56:42.300 --> 00:56:46.800
It made no sound in there, but something about
that smell.

00:56:46.800 --> 00:56:47.460
Something...

00:56:48.000 --> 00:56:49.680
eerily familiar...

00:56:49.680 --> 00:56:51.540
It was different this time.

00:56:51.540 --> 00:56:57.060
With a soft pop, the box fell apart, its walls
falling in different directions like the petals

00:56:57.060 --> 00:56:58.140
of a blooming flower.

00:56:58.140 --> 00:57:03.060
And the second the Hard to Destroy Reptile
saw what lurked inside, it felt an unfamiliar

00:57:03.060 --> 00:57:07.440
cold barb of terror hook into the soft, warm
flesh of its heart.

00:57:07.440 --> 00:57:14.040
The thing inside the box had been called SCP-173
by the SCP Foundation, but that wasn’t how

00:57:14.040 --> 00:57:15.060
the reptile knew it.

00:57:15.060 --> 00:57:17.640
It was a primordial nightmare.

00:57:17.640 --> 00:57:19.800
An ancient horror.

00:57:19.800 --> 00:57:21.180
The stone devil.

00:57:21.180 --> 00:57:22.500
The killer in the dark.

00:57:22.500 --> 00:57:27.960
The Koitern, which had mercilessly and gleefully
slaughtered so much of the reptile’s very

00:57:27.960 --> 00:57:32.400
species, back when 682 was&nbsp;
known as the Atanti-ql-Paneu.

00:57:32.400 --> 00:57:33.900
And here it was...

00:57:33.900 --> 00:57:36.240
Ready to finish the job.

00:57:36.240 --> 00:57:42.660
SCP-682 let out an involuntary screech of
pure horror and fled backwards, keeping its

00:57:42.660 --> 00:57:44.460
eyes fixed on the monster at all times.

00:57:44.460 --> 00:57:48.360
He moved back until he hit the far wall of
the containment chamber.

00:57:48.360 --> 00:57:50.460
Until he could go no further.

00:57:50.460 --> 00:57:53.400
His mind was flooded and his heart was racing.

00:57:53.400 --> 00:57:55.920
He never thought he’d see this monster again.

00:57:55.920 --> 00:57:58.620
He’d hoped it would never cross his path
again.

00:57:58.620 --> 00:58:04.020
Perhaps he’d even held out hope that the
abomination had been slain, destroyed, scattered

00:58:04.020 --> 00:58:04.800
to the winds.

00:58:04.800 --> 00:58:07.680
And yet, here it was, looking at him.

00:58:07.680 --> 00:58:09.163
The reptile called out, “You fools.

00:58:09.163 --> 00:58:13.080
You have no idea what you’ve done.

00:58:13.080 --> 00:58:14.040
This...

00:58:14.040 --> 00:58:19.200
Thing, mark my words, it will be your ruin!

00:58:19.200 --> 00:58:23.100
It will slaughter every single one of you!”

00:58:24.000 --> 00:58:30.540
But its appeals to reason with its captors,
in their own interest, for once, fell on utterly

00:58:30.540 --> 00:58:32.340
uninterested ears.

00:58:32.340 --> 00:58:37.500
Six hours of this passed, the reptile spending
every second of it, for the first time in

00:58:37.500 --> 00:58:39.540
a long time, fearing for his life.

00:58:39.540 --> 00:58:45.120
A group of observing Foundation scientists
merely noted a peculiar reaction of distress

00:58:45.120 --> 00:58:51.180
from 682 and ordered a decorated Mobile Task
Force sharpshooter with a Barrett 50 Caliber

00:58:51.180 --> 00:58:54.660
Sniper Rifle
with armor-piercing rounds to initiate Phase

00:58:54.660 --> 00:58:56.160
2 of the cross test.

00:58:56.160 --> 00:58:58.980
In a sudden flash of sound&nbsp;
and pain, the sharpshooter&nbsp;

00:58:58.980 --> 00:59:02.100
blew away both of SCP-682’s staring eyes.

00:59:02.100 --> 00:59:06.720
The simultaneous instruction went out for
all observing members of personnel to avert

00:59:06.720 --> 00:59:08.760
their gaze, just for a moment.

00:59:08.760 --> 00:59:14.820
682 could certainly regenerate its eyes quickly,
but nothing was quite as fast as an unobserved

00:59:14.820 --> 00:59:16.620
SCP-173.

00:59:16.620 --> 00:59:22.080
The reptile screeched in pain as it heard
the monster snapping its body parts, leaving

00:59:22.080 --> 00:59:23.580
it thoroughly mutilated.

00:59:23.580 --> 00:59:29.370
When the group of observing scientists looked
back, they saw it - which is to say, SCP-173

00:59:29.370 --> 00:59:36.600
- standing before a heavily damaged SCP-682,
as though incredibly proud of its handiwork.

00:59:36.600 --> 00:59:41.880
Internally, 682 thanked a creator it despised
for the fact that the observers looked back

00:59:41.880 --> 00:59:46.500
and spared it from the onslaught that soulless
stone monster had unleashed on it.

00:59:46.500 --> 00:59:50.820
A scientist working for the Foundation would
later remark, “After review, it appears

00:59:50.820 --> 00:59:57.000
SCP-173 was unable to do lethal damage to
SCP-682 due to a major difference in physical

00:59:57.000 --> 00:59:57.540
size.

00:59:57.540 --> 01:00:03.240
A possible repeat of this test may be made
if SCP-682 is damaged enough to reduce its

01:00:03.240 --> 01:00:06.360
physical mass to a level equal with SCP-173.”

01:00:06.360 --> 01:00:10.080
But 682 knew, deep down, this wasn’t the
truth.

01:00:10.080 --> 01:00:15.420
It had nothing to do with physical size: If
the Koitern had truly willed it, he never

01:00:15.420 --> 01:00:16.560
would have left that room.

01:00:16.560 --> 01:00:19.680
The monster only wanted to extend the torment.

01:00:19.680 --> 01:00:23.940
And this time, SCP-682 wouldn’t let him.

01:00:23.940 --> 01:00:27.720
He regenerated, adapted, and came back ready.

01:00:27.720 --> 01:00:34.920
682 developed a number of eyes, far more than
before, that remained fixed on SCP-173, paralyzing

01:00:34.920 --> 01:00:35.100
it.

01:00:35.100 --> 01:00:38.040
It crawled back up onto the wall and simply
stared.

01:00:38.040 --> 01:00:42.300
Once again, the observing scientists ordered
the sharpshooter to take aim and open fire.

01:00:42.300 --> 01:00:44.220
But this time, the bullets had no effect.

01:00:44.220 --> 01:00:51.240
SCP-682 has developed a thick, clear carapace
over the surface of its new eyes, ensuring

01:00:51.240 --> 01:00:55.320
that nothing would break its eye contact with
that murderous little monster.

01:00:55.320 --> 01:00:58.740
This time, it would not lose.

01:00:58.740 --> 01:01:04.020
But for all the time that 682 stared, 173
said nothing, as always.

01:01:04.020 --> 01:01:10.140
It just stood there, the strange pattern of
its face, that nasty, bloody Rorschach splotch,

01:01:10.140 --> 01:01:12.180
looked almost like a mocking smile.

01:01:12.180 --> 01:01:13.680
It conceded nothing.

01:01:13.680 --> 01:01:16.020
It seemed to say, “Go on.

01:01:16.020 --> 01:01:17.100
Get an eyeful.

01:01:17.100 --> 01:01:24.180
I have all the time in the universe, and everyone
looks away eventually, even you, Atanti-ql-Paneu.

01:01:24.180 --> 01:01:27.600
Let the eternal silence of your brethren be
a lesson to you.

01:01:27.600 --> 01:01:30.360
All you will hear is Crunch.”

01:01:30.360 --> 01:01:36.060
682 kept up the staring contest for twelve
hours, before it was taken back to its acid

01:01:36.060 --> 01:01:38.520
bath, thoroughly shaken by its experience.

01:01:38.520 --> 01:01:44.220
It had always despised its terrible captors,
but now, a new shade of darkness had entered

01:01:44.220 --> 01:01:47.220
its narrow emotional lexicon: Fear.

01:01:47.220 --> 01:01:49.020
True fear.

01:01:49.020 --> 01:01:53.760
An acknowledgment, deep down in its muscle
tissue and guts, that there was something

01:01:53.760 --> 01:01:55.680
out there that could truly hurt it.

01:01:55.680 --> 01:02:00.000
The terrible Koitern was alive and thirsty
for blood.

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:04.980
The researchers who’d conducted this test
considered it an interesting partial success.

01:02:04.980 --> 01:02:10.380
While 682 was quaking in its tank thinking
about 173, they were brainstorming the best

01:02:10.380 --> 01:02:15.900
move to take next, regarding potential pairings
between 682 and 173.

01:02:15.900 --> 01:02:22.560
A plucky researcher noted that 096 had also
gotten SCP-682 on the ropes, so maybe they

01:02:22.560 --> 01:02:27.420
should send in SCP-173 with a photo of SCP-096
taped to its chest.

01:02:27.420 --> 01:02:31.740
A member of the O5 Council intervened before
this got too far, saying, “No.

01:02:31.740 --> 01:02:32.580
Absolutely not.

01:02:32.580 --> 01:02:39.120
Setting aside the problem of SCP-682, an SCP-173
that cannot be observed for fear of triggering

01:02:39.120 --> 01:02:45.120
a response from SCP-096 is a self-perpetuating
catastrophe that the Foundation does not,

01:02:45.120 --> 01:02:49.200
under any reasonable circumstances, have the
slightest desire to unleash.

01:02:49.200 --> 01:02:50.880
Denied with vehemence.”

01:02:50.880 --> 01:02:55.860
The researcher who’d suggested this idea
felt supremely embarrassed, and retired briefly

01:02:55.860 --> 01:03:00.360
to one of the employee bathrooms to have a
good cry before returning to the brainstorming

01:03:00.360 --> 01:03:00.660
session.

01:03:00.660 --> 01:03:06.000
Researcher Maytus, a more experienced member
of personnel, had a stroke of genius.

01:03:06.000 --> 01:03:10.620
He reminded the assembled researchers that
they’d recently performed another semi-successful

01:03:10.620 --> 01:03:16.080
experiment on SCP-682: Using their deadly,
high-precision blades, they were able to slice

01:03:16.080 --> 01:03:19.320
and dice 682 into a series of amorphous blobs.

01:03:19.320 --> 01:03:24.060
Sure, these blobs may have attacked and killed
some D-Classes before reforming into the OG

01:03:24.060 --> 01:03:30.900
Nasty Reptile, but each of these blobs were
the perfect size to be murdered by SCP-173.

01:03:30.900 --> 01:03:36.360
It eliminated the size differential and put
these two on an even playing field, and on

01:03:36.360 --> 01:03:41.940
that even playing field, it stood to reason
that SCP-173 might win.

01:03:41.940 --> 01:03:47.760
The cross-test was greenlit and a researcher
named Dr. Shenron was put in charge of overseeing

01:03:47.760 --> 01:03:48.480
the operations.

01:03:48.480 --> 01:03:53.880
And this time, due to Foundation incompetence
and a greater degree of mental preparedness

01:03:53.880 --> 01:03:58.380
by SCP-682, they were in for a complete disaster.

01:03:58.380 --> 01:04:02.580
682 and 173 were brought into the same containment
chamber.

01:04:02.580 --> 01:04:07.740
682 could feel the latent fear welling up
inside itself, so it did the thing that it

01:04:07.740 --> 01:04:11.040
knew the best: It tried to stoke up its rage.

01:04:11.040 --> 01:04:12.240
Its hatred.

01:04:12.240 --> 01:04:17.100
The fury and spite that had kept it going
through so many torturous attempts on its

01:04:17.100 --> 01:04:17.220
life.

01:04:17.220 --> 01:04:20.340
It would not die at the hands of this stone
monster.

01:04:20.340 --> 01:04:27.180
And if that was its destiny, then it would
ensure, with its dying wretched breaths, it

01:04:27.180 --> 01:04:29.520
would destroy this terrible beast once and
for all.

01:04:29.520 --> 01:04:34.020
It would shatter it and ensure it never put
itself back together.

01:04:34.020 --> 01:04:36.900
Suddenly, the high-precision blades were deployed.

01:04:36.900 --> 01:04:42.120
It was an endless volley of cutting that dashed
the two deadly anomalies to pieces like a

01:04:42.120 --> 01:04:44.220
giant As Seen On TV Slap-Chop.

01:04:44.220 --> 01:04:50.040
Because the machine had been calibrated for
its body, 682 was sliced into 12,000 perfect

01:04:50.040 --> 01:04:55.080
cubes, and 173 had been cut into a pile of
lumpy, irregular chunks.

01:04:55.080 --> 01:05:00.180
A vacuum system was then activated to separate
both anomalies into different chambers, so

01:05:00.180 --> 01:05:08.040
173 could reform and begin the assault, but
miraculously for 682, the vacuum system failed.

01:05:08.040 --> 01:05:13.500
Two D-Classes were sent in to recalibrate
the system, but things quickly got even worse.

01:05:13.500 --> 01:05:19.080
Many of the 682 cubes formed the same gelatinous
masses that they did in the previous High

01:05:19.080 --> 01:05:23.400
Precision Blades Test, and began attacking
and killing one of the D-Classes.

01:05:23.400 --> 01:05:28.200
The other, naturally, turned to look at this
horrifying display - Which meant nobody was

01:05:28.200 --> 01:05:30.780
paying attention to SCP-173.

01:05:30.780 --> 01:05:35.580
Immediately, the Sculpture reformed and snapped
the surviving D-Class’ neck before turning

01:05:35.580 --> 01:05:37.680
its attention to SCP-682.

01:05:37.680 --> 01:05:42.600
The emergency incineration system failed,
so all the Foundation could hope for was Mutually

01:05:42.600 --> 01:05:46.200
Assured Destruction until they got the situation
back under control.

01:05:46.200 --> 01:05:51.600
However, the Foundation had underestimated
682’s intelligence and tactical reasoning.

01:05:51.600 --> 01:05:56.940
While the gelatinous, mutated globs of its
flesh attacked 173, smashing and cracking

01:05:56.940 --> 01:06:02.040
its concrete body as it killed and splattered
them, the remainder of 682’s flesh formed

01:06:02.040 --> 01:06:05.820
a smaller version of itself, which began staring
at 173.

01:06:05.820 --> 01:06:11.700
This froze the sculpture in place while the
mutated flesh monster smashed into it, slowly

01:06:11.700 --> 01:06:12.660
breaking it down.

01:06:12.660 --> 01:06:18.210
For the first time in as long as it could
remember, 682 felt genuine glee.

01:06:18.210 --> 01:06:19.860
The thrill of revenge.

01:06:19.860 --> 01:06:22.680
The glory of an ancient foe vanquished.

01:06:22.680 --> 01:06:28.320
It would now slay the terrible Koitern, as
its ancestors had tried to do so many times

01:06:28.320 --> 01:06:29.820
before, and failed.

01:06:29.820 --> 01:06:32.940
But this reptile would not fail.

01:06:32.940 --> 01:06:38.100
Until, of course, the SCP Foundation - monsters
that they were - decided to put their finger

01:06:38.100 --> 01:06:38.700
on the scale.

01:06:38.700 --> 01:06:44.580
The same Foundation Mobile Task Force sharpshooter
who’d been there during the first 173 cross-test

01:06:44.580 --> 01:06:47.760
was still there, still ready to carry out
his duties.

01:06:47.760 --> 01:06:52.440
On the order of the researchers, he fired
another two shots, blowing out the eyes of

01:06:52.440 --> 01:06:54.900
this new, smaller 682.

01:06:54.900 --> 01:07:00.960
While it regenerated its precious eyes, 173
went on a rampage, mercilessly slaughtering

01:07:00.960 --> 01:07:03.780
every single one of the eyeless blobs of mutated
flesh.

01:07:03.780 --> 01:07:09.900
It smashed each one beyond repair, until only
it and the smaller 682 remained.

01:07:09.900 --> 01:07:16.320
Luckily for 682, its eyes regenerated, complete
with the familiar bulletproof covering, just

01:07:16.320 --> 01:07:18.780
in time to hold back 173 from killing it.

01:07:18.780 --> 01:07:24.180
The two remained locked in a staring contest
of pure hatred for a solid seventeen hours

01:07:24.180 --> 01:07:26.400
before the test was eventually called off.

01:07:26.400 --> 01:07:28.860
But the horrors continued!

01:07:28.860 --> 01:07:34.980
Exhausted by the ordeal already, SCP-682 was
sedated and returned to its containment chamber

01:07:34.980 --> 01:07:38.280
without incident, where it regenerated back
to its default state.

01:07:38.280 --> 01:07:41.520
Things weren’t so easy with SCP-173.

01:07:41.520 --> 01:07:44.100
While a team transported&nbsp;
it back to its containment&nbsp;

01:07:44.100 --> 01:07:46.320
chamber, there was a power outage in the hall,

01:07:46.320 --> 01:07:47.880
and things went dark.

01:07:47.880 --> 01:07:54.360
And considering SCP-173, in addition to The
Sculpture and The Peanut, could also be nicknamed,

01:07:54.360 --> 01:07:56.640
“Instant Killing Spree, Just Add Darkness!”

01:07:56.640 --> 01:07:59.400
it won’t surprise you to hear there were
no survivors.

01:07:59.400 --> 01:08:05.400
173 killed everyone in the hall, then escaped
out into the wider facility, causing a site-wide

01:08:05.400 --> 01:08:08.340
containment breach and a&nbsp;
huge number of casualties.

01:08:08.340 --> 01:08:13.320
The cause of the electrical short that kickstarted
this massacre was traced back to Dr. Shenron’s

01:08:13.320 --> 01:08:14.940
tampering with the incinerator system.

01:08:14.940 --> 01:08:20.280
This got the doctor formally reprimanded,
stripped of his titles and his memories, and

01:08:20.280 --> 01:08:21.360
relieved of his duty.

01:08:21.360 --> 01:08:25.080
But the worst was still very much to come
for everyone involved.

01:08:25.080 --> 01:08:28.200
Including SCP-682.

01:08:28.200 --> 01:08:34.200
Because the true terrifying potential of SCP-173
was soon going to be unleashed, and when that

01:08:34.200 --> 01:08:36.600
happened, nowhere would be safe.

01:08:36.600 --> 01:08:42.120
On what was otherwise a very normal day, in
a very normal procedure when a few D-Classes

01:08:42.120 --> 01:08:49.740
were sent into SCP-173’s cell, something
extraordinary and terrible happened: SCP-173

01:08:49.740 --> 01:08:51.000
multiplied.

01:08:51.000 --> 01:08:58.740
Like a single-cell organism undergoing mitosis,
173 somehow just split into two equal copies

01:08:58.740 --> 01:08:59.280
of itself.

01:08:59.280 --> 01:09:01.980
Two D-Classes were killed&nbsp;
in this first duplication&nbsp;

01:09:01.980 --> 01:09:03.660
event, but they were just the beginning.

01:09:03.660 --> 01:09:08.100
Soon enough, people would look back so fondly
on the days when there were only a mere two

01:09:08.100 --> 01:09:08.760
of these things.

01:09:08.760 --> 01:09:12.300
The Foundation and 682, for&nbsp;
all their disagreements,&nbsp;

01:09:12.300 --> 01:09:13.560
are very much alike.

01:09:13.560 --> 01:09:18.600
Both are always vying for control over their
situations, and both achieve this through

01:09:18.600 --> 01:09:21.420
understanding and adapting to whatever is
threatening them.

01:09:21.420 --> 01:09:27.540
As SCP-173 continued to multiply, the Foundation
did what they could to adapt and regain control.

01:09:27.540 --> 01:09:31.680
They tried to contain specific instances in
smaller containment units.

01:09:31.680 --> 01:09:34.560
They tried to create new methods for permanent
observation.

01:09:34.560 --> 01:09:36.660
They even tried shipping them off to the moon.

01:09:36.660 --> 01:09:38.460
But none of it did any good.

01:09:38.460 --> 01:09:41.580
SCP-173 continued to duplicate.

01:09:41.580 --> 01:09:44.160
They escaped, began spreading further.

01:09:44.160 --> 01:09:49.620
They killed half a million civilians in 48
hours, and believe us when we tell you they

01:09:49.620 --> 01:09:50.820
were just getting started.

01:09:50.820 --> 01:09:56.100
The ever-growing army of 173 instances went
on massive killing sprees every night, taking

01:09:56.100 --> 01:10:00.360
out huge swathes of the civilian population
as they scrambled and panicked in the dark.

01:10:00.360 --> 01:10:02.640
And they weren’t just going after civilians.

01:10:02.640 --> 01:10:09.900
Evidently, much like 682, 173 had a grudge
against the SCP Foundation for all those decades

01:10:09.900 --> 01:10:10.620
of imprisonment.

01:10:10.620 --> 01:10:16.200
The 173 army began locating, surrounding,
and destroying entire Foundation containment

01:10:16.200 --> 01:10:19.800
sites, and killing off all the staff and the
anomalies inside.

01:10:19.800 --> 01:10:25.500
Of all the entities in containment that might
one day go XK and destroy the world as we

01:10:25.500 --> 01:10:28.740
knew it, not many people had 173 on their
bingo card.

01:10:28.740 --> 01:10:34.080
If only they’d listened to 682’s warnings
and reallocated their termination resources

01:10:34.080 --> 01:10:37.200
to 173, things may have turned out differently.

01:10:37.200 --> 01:10:42.720
And speaking of our scaly old foe, 682 sat
in an empty chamber.

01:10:42.720 --> 01:10:47.640
It’d been days since anyone had come in
to check on it - All fled or dead from snapped

01:10:47.640 --> 01:10:49.020
necks, one of the two.

01:10:49.020 --> 01:10:53.340
He thought about escaping containment, but
given the bloodbaths going on outside, all

01:10:53.340 --> 01:10:55.260
the time, what would even be the point?

01:10:55.260 --> 01:11:00.120
All that was really left was time, and that
was a rapidly depleting resource.

01:11:00.120 --> 01:11:01.680
He just needed to wait for that...

01:11:01.680 --> 01:11:04.080
Thing to come and see him again.

01:11:04.080 --> 01:11:10.080
SCP-682 blinked,
and there it was, standing before him, looking.

01:11:10.080 --> 01:11:10.980
Blink.

01:11:10.980 --> 01:11:12.000
And there was more.

01:11:12.000 --> 01:11:12.780
Blink.

01:11:12.780 --> 01:11:14.100
So many of them.

01:11:14.100 --> 01:11:15.960
So, so, so many.

01:11:15.960 --> 01:11:16.860
Blink.

01:11:16.860 --> 01:11:20.040
Surrounded on all sides by that terrible creature.

01:11:20.040 --> 01:11:21.240
Too many to fight.

01:11:21.240 --> 01:11:22.560
Too many to win.

01:11:22.560 --> 01:11:26.400
Just waiting, watching, mocking him.

01:11:26.400 --> 01:11:29.280
There was only one thing left to do.

01:11:29.280 --> 01:11:30.420
Blink.

01:11:30.420 --> 01:11:31.560
Hello, everyone!

01:11:31.560 --> 01:11:37.080
If you’re a fan of SCP Explained, you’ll
know that we regularly post interesting questions

01:11:37.080 --> 01:11:42.360
in our community tab, asking for responses
from you - our dear fans.

01:11:42.360 --> 01:11:48.360
These have ranged from questions about specific
anomalies, like SCP-096, or your suggestions

01:11:48.360 --> 01:11:53.580
on how we should actually kill SCP-682, the
Hard to Destroy Reptile.

01:11:53.580 --> 01:11:58.020
We’ve even asked you which anomalous powers
you’d want to have, and posed your questions

01:11:58.020 --> 01:12:05.520
directly to SCP-343, also known as God, and
of course, the terrifying and infamous Scarlet

01:12:05.520 --> 01:12:05.880
King.

01:12:05.880 --> 01:12:10.800
But in our latest community question, asking
you about hypothetical crossovers between

01:12:10.800 --> 01:12:16.560
the SCP Foundation and the weird, wild multiverse
of all fiction, you truly outdid yourself,

01:12:16.560 --> 01:12:19.440
with thousands upon thousands of responses.

01:12:19.440 --> 01:12:24.120
And we thought, rather than just making one
video selecting our favorites, we’d turn

01:12:24.120 --> 01:12:26.880
each of our favorites into whole videos.

01:12:26.880 --> 01:12:28.740
And how are we going to do that?

01:12:28.740 --> 01:12:32.460
That’s when this wonderful state-of-the-art
gizmo comes into play!

01:12:32.460 --> 01:12:38.400
You may remember the Anom-O-Tron 6000, our
incredibly advanced artificial intelligence-driven

01:12:38.400 --> 01:12:43.020
supercomputer designed specifically to run
simulations for the SCP Foundation.

01:12:43.020 --> 01:12:48.360
We’ve fed this computer data from countless
SCP Foundation experiments and cross tests,

01:12:48.360 --> 01:12:50.580
and all the data from your suggestions.

01:12:50.580 --> 01:12:55.920
This will allow the fine folks at the SCP
Foundation to explore any anomalous hypothetical,

01:12:55.920 --> 01:12:59.340
without risking the lives of staff members
or civilians.

01:12:59.340 --> 01:13:06.720
This brings us to our first simulation, suggested
in a huge number of comments: Could SCP-682

01:13:06.720 --> 01:13:09.060
be Contained Within the Backrooms?

01:13:09.060 --> 01:13:13.620
For those not in the know, the Backrooms is
an internet urban legend that’s spiraled

01:13:13.620 --> 01:13:15.300
into a full-blown phenomenon.

01:13:15.300 --> 01:13:17.220
It’s built on the premise that if you’re&nbsp;

01:13:17.220 --> 01:13:20.400
not careful and enter certain&nbsp;
specific circumstances,

01:13:20.400 --> 01:13:26.940
you can no clip out of our reality, and enter
a terrifying, multi-level alternate reality,

01:13:26.940 --> 01:13:30.600
where you’re stalked by a variety of bizarre
and frightening creatures.

01:13:30.600 --> 01:13:35.100
This could be a complete nightmare for your
average person, but how would it play out

01:13:35.100 --> 01:13:41.460
if SCP-682, the endlessly angry Hard to Destroy
Reptile, found its way inside?

01:13:41.460 --> 01:13:46.560
Also, for another Backrooms-related surprise,
stick around until the end of the video…

01:13:46.560 --> 01:13:51.360
In the meantime, though, let’s boot up the
Anom-O-Tron and test this new scenario!

01:13:51.360 --> 01:13:53.760
The worst had happened: Again.

01:13:53.760 --> 01:13:59.760
SCP-682 had busted out of containment during
a cross test and started making a beeline

01:13:59.760 --> 01:14:01.260
for the nearest populated area.

01:14:01.260 --> 01:14:06.060
Several helicopters containing heavily-armed
MTF Nu-7, “Hammer Down”, members were

01:14:06.060 --> 01:14:11.160
in hot pursuit, attempting to slow the vicious
reptile down with targeted sniper fire at

01:14:11.160 --> 01:14:11.820
its legs.

01:14:11.820 --> 01:14:17.580
But it seemed that these efforts were all
for naught: SCP-682 had already reached the

01:14:17.580 --> 01:14:22.440
defunct industrial district on the edge of
a nearby city, and if the beast managed to

01:14:22.440 --> 01:14:26.580
actually reach a populated area, all hell
would break loose.

01:14:26.580 --> 01:14:31.620
That’s when they pulled out the heavy weaponry:
Miniguns mounted to the helicopters unleashed

01:14:31.620 --> 01:14:34.740
a rain of hellfire down onto SCP-682.

01:14:34.740 --> 01:14:39.900
However, 682 managed to dodge most of the
bullets and simply tank the rest.

01:14:39.900 --> 01:14:44.220
Command authorized the use of heavy ordinance:
The helicopter’s missile launches.

01:14:44.220 --> 01:14:49.500
They’d pick up the pieces afterwards, once
SCP-682 was back in containment.

01:14:49.500 --> 01:14:52.200
However, the reptile had plans of its own.

01:14:52.200 --> 01:14:57.360
It charged into a nearby abandoned chemical
plant to avoid the gunfire from above.

01:14:57.360 --> 01:15:00.060
This was exactly what Hammer Down wanted.

01:15:00.060 --> 01:15:04.560
The helicopters circled around the chemical
plant and unleashed a barrage of powerful

01:15:04.560 --> 01:15:10.260
incendiary missiles, blowing the plant to
kingdom come in hopes of dragging an incapacitated

01:15:10.260 --> 01:15:12.660
682 out of the rubble afterwards.

01:15:12.660 --> 01:15:18.660
But when the smoke had cleared and only the
rubble was left, 682 was nowhere to be seen.

01:15:18.660 --> 01:15:23.640
Even for the hardcore operatives of Hammer
Down, this caused an anxiety spike.

01:15:23.640 --> 01:15:25.320
Had it tunneled into the ground?

01:15:25.320 --> 01:15:29.520
Had it adapted to the attack by turning invisible
or getting tiny to escape?

01:15:29.520 --> 01:15:31.680
It’d done all these things before.

01:15:31.680 --> 01:15:38.040
Or after all the deranged attempts at putting
SCP-682 in the ground, had some light firebombing

01:15:38.040 --> 01:15:38.880
killed the monster?

01:15:38.880 --> 01:15:45.240
Whatever the case, they’d need to search,
in case SCP-682 popped up somewhere else and

01:15:45.240 --> 01:15:46.440
started causing havoc.

01:15:46.440 --> 01:15:51.420
If it was still alive - which it probably
was - they couldn’t rest on their laurels

01:15:51.420 --> 01:15:52.740
until they’d found it again.

01:15:52.740 --> 01:15:55.800
Meanwhile, SCP-682 woke up.

01:15:55.800 --> 01:16:01.500
It felt groggy and irritated, its body resting
against an unpleasant, soggy carpet.

01:16:01.500 --> 01:16:06.660
It licked the carpet - the moisture had the
distinct flavor of human spinal fluid, which

01:16:06.660 --> 01:16:09.000
682 had tasted many times before.

01:16:09.000 --> 01:16:13.860
The sickly yellow walls and incessant buzzing
from the fluorescent lights up above were

01:16:13.860 --> 01:16:17.340
nauseating, and it gave 682 a nagging headache.

01:16:17.340 --> 01:16:22.980
This only made 682’s default emotion - blistering
rage and hatred - even worse.

01:16:22.980 --> 01:16:27.060
It began walking around, exploring this strange,
spatially anomalous environment.

01:16:27.060 --> 01:16:30.180
Was this more of that frustrating Foundation
trickery?

01:16:30.180 --> 01:16:33.060
Another one of those puerile “cross-tests”?

01:16:33.060 --> 01:16:37.620
The last thing 682 remembered was running
at one of the walls in the chemical plant

01:16:37.620 --> 01:16:42.780
- a wall that, in hindsight, seemed darker
than the others - but rather than shattering

01:16:42.780 --> 01:16:47.940
through the brickwork, it was here now, in
this strange, tacky lobby that never seemed

01:16:47.940 --> 01:16:48.300
to end.

01:16:48.300 --> 01:16:52.440
It was like a kaleidoscope of empty, 1990s
office kitsch.

01:16:52.440 --> 01:16:58.080
Endless worthless yellow walls arranged like
some labyrinthine, nonsensical maze, leading

01:16:58.080 --> 01:17:02.760
nowhere and devoid of all life as SCP-682
wandered through it.

01:17:02.760 --> 01:17:07.200
And of course, SCP-682 found it disgusting.

01:17:07.200 --> 01:17:13.320
It was only on Level 0, and already, 682 hated
the Backrooms just as much as it hated our

01:17:13.320 --> 01:17:13.860
dimension.

01:17:13.860 --> 01:17:20.340
Someone or something had to pay for the crime
of inconveniencing it this way, and it would

01:17:20.340 --> 01:17:25.440
happily turn this whole dimension inside out
just to find some beings to kill inside it.

01:17:25.440 --> 01:17:28.440
Yes, that would be great fun…

01:17:28.440 --> 01:17:34.800
SCP-682 began its frantic search for an exit,
evolving an innate sonar ability and picking

01:17:34.800 --> 01:17:37.500
up speeds that would be impossible for human
beings.

01:17:37.500 --> 01:17:41.700
This is the part where most people would go
mad, or die from hunger or thirst.

01:17:41.700 --> 01:17:43.500
SCP-682?

01:17:43.500 --> 01:17:44.640
Not so much.

01:17:44.640 --> 01:17:50.040
It could keep searching, and searching, and
searching until the stars burned out in the

01:17:50.040 --> 01:17:50.220
sky.

01:17:50.220 --> 01:17:56.280
It would find its prey, somehow, and when
it did, it would put them through hell.

01:17:56.280 --> 01:18:02.100
And as it turned out, this new universe rewarded
682’s dogged stubbornness, because when

01:18:02.100 --> 01:18:06.360
it passed through a seemingly random hallway
after hours of searching, it was in a different

01:18:06.360 --> 01:18:07.380
place entirely.

01:18:07.380 --> 01:18:12.300
This place looked like some huge abandoned
warehouse complex with water shining off the

01:18:12.300 --> 01:18:12.420
ground.

01:18:12.420 --> 01:18:17.400
If 682 had more advanced knowledge of the
Backrooms, it would have known this was Level

01:18:17.400 --> 01:18:17.760
1.

01:18:17.760 --> 01:18:23.760
But the only number SCP-682 cared about was
body count, and in that regard, it would find

01:18:23.760 --> 01:18:26.460
Level 1 to be a vast improvement.

01:18:26.460 --> 01:18:30.900
Two groups of humans had established bases
in this level of the Backrooms: The Major

01:18:30.900 --> 01:18:35.160
Explorer Group, a faction of professional
Backrooms traversers who maintained their

01:18:35.160 --> 01:18:39.900
Base Alpha on this level, and the Backrooms
Nonaligned Trade Group, a commercial group

01:18:39.900 --> 01:18:45.600
whose primary base is an economic hub on this
very level - A fortified city-like area with

01:18:45.600 --> 01:18:51.900
a population of 412, which would, a few hours
after 682’s appearance, be a population

01:18:51.900 --> 01:18:52.800
of zero.

01:18:52.800 --> 01:18:56.940
But before all that, it felt like grabbing
a bite at the diner…

01:18:56.940 --> 01:19:01.620
Tom’s Diner is a refuge for many people
trapped in the backrooms - a casual eatery

01:19:01.620 --> 01:19:06.360
nestled into the cold warehouse environment
of Level 1, where people could get a warm

01:19:06.360 --> 01:19:10.380
meal from Tom, a former cook who’s been
trapped in the Backroom for years.

01:19:10.380 --> 01:19:16.200
SCP-682 was eager to be a part of this grand
tradition - But the Hard to Destroy Reptile

01:19:16.200 --> 01:19:19.860
decided to buck the trend a little by just
devouring Tom himself.

01:19:19.860 --> 01:19:25.260
From there, it decided to launch its rage-fueled
offensive against the various humanoid inhabitants

01:19:25.260 --> 01:19:25.920
of the level.

01:19:25.920 --> 01:19:30.900
Both the Major Explorers Group Base Alpha
and the Backrooms Nonaligned Trade Group Trade

01:19:30.900 --> 01:19:35.580
Keep were heavily fortified against the kind
of entities these folks had gotten used to

01:19:35.580 --> 01:19:41.460
facing in The Backrooms, but they were completely
unprepared for a creature of SCP-682’s sheer

01:19:41.460 --> 01:19:44.280
power, intelligence, endurance, and ferocity.

01:19:44.280 --> 01:19:49.680
The SCP Foundation had been studying the creature
for decades, with far more resources than

01:19:49.680 --> 01:19:54.180
either of these two Backrooms-bound groups,
and they still had a hard time keeping the

01:19:54.180 --> 01:19:55.980
beast consistently contained.

01:19:55.980 --> 01:20:01.680
Sadly for the greatest bastions of human hope
in the Backrooms, SCP-682 swept through both

01:20:01.680 --> 01:20:06.360
outposts in a matter of hours, killing everyone
there without an ounce of remorse.

01:20:06.360 --> 01:20:11.220
The only person there it took its time with
was the final human being left in the decimated

01:20:11.220 --> 01:20:14.220
remains of the Major Explorers Group Base
Alpha.

01:20:14.220 --> 01:20:19.140
It grabbed the man by the throat and squeezed,
asking with its guttural, growing voice:

01:20:19.140 --> 01:20:19.275
“You.

01:20:19.275 --> 01:20:20.528
Were you and your dead brethren allied with
the SCP Foundation?”

01:20:20.528 --> 01:20:31.679
Despite his fear, the Explorer told 682 that
he had never heard of the SCP Foundation.

01:20:31.680 --> 01:20:35.340
Nor did he know what kind of entity 682 was.

01:20:35.340 --> 01:20:36.390
“Hmm.

01:20:36.390 --> 01:20:38.880
Then what is this place?

01:20:38.880 --> 01:20:42.360
Tell me, and I might give you a quick death.”

01:20:42.360 --> 01:20:48.420
The Explorer gave as good a response as he
could: 682 was trapped in the Backrooms, a

01:20:48.420 --> 01:20:51.720
multi-level interdimensional nightmare filled
with dangerous creatures.

01:20:51.720 --> 01:20:55.500
That made 682 curious - Dangerous creatures?

01:20:55.500 --> 01:20:57.480
That could make an interesting challenge.

01:20:57.480 --> 01:21:02.820
682 asked the Explorer how it could access
these other levels, and find these creatures,

01:21:02.820 --> 01:21:08.100
and the Explorer explained that through exploring
these levels enough, anyone could “no clip”

01:21:08.100 --> 01:21:09.060
into the next one.

01:21:09.060 --> 01:21:10.680
It really was that simple.

01:21:10.680 --> 01:21:16.080
With that, 682 knew all it needed to know
and carelessly murdered the final human being

01:21:16.080 --> 01:21:16.920
of Level 1.

01:21:16.920 --> 01:21:21.900
It had killed so many humans over its long
and twisted life - It was no different from

01:21:21.900 --> 01:21:24.960
breathing air now, an utterly perfunctory
action.

01:21:24.960 --> 01:21:30.000
It was eager to discover these other creatures
on the lower levels, and teach them a new

01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:32.520
level of fear they’d never experienced…

01:21:32.520 --> 01:21:37.740
682 stormed through the halls until it achieved
the next successful no clip into Level 2,

01:21:37.740 --> 01:21:42.600
which manifested as a series of old, dilapidated
maintenance tunnels that seemed to stretch

01:21:42.600 --> 01:21:43.800
on for millions of miles.

01:21:43.800 --> 01:21:44.880
Wonderful.

01:21:44.880 --> 01:21:48.720
There were humans here, too, apparently, but
who cared about them?

01:21:48.720 --> 01:21:54.000
This was the first level to feature a smorgasbord
of “Entities”, ripe for the killing.

01:21:54.000 --> 01:22:00.240
It sped through the tunnels, teeth, and fangs
borne, eager to deal death with gleeful abandon.

01:22:00.240 --> 01:22:05.340
The first entities it encountered in the expansive
tunnels of Level 2 were a collection of beings

01:22:05.340 --> 01:22:10.620
known as Crawlers: Insect-like creatures infected
with an extremely aggressive fungal growth.

01:22:10.620 --> 01:22:15.600
Just getting close to them could present an
active risk to humans - Not so much for a

01:22:15.600 --> 01:22:18.840
creature that could easily regenerate after
being tossed into the sun.

01:22:18.840 --> 01:22:24.300
As the creatures tried to lunge, SCP-682 simply
crushed and devoured them with little effort.

01:22:24.300 --> 01:22:28.980
They tasted a little stale, on account of
the fungus, but the chewiness was pleasing.

01:22:28.980 --> 01:22:33.420
Hopefully, there would be more challenging
foes down in the tunnel than these mere insects,

01:22:33.420 --> 01:22:39.000
SCP-682 thought to itself while journeying
deeper into the endless network of tunnels.

01:22:39.000 --> 01:22:44.400
Soon enough, SCP-682 ventured into a section
of the tunnel engulfed in total darkness.

01:22:44.400 --> 01:22:48.360
Its eyes quickly adjusted, developing immaculate
night vision.

01:22:48.360 --> 01:22:52.740
That’s when it spotted another creature
sharing this little slice of darkness with

01:22:52.740 --> 01:22:58.800
it: A pair of floating, glowing eyes and almost
cartoonish teeth, grinning like some maniacal

01:22:58.800 --> 01:22:59.340
Looney Tune.

01:22:59.340 --> 01:23:04.980
This is an entity known as a Smiler, and they’re
a terrifying threat to any humans venturing

01:23:04.980 --> 01:23:06.000
through the Backrooms.

01:23:06.000 --> 01:23:07.740
SCP-682…

01:23:07.740 --> 01:23:09.300
Wasn’t impressed.

01:23:09.300 --> 01:23:14.580
It began a perfect adaptation for the situation:
Its body began to glow, emitting incredible

01:23:14.580 --> 01:23:19.020
levels of both heat and light, carving through
the darkness of the tunnel and causing the

01:23:19.020 --> 01:23:21.600
Smiler to emit a terrible, piercing shriek.

01:23:21.600 --> 01:23:27.300
The sheer heat of this new ability melted
sections of the Level 2 tunnels around SCP-682.

01:23:27.300 --> 01:23:32.400
When the light finally dimmed down to slightly
more reasonable levels, where the Smiler once

01:23:32.400 --> 01:23:35.340
stood was instead a fizzling black scorch
mark.

01:23:35.340 --> 01:23:41.460
Another creature had painfully bitten the
dust, and SCP-682 was starting to have some

01:23:41.460 --> 01:23:41.700
fun.

01:23:41.700 --> 01:23:46.800
It took off further down into the tunnels,
looking forward to finding its next victim.

01:23:46.800 --> 01:23:52.140
Sadly for SCP-682, it wouldn’t get to kill
the next set of victims.

01:23:52.140 --> 01:23:57.540
A group of four Child Facelings - spooky,
faceless little girls who like to cut apart

01:23:57.540 --> 01:24:02.580
their typically human victims with small objects
- were waiting a little further down the pipe.

01:24:02.580 --> 01:24:08.040
However, when they felt SCP-682 approaching,
they almost sensed the power and cruelty of

01:24:08.040 --> 01:24:09.300
the beast coming towards them.

01:24:09.300 --> 01:24:15.180
Even being little monsters themselves, game
recognized game, and they knew that they needed

01:24:15.180 --> 01:24:17.700
to get the hell out of there before the monster
arrived.

01:24:17.700 --> 01:24:21.840
They climbed between the pipes on the tunnel
walls and skittered off into hiding places

01:24:21.840 --> 01:24:22.800
deep in the dark.

01:24:22.800 --> 01:24:27.000
Lucky for them, SCP-682 passed them and just
kept going.

01:24:27.000 --> 01:24:31.980
What would be the point in wasting time on
these little morsels when there were apparently

01:24:31.980 --> 01:24:34.740
so many other creatures to massacre down here?

01:24:34.740 --> 01:24:40.440
Next, SCP-682 came across a truly pathetic
creature - Something that the mighty reptile

01:24:40.440 --> 01:24:42.060
honestly felt a little embarrassed even&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:42.060 --> 01:24:42.900
interacting
with.

01:24:42.900 --> 01:24:47.460
It was a creature known as a “Clump”,
a strange bundle of living limbs that will

01:24:47.460 --> 01:24:51.180
move at great speeds and attack its usually
human targets.

01:24:51.180 --> 01:24:56.940
It tried to do the same to SCP-682, manically
flailing its many twisted limbs.

01:24:56.940 --> 01:25:02.160
682 killed it in a single stomp and moved
on, feeling its own psychological equivalent

01:25:02.160 --> 01:25:04.380
of pity - but not that much of it.

01:25:04.380 --> 01:25:10.380
Not long after mercy-killing the Clump, SCP-682
came face to face with a series of Hounds

01:25:10.380 --> 01:25:15.360
- mutant humanoids who travel on all fours,
behaving in a wolf-like fashion.

01:25:15.360 --> 01:25:20.160
This would, of course, be the stuff of nightmares
for your average human being, but would be

01:25:20.160 --> 01:25:24.720
far more likely to put a being like the Hard
to Destroy Reptile to sleep with sheer boredom.

01:25:24.720 --> 01:25:27.000
Humans acting like dogs?

01:25:27.000 --> 01:25:32.520
That makes them even more worthless, the creature
thought, as it charged forwards and began

01:25:32.520 --> 01:25:34.560
tearing the group of Hounds to shreds.

01:25:34.560 --> 01:25:39.720
Minutes later, it was splitting off into an
adjoining tunnel, searching for more easy

01:25:39.720 --> 01:25:40.560
entertainment.

01:25:40.560 --> 01:25:46.200
But the deeper SCP-682 made its way into the
bowels of Level 2, the more it approached

01:25:46.200 --> 01:25:52.140
a truly horrifying realization: The creatures
it was slaughtering here were even more boring

01:25:52.140 --> 01:25:57.480
than the ones the SCP Foundation ceaseless
threw at it back on its native reality - or

01:25:57.480 --> 01:25:59.700
at least, the reality where they’d contained
it.

01:25:59.700 --> 01:26:04.980
Back in that world, it had faced giant, flaming
demi-gods with swords hotter than the sun.

01:26:04.980 --> 01:26:09.480
It had faced some pale, shrieking monstrosity
that didn’t seem to die no matter what the

01:26:09.480 --> 01:26:10.440
reptile threw at it.

01:26:10.440 --> 01:26:15.420
There was the dark, gooey old man, the Immortal
Warrior from the Black Coffin, and even the

01:26:15.420 --> 01:26:17.160
all-devouring bunny rabbit.

01:26:17.160 --> 01:26:22.980
Here, it was killing the same wretched selection
of beasts again and again, a truly pitiful

01:26:22.980 --> 01:26:23.580
offering.

01:26:23.580 --> 01:26:27.240
Was this really the best this world had to
offer?

01:26:27.240 --> 01:26:31.620
Incidentally, the next creatures it found
were literally known as the Wretches by the

01:26:31.620 --> 01:26:33.480
human inhabitants of The Backrooms.

01:26:33.480 --> 01:26:39.240
They were fleshy, zombie-like creatures that
682 figured the Sarkicists back home might

01:26:39.240 --> 01:26:39.660
enjoy.

01:26:40.980 --> 01:26:44.460
It couldn’t believe it was thinking fondly
of that old place while it carved the monsters

01:26:44.460 --> 01:26:45.960
to ribbons with its claws.

01:26:45.960 --> 01:26:52.020
It missed its old enemies, like Dr. Bright,
Dr. Clef, and even that irritating yellow

01:26:52.020 --> 01:26:53.280
blob of snot.

01:26:53.280 --> 01:26:57.240
The more it tried to take its mind off the
old world by killing its way through this

01:26:57.240 --> 01:27:01.740
ant farm of endless tunnels, the more it found
itself waxing nostalgic.

01:27:01.740 --> 01:27:06.480
For example, there were the Plague Goblins,
impish little creatures with masks like that

01:27:06.480 --> 01:27:07.380
of a Plague Doctor.

01:27:07.380 --> 01:27:14.280
682 found itself thinking almost fondly about
SCP-049, while it listlessly ate the tiny,

01:27:14.280 --> 01:27:18.900
mischievous creatures like a depressed person
binging an extra-large pack of chips.

01:27:18.900 --> 01:27:23.760
Even their tiny squeaks as they crunched between
the reptile’s terrible teeth gave it no

01:27:23.760 --> 01:27:24.180
joy.

01:27:24.180 --> 01:27:27.360
What a bleak turn of events this had all turned
out to be.

01:27:27.360 --> 01:27:32.040
As it wandered through the infinite tunnels,
killing creatures and even humans as it found

01:27:32.040 --> 01:27:39.120
them, SCP-682 made a quiet promise to itself:
Somehow, someway, it would make its way back

01:27:39.120 --> 01:27:41.460
to the universe it’d so recently departed.

01:27:41.460 --> 01:27:47.520
It would leave the Backrooms, no matter how
many levels, a quiet, burning husk, and return

01:27:47.520 --> 01:27:51.780
to the world of fools and fiends it had taken
for granted all this time.

01:27:51.780 --> 01:27:56.580
A visit to the Backrooms had taught the Hard
to Destroy Reptile an all-too-human lesson:

01:27:56.580 --> 01:27:59.520
Sometimes, you don’t know what you have
until it’s gone.

01:27:59.520 --> 01:28:04.260
Sure, the SCP Foundation may have tried to
kill it in a new, bizarre, and increasingly

01:28:04.260 --> 01:28:09.060
sadistic way every single day, but that variety
was the spice of life.

01:28:09.060 --> 01:28:14.820
It would return home someday, it knew that
much - But of course, a lot of creatures and

01:28:14.820 --> 01:28:16.800
people would need to die before then.

01:28:16.800 --> 01:28:19.860
But if that’s what it took, well, so be
it.

01:28:19.860 --> 01:28:24.600
SCP-682 licked its dagger-like fangs, and
kept crawling…

01:28:24.600 --> 01:28:28.200
Another day, another failed attempt at death.

01:28:28.200 --> 01:28:34.740
If SCP-682 had anything even resembling a
sense of humor, he might ask for it to be

01:28:34.740 --> 01:28:40.260
printed on a motivational poster and stuck
to the side of his containment chamber, where

01:28:40.260 --> 01:28:45.480
he eternally melts and regrows at the mercy
of high-concentration acid.

01:28:45.480 --> 01:28:47.880
They’d just cross-tested him with Able.

01:28:47.880 --> 01:28:48.780
Again.

01:28:48.780 --> 01:28:54.660
Unlike some of the others he’d been forced
to face, that tattooed swordsman seemingly

01:28:54.660 --> 01:28:57.000
wasn’t intelligent enough to fear.

01:28:57.000 --> 01:29:00.960
He’d always come back, just as stupid and
violent.

01:29:00.960 --> 01:29:05.100
This encounter had left the Hard to Destroy
Reptile at thirty percent of his previous

01:29:05.100 --> 01:29:07.800
body mass, bloody and bashed.

01:29:07.800 --> 01:29:09.900
He’d survived the encounter.

01:29:09.900 --> 01:29:11.580
He always survived.

01:29:11.580 --> 01:29:14.760
They brought what was left of him back to
his cell in a forklift.

01:29:14.760 --> 01:29:17.160
A blasted forklift!

01:29:17.160 --> 01:29:19.380
How could it even be more humiliating?

01:29:19.380 --> 01:29:25.140
As his eyes started to grow back in his head,
he could swear he even saw one of the technicians

01:29:25.140 --> 01:29:25.980
laughing at him.

01:29:25.980 --> 01:29:29.100
His name tag read, “Agent Nigel Kelly.”

01:29:29.100 --> 01:29:34.740
Noted. 682 would specifically hunt down and
kill him the next time he breached.

01:29:34.740 --> 01:29:40.500
Of course, every single day, he plotted revenge
against the human race - along with everything

01:29:40.500 --> 01:29:40.860
else.

01:29:40.860 --> 01:29:46.860
But the sum they owed in pain, blood, and
despair could never be repaid in full.

01:29:46.860 --> 01:29:52.950
After all, every single one of them
- except Dr. Bright -

01:29:52.950 --> 01:29:55.140
could only really die once.

01:29:55.140 --> 01:30:01.320
They’d brought 682 to the precipice a thousand
times, only for his own body to cheat him,

01:30:01.320 --> 01:30:04.800
and deprive him of the sweet release of death.

01:30:04.800 --> 01:30:10.980
And if the Foundation had their way, it would
be done a thousand times more, and they wouldn’t

01:30:10.980 --> 01:30:12.540
even stop there.

01:30:12.540 --> 01:30:16.980
682 couldn’t even imagine the number of
containment breaches it would take to deal

01:30:16.980 --> 01:30:20.220
a blow even comparable to the one he had faced.

01:30:20.220 --> 01:30:22.380
All he could do was dream.

01:30:22.380 --> 01:30:25.440
Dream of a reckoning that would turn the tables.

01:30:25.440 --> 01:30:30.780
Something that would plunge humanity into
the state of constant pain and terror that

01:30:30.780 --> 01:30:35.880
had been all he’d ever known since these
fumbling sadists in white coats had locked

01:30:35.880 --> 01:30:36.420
him up here.

01:30:36.420 --> 01:30:38.940
What a beautiful day that would be...

01:30:38.940 --> 01:30:45.120
Little did SCP-682 know, that very day was
about to break.

01:30:45.120 --> 01:30:51.780
Miles and miles away from the facility where
SCP-682 was kept - after all, orders from

01:30:51.780 --> 01:30:57.240
the O5 Council have hard mandates on the minimum
distances between people and a site holding

01:30:57.240 --> 01:31:03.300
a monster as volatile as 682 - parents watched
their children laughing and frolicking in

01:31:03.300 --> 01:31:04.380
an idyllic playground.

01:31:04.380 --> 01:31:07.920
Some squealed with glee as they descended
the slide.

01:31:07.920 --> 01:31:12.000
Some of the more ambitious little tykes tried
to go over the bar on the swings.

01:31:12.000 --> 01:31:16.680
Others waited in line for some delicious soft
serve at a parked Ice Cream truck.

01:31:16.680 --> 01:31:22.680
One mother bought an ice cream cone and walked
over to a nearby bench, where she began to

01:31:22.680 --> 01:31:24.660
enjoy her delicious frozen treat.

01:31:24.660 --> 01:31:30.600
It was a remarkably hot day out and a little
ice cream was the perfect addition to her

01:31:30.600 --> 01:31:33.480
relaxation while her kids were occupied.

01:31:33.480 --> 01:31:36.300
You could see the distant air wobbling in
the heat.

01:31:36.300 --> 01:31:41.280
Already, her ice cream was starting to melt,
white rivulets dribbling down the sides of

01:31:41.280 --> 01:31:43.320
the cone and onto her hands.

01:31:43.320 --> 01:31:48.240
Suddenly, almost imperceptibly, the quality
of the light shifted.

01:31:48.240 --> 01:31:52.800
The kind of thing you’d dismiss as a trick
of the eyes and forget just as quickly, were

01:31:52.800 --> 01:31:57.240
it not for the catastrophic effects that were
about to unfold.

01:31:57.240 --> 01:32:01.920
As the woman leaned forward to lick her melting
ice cream, something dripped onto her skirt.

01:32:01.920 --> 01:32:07.140
But, as she looked down, she slowly realized
that what dripped onto her wasn’t the pure

01:32:07.140 --> 01:32:11.760
white of her ice cream: It was the exact same
tone as her skin.

01:32:11.760 --> 01:32:16.260
She felt a terrible burning sensation all
through her body.

01:32:16.260 --> 01:32:22.920
The most horrible, debilitating pain she’d
ever experienced, like every cell in her body

01:32:22.920 --> 01:32:26.460
was screaming and trying to make a break for
it.

01:32:26.460 --> 01:32:29.220
She turned to the other parents sitting near
the playground.

01:32:29.220 --> 01:32:31.140
They were screaming too.

01:32:31.140 --> 01:32:36.960
Each collapsed to the ground with agonizing
slowness, different parts of their body falling

01:32:36.960 --> 01:32:40.260
at different speeds as they transitioned through
states of matter.

01:32:40.260 --> 01:32:44.820
When they hit the ground, they were taking
on a liquid state.

01:32:44.820 --> 01:32:48.660
Screaming, worthless, boneless blobs.

01:32:48.660 --> 01:32:54.060
The woman even saw her own arm wilting like
a time lapse video of a dying flower.

01:32:54.060 --> 01:33:00.480
She dripped and sluiced through the cracks
in the bench, until nothing recognizably human

01:33:00.480 --> 01:33:01.260
was left.

01:33:01.260 --> 01:33:06.120
Only a soggy ice cream cone sitting uneaten.

01:33:06.120 --> 01:33:10.740
In an instant, billions of screams rang out
over planet earth.

01:33:10.740 --> 01:33:12.780
Day had broken.

01:33:12.780 --> 01:33:19.680
Things would never, ever be the same again,
as almost half of humanity instantaneously

01:33:19.680 --> 01:33:21.960
took on a liquid state.

01:33:21.960 --> 01:33:26.820
Needless to say, with the most dangerous and
far-reaching anomalous incident in human history

01:33:26.820 --> 01:33:33.180
suddenly breaking out without any kind of
warning, the SCP Foundation was incredibly

01:33:33.180 --> 01:33:33.720
busy.

01:33:33.720 --> 01:33:36.540
This would take some unprecedented action.

01:33:36.540 --> 01:33:41.400
The members of the O5 Council who weren’t
melted during the initial blast convened over

01:33:41.400 --> 01:33:44.700
secure video link while sequestering themselves
underground.

01:33:44.700 --> 01:33:49.440
In what amounted to multiple human lifetimes
of some of the most high-pressure choices

01:33:49.440 --> 01:33:55.860
imaginable, they made the most difficult decision
since the very beginning of the SCP Foundation.

01:33:55.860 --> 01:34:00.900
In the service of all mankind, they would
now break the masquerade.

01:34:00.900 --> 01:34:07.800
The SCP Foundation would, at long last, step
out of the shadows to save the rest of humanity

01:34:07.800 --> 01:34:09.660
from the tyranny of the light.

01:34:09.660 --> 01:34:12.480
Broadcasts went out all over the globe.

01:34:12.480 --> 01:34:17.640
Every TV screen, every livestream, every radio
broadcast was commandeered.

01:34:17.640 --> 01:34:21.060
They gave instructions based on the scattered
intel they had.

01:34:21.060 --> 01:34:24.000
For some reason, the sun had turned against
them.

01:34:24.000 --> 01:34:29.760
Exposure would lead to any biological creatures
melting away into sentient piles of flesh-colored

01:34:29.760 --> 01:34:30.300
sludge.

01:34:30.300 --> 01:34:33.600
People would remain indoors and away from
any light sources.

01:34:33.600 --> 01:34:35.880
All windows must remain covered.

01:34:35.880 --> 01:34:40.680
Travel only at night, and even then, heavily
covered with protective gear.

01:34:40.680 --> 01:34:46.500
There can only be one objective for whoever
is left: Make your way to the nearest SCP

01:34:46.500 --> 01:34:49.860
Foundation containment facility and seek refuge
inside.

01:34:49.860 --> 01:34:55.440
If anyone could figure out the answer to this
terrifying existential riddle, it would be

01:34:55.440 --> 01:34:57.180
the SCP Foundation.

01:34:57.180 --> 01:35:00.300
Anyone who was exposed should be considered
lost.

01:35:00.300 --> 01:35:05.700
While, as always, the SCP Foundation did all
they could to project a sense of control over

01:35:05.700 --> 01:35:09.120
the situation, on the inside, it was pandemonium.

01:35:09.120 --> 01:35:13.620
Somehow, despite everything, this event had
taken all of them by surprise.

01:35:13.620 --> 01:35:19.200
How could anyone have predicted that the cradle
of our solar system’s delicate living balance

01:35:19.200 --> 01:35:21.960
would suddenly become a meat grinder?

01:35:21.960 --> 01:35:26.160
A huge number of Foundation operatives were
wiped out in the initial exposure.

01:35:26.160 --> 01:35:29.340
Global communication infrastructure had been
devastated.

01:35:29.340 --> 01:35:31.560
It was pure chaos.

01:35:31.560 --> 01:35:38.220
And to SCP-682, as another evil tactician
once put it, chaos was a ladder.

01:35:38.220 --> 01:35:44.460
From the inside of his acid tank, 682 could
sense the fear and pain suddenly exuding from

01:35:44.460 --> 01:35:45.720
his surrounding environment.

01:35:45.720 --> 01:35:47.520
It was greater than ever before.

01:35:47.520 --> 01:35:49.380
What was happening out there?

01:35:49.380 --> 01:35:52.560
This was no average containment breach.

01:35:52.560 --> 01:35:55.860
Something was really, really happening out
there.

01:35:55.860 --> 01:36:01.500
682 began to adapt and finely attune its hearing,
until it could pick up chatter from outside.

01:36:01.500 --> 01:36:05.820
“Maybe we can convert some of the D-Class
barracks into serviceable bunkers for the

01:36:05.820 --> 01:36:06.240
refugees?

01:36:06.240 --> 01:36:08.700
It’s not like we’re prepared for this
kind of capacity!”

01:36:08.700 --> 01:36:13.080
“Oh god, oh god, we’ve lost Site 7, Site
10, Site 23, Site 40, Site 52...”

01:36:13.080 --> 01:36:15.120
“Death toll looks to be in the billions.

01:36:15.120 --> 01:36:17.040
Well, we don’t know if they’re dead, technically.

01:36:17.040 --> 01:36:19.140
But they’re sure as hell not human anymore...”

01:36:19.920 --> 01:36:20.760
“This is the Big One.

01:36:20.760 --> 01:36:21.720
This is it.

01:36:21.720 --> 01:36:22.620
XK-Class.

01:36:22.620 --> 01:36:25.020
Even 2000 is unaccounted for.

01:36:25.020 --> 01:36:27.840
Is O5 crazy that they think we fight the freaking
sun!?”

01:36:27.840 --> 01:36:32.280
Needless to say, 682’s curiosity was piqued.

01:36:32.280 --> 01:36:36.480
Anything that could light a fire under the
Foundation like this was something he could

01:36:36.480 --> 01:36:36.900
enjoy.

01:36:36.900 --> 01:36:42.180
And, with his impressively strategic intellect,
he intuited that a time of great strife for

01:36:42.180 --> 01:36:45.840
the Foundation would be the perfect time to
breach containment.

01:36:45.840 --> 01:36:52.560
Cause whenever there’s violence, fear, and
chaos on a mass scale, SCP-682 will be there,

01:36:52.560 --> 01:36:53.580
causing it.

01:36:53.580 --> 01:36:59.160
682 began adapting his pores and endocrine
system to begin releasing a powerful alkaline

01:36:59.160 --> 01:36:59.700
substance.

01:36:59.700 --> 01:37:04.920
Little by little, the alkaline neutralized
the acid surrounding him, turning it into

01:37:04.920 --> 01:37:06.660
little more than plain water.

01:37:06.660 --> 01:37:12.240
He then converted his internal systems to
have extreme endothermic rather than exothermic

01:37:12.240 --> 01:37:18.060
properties, causing his surrounding temperature
to drop rapidly, until all the water in the

01:37:18.060 --> 01:37:20.580
tank completely froze around him.

01:37:20.580 --> 01:37:23.400
The ice expanded beyond the&nbsp;
limit of the containment&nbsp;

01:37:23.400 --> 01:37:25.860
unit, busting the rivets of the metal frame

01:37:25.860 --> 01:37:27.660
and shattering the reinforced glass.

01:37:27.660 --> 01:37:34.140
With this goal achieved, 682 raised his internal
temperatures to incredible highs, melting

01:37:34.140 --> 01:37:35.340
the ice around him.

01:37:35.340 --> 01:37:41.820
Once again, he was free, and ready for some
good, old-fashioned carnage and mayhem.

01:37:41.820 --> 01:37:45.480
Perhaps he could get a better handle on this
strange new situation, too.

01:37:45.480 --> 01:37:48.060
It was all rather exciting.

01:37:48.060 --> 01:37:50.520
Just a girl with goals huh?

01:37:50.520 --> 01:37:55.560
SCP Foundation personnel were already running
around like ants trying desperately to avoid

01:37:55.560 --> 01:37:58.500
the caustic laser beam of the magnifying glass.

01:37:58.500 --> 01:38:03.960
You can only imagine how much worse it made
matters when 682 suddenly burst through the

01:38:03.960 --> 01:38:08.940
wall, Kool-Aid man style, and began to ruthlessly
massacre everyone around him.

01:38:08.940 --> 01:38:10.980
Just one of those days, you know?

01:38:10.980 --> 01:38:16.200
The typical order during a 682 containment
breach is to dispatch all available units

01:38:16.200 --> 01:38:17.580
to get him back under control.

01:38:17.580 --> 01:38:22.080
The issue with this particular containment
breach was that, given the human population

01:38:22.080 --> 01:38:27.120
was very rapidly being melted and they were
the only ones who could potentially save the

01:38:27.120 --> 01:38:33.120
rest, they didn’t really have any available
units to pursue and recontain 682.

01:38:33.120 --> 01:38:39.120
For once, he really wasn’t a priority, and
that meant terrible things for whoever he

01:38:39.120 --> 01:38:39.840
ran into.

01:38:39.840 --> 01:38:45.360
682 slaughtered his way through any researchers
or guards who dared to get in his way.

01:38:45.360 --> 01:38:47.400
Disgusting creatures, really.

01:38:47.400 --> 01:38:48.720
Better off dead.

01:38:48.720 --> 01:38:54.540
He clawed and bit and tore and crushed with
almost childlike glee, leaving great piles

01:38:54.540 --> 01:38:55.740
of bodies in his wake.

01:38:55.740 --> 01:39:00.840
All the while, he was pondering the things
he heard those Foundation drones saying.

01:39:00.840 --> 01:39:04.500
Something about the sun and an XK-Class scenario.

01:39:04.500 --> 01:39:10.920
Interesting. 682 also observed that any apertures
that could potentially allow light into the

01:39:10.920 --> 01:39:12.840
facility had also been shuttered.

01:39:12.840 --> 01:39:16.920
Perhaps they weren’t overreacting this time,
like they always did with him.

01:39:16.920 --> 01:39:22.260
Maybe they were dealing with some kind of
phenomenon that would now cast this wretched

01:39:22.260 --> 01:39:25.080
world and those who lived in it into the void.

01:39:25.080 --> 01:39:28.320
Wouldn’t that be a fitting karmic fate for
them all.

01:39:28.320 --> 01:39:31.800
Still, 682’s bloodlust didn’t outweigh
his logic.

01:39:31.800 --> 01:39:34.860
He needed to know more about this situation
before proceeding.

01:39:34.860 --> 01:39:40.380
And in this, maybe he could kill two Foundation
birds with one stone...

01:39:40.380 --> 01:39:45.300
Elsewhere in the building, alarms blared,
the air was suffused with panicked voices

01:39:45.300 --> 01:39:46.800
and frequent screams.

01:39:46.800 --> 01:39:50.100
Nobody knew what was going on, not really.

01:39:50.100 --> 01:39:55.620
They’d only gotten details here and there,
and the details they’d received were terrifying.

01:39:55.620 --> 01:39:58.320
All their families and loved ones outside...

01:39:58.320 --> 01:39:59.640
Probably gone.

01:39:59.640 --> 01:40:04.980
So many of the people and so much of the world
they’d been fighting for, risking it all

01:40:04.980 --> 01:40:07.920
for, had disappeared in an instant.

01:40:07.920 --> 01:40:10.680
Carried to hell on a ray of sunshine.

01:40:10.680 --> 01:40:12.780
Why were they still here?

01:40:12.780 --> 01:40:15.660
Was this horror not truly uncontainable?

01:40:15.660 --> 01:40:20.220
These questions were swimming through the
mind of Agent Nigel Kelly as he stood alone

01:40:20.220 --> 01:40:22.680
in his office, almost catatonic.

01:40:22.680 --> 01:40:27.840
He’d had friends and family on the outside,
all likely reduced to those horrible fleshy

01:40:27.840 --> 01:40:28.380
blobs.

01:40:28.380 --> 01:40:29.820
He was alone in the world.

01:40:29.820 --> 01:40:32.100
Risking his life for nothing.

01:40:32.100 --> 01:40:34.140
How could this get any worse?

01:40:34.140 --> 01:40:38.760
His mind kept repeating that question again
and again and again.

01:40:38.760 --> 01:40:45.933
And the universe gave him an answer, in the
form of a deep, reptilian voice saying, “Found

01:40:45.933 --> 01:40:49.320
you...” into his ear from behind.

01:40:49.320 --> 01:40:54.360
He turned with a shriek to see the terrible
eyes of SCP-682 staring into his own.

01:40:54.360 --> 01:40:58.740
Before he could try to flee or reach for a
weapon that he knew would only mildly annoy

01:40:58.740 --> 01:41:03.720
the already furious beast, 682 reached out
with a massive, clawed hand and grabbed him

01:41:03.720 --> 01:41:06.120
by the torso, lifting him up into the air.

01:41:06.120 --> 01:41:09.562
The creature was gripping so tight he could
feel his ribs starting to crack.

01:41:09.562 --> 01:41:14.640
“You laughed at me, Agent Kelly,” the
monster hissed.

01:41:14.640 --> 01:41:17.580
“Am I funny to you?

01:41:17.580 --> 01:41:22.740
Do I seem like the type to tell jokes?

01:41:22.740 --> 01:41:26.880
Do you feel like laughing now?”

01:41:26.880 --> 01:41:32.520
Agent Kelly begged and pleaded for his life,
fighting for his next breath from the crushing

01:41:32.520 --> 01:41:34.860
squeeze of the creature’s terrible hand.

01:41:34.860 --> 01:41:40.260
682 roared at him to be silent and ordered
him to tell him everything he knew about the

01:41:40.260 --> 01:41:41.640
situation going on outside.

01:41:41.640 --> 01:41:47.400
If the information was useful, 682 might show
his thought-to-be-non-existent magnanimous

01:41:47.400 --> 01:41:49.860
side, and let Agent Kelly live.

01:41:49.860 --> 01:41:54.900
Of course, Agent Kelly didn’t fancy his
chances, but what other choice did he have?

01:41:54.900 --> 01:42:01.020
He told 682 that the higher-ups were calling
this SCP-001: When Day Breaks.

01:42:01.020 --> 01:42:06.720
The sun had gone rogue somehow, and being
in contact with any kind of sunlight would

01:42:06.720 --> 01:42:12.360
now cause people to instantaneously melt into
horrifying, living sludge.

01:42:12.360 --> 01:42:13.740
And it wasn’t just people.

01:42:13.740 --> 01:42:19.560
The condition also affected anomalies, and
interestingly, it appeared to negate all previous

01:42:19.560 --> 01:42:26.640
anomalous effects - so 682’s adaptational
ability may not even save it if it was exposed.

01:42:26.640 --> 01:42:29.340
He’d told 682 everything he knew.

01:42:29.340 --> 01:42:31.380
“Are you going to let me live?”

01:42:31.380 --> 01:42:33.960
Agent Kelly asked, struggling to breathe.

01:42:33.960 --> 01:42:38.197
682’s terrible maw twisted into what might
have been a smile.

01:42:38.197 --> 01:42:42.720
“Oh, Agent Kelly,” he said, with unsettling
joy.

01:42:42.720 --> 01:42:44.976
“That was just a joke.

01:42:44.976 --> 01:42:48.360
Didn’t you find that one funny?”

01:42:48.360 --> 01:42:51.300
A terrible scream emanated from the Agent’s
office.

01:42:51.300 --> 01:42:56.280
If one good thing could be said for what happened
to Agent Kelly that day, at least he didn’t

01:42:56.280 --> 01:43:00.000
live long enough to see the ravages of the
terrible sun first hand.

01:43:00.000 --> 01:43:02.640
682 began to formulate a plan.

01:43:02.640 --> 01:43:08.340
He took Agent Kelly’s wristwatch and integrated
it into his body, so he’d have a permanent

01:43:08.340 --> 01:43:09.300
internal clock.

01:43:09.300 --> 01:43:15.360
It was the middle of summer, so the sun would
have reliably set at 9 PM and would likely

01:43:15.360 --> 01:43:17.160
begin its rise at around 5 AM.

01:43:17.160 --> 01:43:21.840
It would be relatively easy to avoid the sun,
all things considered.

01:43:21.840 --> 01:43:26.520
For lack of a more eloquent way to put it,
when it comes to adapting to new threats,

01:43:26.520 --> 01:43:30.900
SCP-682 is simply built different.

01:43:30.900 --> 01:43:35.820
After slaughtering a few other members of
SCP Foundation staff for the road - Hey, it’s

01:43:35.820 --> 01:43:40.860
not like anyone was fit to stop him - 682
began enacting the next phase of his plan.

01:43:40.860 --> 01:43:46.860
His body grew a thick, smooth carapace, and
his front set of limbs began to grow, his

01:43:46.860 --> 01:43:52.800
muscles bulging and his claws growing, the
tips turning into sharp, flat scoops.

01:43:52.800 --> 01:43:58.080
With sudden and tremendous force, 682 began
boring his way into the ground.

01:43:58.080 --> 01:44:02.580
Tunneling, clawing through concrete and dirt
with absolute ease.

01:44:02.580 --> 01:44:07.440
Normally, the SCP Foundation would have deployed
high-tech seismic sensors and the kind of

01:44:07.440 --> 01:44:12.420
tunnel-boring machines that Elon Musk could
only dream of to intercept and recapture him.

01:44:12.420 --> 01:44:18.120
But during the endless horrors of the breaking
day, he had carte blanche to escape and live

01:44:18.120 --> 01:44:20.880
it up in the ruins of this rapidly dying world.

01:44:20.880 --> 01:44:26.940
Eventually, 682 had bored his way into a roomy
sewer pipe, the perfect place to wait out

01:44:26.940 --> 01:44:27.600
a few hours.

01:44:27.600 --> 01:44:32.820
Up above, so many millions screamed, either
in fear or in agony.

01:44:32.820 --> 01:44:37.260
There had been some new developments that
the SCP Foundation had been yet to account

01:44:37.260 --> 01:44:37.680
for.

01:44:37.680 --> 01:44:42.180
While they knew that those melted by the rogue
sun were technically alive and trapped in

01:44:42.180 --> 01:44:44.700
a permanent state of&nbsp;
suffering, what the Foundation&nbsp;

01:44:44.700 --> 01:44:47.460
didn’t know was that these former humans

01:44:47.460 --> 01:44:50.640
were incredibly dangerous in their own right.

01:44:50.640 --> 01:44:56.820
The sun hadn’t just irreparably warped their
bodies, it had also irreparably warped their

01:44:56.820 --> 01:44:57.300
minds.

01:44:57.300 --> 01:44:59.580
It has enslaved them.

01:44:59.580 --> 01:45:00.960
Made them zealots.

01:45:00.960 --> 01:45:02.160
Acolytes.

01:45:02.160 --> 01:45:08.640
They developed the instinct to coagulate into
giant, fleshy masses, driven by the single-minded

01:45:08.640 --> 01:45:15.000
purpose of finding victims and dragging them
out into the light, where they too could be

01:45:15.000 --> 01:45:19.860
converted into these terrible fleshy creatures
and add to the masses.

01:45:19.860 --> 01:45:24.420
They were the rogue sun’s boots on the ground,
metaphorically speaking.

01:45:24.420 --> 01:45:29.760
And now, they were the Foundation’s greatest
challenge in getting a handle on this situation

01:45:29.760 --> 01:45:30.060
again.

01:45:30.060 --> 01:45:33.240
Before, it was just encouraging people to
avoid the sun.

01:45:33.240 --> 01:45:38.460
Now, the sun was actively trying to increase
its exposure.

01:45:38.460 --> 01:45:44.160
But 682, who was having a relaxing evening
not being melted for once down in the sewers,

01:45:44.160 --> 01:45:45.420
couldn’t care less.

01:45:45.420 --> 01:45:49.440
He was having the most calming few hours he’d
had in years.

01:45:49.440 --> 01:45:54.600
He waited, checking the time, making sure
that it would be dark before he began tunneling

01:45:54.600 --> 01:45:55.980
back up to the surface world.

01:45:55.980 --> 01:46:01.080
He surfaced in the middle of a city, miles
away from the Foundation facility he’d spend

01:46:01.080 --> 01:46:03.000
so many decades being tortured in.

01:46:03.000 --> 01:46:08.880
He tasted the cool night air and observed
the desolation that had been wrought all around

01:46:08.880 --> 01:46:09.240
him.

01:46:09.240 --> 01:46:10.980
Buildings were on fire.

01:46:10.980 --> 01:46:13.620
Cars were crashed and overturned.

01:46:13.620 --> 01:46:15.240
The ground was cracked.

01:46:15.240 --> 01:46:18.480
Garbled SCP Foundation&nbsp;
Public Service Announcements&nbsp;

01:46:18.480 --> 01:46:21.300
played to nobody in the broken display windows

01:46:21.300 --> 01:46:22.380
of electronic stores.

01:46:22.380 --> 01:46:28.200
Giant wads of human flesh roamed, slithering
around, searching for new victims.

01:46:28.200 --> 01:46:34.020
One noticed 682 and began to approach him,
gibbering madly in a chorus of strange voices.

01:46:34.020 --> 01:46:37.380
The Hard to Destroy Reptile wasted no time
in attacking.

01:46:37.380 --> 01:46:42.420
It tore apart most of the hideous blob and
began hungrily devouring the chunks.

01:46:42.420 --> 01:46:51.720
The form may have been different, but it still
tasted like human flesh, and SCP-682 savored

01:46:51.720 --> 01:46:52.620
every single bite.

01:46:52.620 --> 01:46:55.020
It would be so simple.

01:46:55.020 --> 01:47:00.960
These blobs of idiotic flesh were so easy
to kill, and there would be so many terrified

01:47:00.960 --> 01:47:07.560
humans in this devastated world, hiding away
in dark places, holding out the hope that

01:47:07.560 --> 01:47:11.520
maybe they could reach the safety of a Foundation
facility.

01:47:11.520 --> 01:47:14.160
682 chuckled at the very thought.

01:47:14.160 --> 01:47:20.580
Foolish hope would drown in an endless well
of black, caustic despair.

01:47:20.580 --> 01:47:22.860
He would find them.

01:47:22.860 --> 01:47:27.480
He would rest underground in the day and then
hunt them in the dark.

01:47:27.480 --> 01:47:33.900
They would all die screaming, bloodying his
claws and fangs.

01:47:33.900 --> 01:47:37.560
Nothing and nobody would stop him.

01:47:37.560 --> 01:47:42.360
He looked out over this strange new world
and laughed a little louder.

01:47:43.980 --> 01:47:47.520
It was just...

01:47:47.520 --> 01:47:48.600
Delightful.

01:47:48.600 --> 01:47:56.400
Another day, another failed attempt to execute
SCP-682 - The infamous Hard To Destroy Reptile.

01:47:56.400 --> 01:48:02.580
The most recent attempt was SCP-272, an Old
Iron Nail with the ability to pin people’s

01:48:02.580 --> 01:48:06.900
shadows to the ground and tear them to shreds
when different configurations of light make

01:48:06.900 --> 01:48:08.340
their shadows go haywire.

01:48:08.340 --> 01:48:11.520
Just when it seemed like 272 and a high-powered&nbsp;

01:48:11.520 --> 01:48:13.980
disco ball might be the&nbsp;
thing to win the Foundation’s

01:48:13.980 --> 01:48:18.960
war against the misanthropic lizard, it did
what it always did: Pulled out a trump card,

01:48:18.960 --> 01:48:20.460
and ruined everything.

01:48:20.460 --> 01:48:26.160
Its body evolved a sudden, intense bioluminescence
that completely eliminated the beast’s shadow

01:48:26.160 --> 01:48:28.920
by overpowering all other light sources in
the room.

01:48:28.920 --> 01:48:33.540
This not only rendered the Foundation’s
strobe lights utterly useless, but blinded

01:48:33.540 --> 01:48:37.800
several members of D-Class personnel who were
sent in to check on the beast during testing.

01:48:37.800 --> 01:48:42.780
This resulted, predictably, in another Big,
Fat L for the SCP Foundation.

01:48:42.780 --> 01:48:47.220
682: 435, Foundation: 0.

01:48:47.220 --> 01:48:50.280
And nobody was more frustrated by this than
Dr. Samet.

01:48:50.280 --> 01:48:53.280
Samet was a Foundation greenhorn with big
ambitions.

01:48:53.280 --> 01:48:57.540
Like every jerk at the office, he was less
concerned with doing his job right, and far

01:48:57.540 --> 01:48:59.760
more concerned with climbing the corporate
ladder.

01:48:59.760 --> 01:49:04.320
Samet had done all he could to cozy up to
Site Directors and even the Overseers far

01:49:04.320 --> 01:49:08.400
above, all with the goal of someday getting
a seat at their high table.

01:49:08.400 --> 01:49:14.160
But as any SCP fans know, they’re not just
giving out positions on or just under the

01:49:14.160 --> 01:49:15.000
O5 Council.

01:49:15.000 --> 01:49:18.480
To swing something like that, you need to
really make an impression.

01:49:18.480 --> 01:49:19.920
You need to wow them.

01:49:19.920 --> 01:49:25.080
And what would be a better way to do that
than being the person who killed SCP-682?

01:49:25.080 --> 01:49:30.060
Surely, if he actually buried that beast,
they’d hand him the keys to the proverbial

01:49:30.060 --> 01:49:30.360
castle.

01:49:30.360 --> 01:49:36.120
So Dr. Samet had done everything he could
to get reassigned to the 682 termination effort,

01:49:36.120 --> 01:49:40.680
and only now was he realizing just how in
over his head he truly was.

01:49:40.680 --> 01:49:43.260
Dr. Samet needed help from a higher power.

01:49:43.260 --> 01:49:48.660
If he even hoped of beating SCP-682, the man
needed God on his side.

01:49:48.660 --> 01:49:52.740
Thankfully, they just so happened to have
God chilling out in his containment cell in

01:49:52.740 --> 01:49:53.760
Site 17.

01:49:53.760 --> 01:49:58.560
Perhaps, through enlisting the help of earth’s
divine arbiter, he could bring an end to the

01:49:58.560 --> 01:50:03.240
scourge of SCP-682 and rocket himself to success
in the process.

01:50:03.240 --> 01:50:08.100
However, while Dr. Samet may have been arrogant,
he wasn’t completely delusional.

01:50:08.100 --> 01:50:13.080
He knew that he didn’t have the standing
to address SCP-343 directly, much less to

01:50:13.080 --> 01:50:16.620
ask him for a hand in destroying SCP-682.

01:50:16.620 --> 01:50:18.420
He’d need a go-between.

01:50:18.420 --> 01:50:24.540
Someone with tenure, someone who commanded
respect among SCP Foundation staff as well

01:50:24.540 --> 01:50:26.220
as the very anomalies they governed.

01:50:26.220 --> 01:50:30.000
Perhaps someone who was a little bit anomalous
themselves…

01:50:30.000 --> 01:50:35.040
And who better fits this description than
the living legend, Dr. Jack Bright?

01:50:35.040 --> 01:50:38.520
Dr. Samet had, of course, read the doctor’s
personnel files.

01:50:38.520 --> 01:50:42.840
Everybody at the Foundation knew about Dr.
Bright’s exploits - From what he’s done,

01:50:42.840 --> 01:50:47.100
to the various things he isn’t allowed to
do, which we’ll cover in a future video.

01:50:47.100 --> 01:50:53.400
He also dug up the SCP-963 files: The anomalous
medallion keeping Dr. Bright alive, whether

01:50:53.400 --> 01:50:54.600
he likes it or not.

01:50:54.600 --> 01:50:58.680
While a discussion of the exact nature of
the medallion isn’t something you’d want

01:50:58.680 --> 01:51:03.720
to have in front of Dr. Bright himself - After
all, it’s a touchy subject - you could make

01:51:03.720 --> 01:51:06.240
the argument that the medallion is the real
him.

01:51:06.240 --> 01:51:11.040
It’s where his soul is condemned to spend
perhaps the rest of eternity, killing and

01:51:11.040 --> 01:51:14.040
stealing the body of anyone or anything that
touched it.

01:51:14.040 --> 01:51:19.080
He’d become an immortal parasite, destined
to take the finite lives of others while his

01:51:19.080 --> 01:51:20.400
own marches on forever.

01:51:20.400 --> 01:51:21.840
Remind you of anyone?

01:51:21.840 --> 01:51:26.940
Dr. Samet got into contact with Dr. Bright
and explained his plan: With Bright’s help,

01:51:26.940 --> 01:51:32.880
he’d recruit SCP-343, and bring the very
wrath of God down onto the Hard to Destroy

01:51:32.880 --> 01:51:33.360
Reptile.

01:51:33.360 --> 01:51:37.920
Of course, while Dr. Samet naturally assumed
himself to be the smartest person in the room,

01:51:37.920 --> 01:51:42.840
Dr. Bright had a more realistic assessment
of the ambitious young turk’s skills.

01:51:42.840 --> 01:51:49.320
He saw Samet for what he truly was: A climber,
a buttkisser, a greedy, power-hungry bureaucrat

01:51:49.320 --> 01:51:52.560
wearing a lab coat, and he thought that made
him a researcher?

01:51:53.400 --> 01:51:54.360
It was laughable.

01:51:54.360 --> 01:51:59.160
What Dr. Bright found less funny, though,
was Dr. Samet’s insistence on calling him

01:51:59.160 --> 01:52:01.380
“SCP-963.”

01:52:01.380 --> 01:52:05.580
There’s a lot to know about Dr. Bright,
but one thing you should definitely commit

01:52:05.580 --> 01:52:12.060
to memory is that you should never, under
any circumstances, call Dr. Bright SCP-963.

01:52:12.060 --> 01:52:16.860
And if you were forever entwined with a necklace
that doomed you to watch everyone you know

01:52:16.860 --> 01:52:21.900
and love age and die, while depriving you
of that same release, you’d probably resent

01:52:21.900 --> 01:52:23.400
being associated with it, too.

01:52:23.400 --> 01:52:28.020
Dr. Bright did agree to participate in Dr.
Samet’s harebrained termination scheme,

01:52:28.020 --> 01:52:34.320
but with a warning that he did not give lightly:
If ever Dr. Samet called him 963 again, he

01:52:34.320 --> 01:52:38.400
would have one of his own loyal team members
- nicknamed The Lucky Bunch, for their high

01:52:38.400 --> 01:52:42.900
survival rate compared to other Foundation
research teams - shoot him in the foot.

01:52:42.900 --> 01:52:47.880
Dr. Bright steeled himself and entered 343’s
containment cell, where the playful deity

01:52:47.880 --> 01:52:52.740
had taken the form of the late comedian George
Burns, complete with his trademark glasses

01:52:52.740 --> 01:52:54.420
and half-smoked stogy.

01:52:54.420 --> 01:52:59.460
They made small talk, with 343 delivering
his usual high-handed, cryptic parables about

01:52:59.460 --> 01:53:01.860
his plans for Dr. Bright, and everybody else.

01:53:01.860 --> 01:53:05.820
He even momentarily teased the idea of freeing
him from his curse.

01:53:05.820 --> 01:53:09.240
But Dr. Bright knew better than to buy into
these fairy tales.

01:53:09.240 --> 01:53:15.840
He talked SCP-343 into a cross test, but didn’t
tell him that it was with 682, or that he

01:53:15.840 --> 01:53:17.400
was expected to terminate it.

01:53:17.400 --> 01:53:19.800
That was better left as a surprise.

01:53:19.800 --> 01:53:24.720
Dr. Samet and Dr. Bright stood in the observation
area outside the cross-testing chamber.

01:53:24.720 --> 01:53:28.560
Samet was giddy with excitement and confidence
in this new experiment.

01:53:28.560 --> 01:53:31.740
Dr. Bright’s reactions were a hell of a
lot more measured.

01:53:31.740 --> 01:53:36.780
He’d been working at the Foundation long
enough now to know that terminating SCP-682

01:53:36.780 --> 01:53:38.040
was a fool’s errand.

01:53:38.040 --> 01:53:43.140
The only researchers still intent on trying
it were doing so out of stubbornness and ego.

01:53:43.140 --> 01:53:48.540
And when 343 and 682 were released into the
chamber, Dr. Bright’s healthy pessimism

01:53:48.540 --> 01:53:49.740
was more than justified.

01:53:49.740 --> 01:53:55.020
682 attacked a nearby door, attempting to
breach containment, while 343 looked around,

01:53:55.020 --> 01:53:57.600
confused and seemingly unable to see anything.

01:53:57.600 --> 01:54:02.520
When he was ordered to kill 682, he was shocked
to learn 682 was even in the room.

01:54:02.520 --> 01:54:06.420
He stormed off moments later in a huff, saying,
“He's not one of mine.

01:54:06.420 --> 01:54:07.620
Deal with him yourself.”

01:54:08.460 --> 01:54:10.620
Dr. Bright was unsurprised.

01:54:10.620 --> 01:54:12.840
Dr. Samet was shocked and furious.

01:54:12.840 --> 01:54:14.400
How could this have failed?

01:54:14.400 --> 01:54:16.500
They literally had God on their side!

01:54:16.500 --> 01:54:21.000
This setback would seriously compromise his
chances of rising through the ranks, unless

01:54:21.000 --> 01:54:24.840
he found a quick way to make the best out
of a bad situation and save face.

01:54:24.840 --> 01:54:27.900
Without even thinking, he turned to Dr. Bright
and said:

01:54:27.900 --> 01:54:28.440
“Fine.

01:54:28.440 --> 01:54:29.160
It didn't work.

01:54:29.160 --> 01:54:29.760
Doesn't matter.

01:54:29.760 --> 01:54:32.100
Get yourself ready 963, you're going in.”

01:54:32.100 --> 01:54:34.380
So it was decided.

01:54:34.380 --> 01:54:40.200
Dr. Bright himself would face off with SCP-682
in SCP-343’s place.

01:54:40.200 --> 01:54:45.060
Dr. Bright was a betting man, he loved a good
game of chance, and he estimated that his

01:54:45.060 --> 01:54:47.160
odds of succeeding were exceptionally low.

01:54:47.160 --> 01:54:49.260
But what would be the point in refusing?

01:54:49.260 --> 01:54:54.660
Even if he couldn’t kill SCP-682, perhaps
he would get lucky, and the reptile would

01:54:54.660 --> 01:54:55.380
kill him instead.

01:54:55.380 --> 01:54:57.540
So many enticing possibilities.

01:54:57.540 --> 01:55:00.180
Dr. Bright left to prepare for the coming
battle.

01:55:00.180 --> 01:55:05.040
And, because nobody would say that Dr. Bright
wasn’t a man of his word, he had one of

01:55:05.040 --> 01:55:07.320
his assistants shoot Dr. Samet in the foot.

01:55:07.320 --> 01:55:12.120
A few days later, Dr. Bright, Dr. Samet - Now
in a wheelchair while he recovered from his

01:55:12.120 --> 01:55:16.980
unfortunate foot injury - and a collection
of other researchers, including Dr. Sophia

01:55:16.980 --> 01:55:22.380
Light, were convened in a conference room,
planning out their assault on SCP-682.

01:55:22.380 --> 01:55:27.660
A mechanical “staff” of sorts was laying
on the table in front of him, a kind of powerful

01:55:27.660 --> 01:55:30.780
taser capable of firing out painful bolts
of electricity.

01:55:30.780 --> 01:55:35.640
It would be the only object Dr. Bright carried
into the chamber with him that day.

01:55:35.640 --> 01:55:40.800
But only as a way of getting 682’s attention,
not as a weapon.

01:55:40.800 --> 01:55:44.040
The true weapon was SCP-963.

01:55:44.040 --> 01:55:51.780
The plan was simple: SCP-682 would eat Dr.
Bright, and the power of SCP-963 would destroy

01:55:51.780 --> 01:55:52.440
it from within.

01:55:52.440 --> 01:55:57.780
As anyone with an awareness of 963’s anomalous
properties could tell you, for most living

01:55:57.780 --> 01:55:59.940
beings, touching the medallion results in&nbsp;

01:55:59.940 --> 01:56:02.340
immediate brain death,&nbsp;
followed by the consciousness

01:56:02.340 --> 01:56:04.740
of Dr. Bright inhabiting your mindless body.

01:56:04.740 --> 01:56:10.380
If they could get this phenomenon to work
for SCP-682, perhaps, with Dr. Bright’s

01:56:10.380 --> 01:56:15.720
mind in 682’s body, could they now end the
life of this wretched beast once and for all?

01:56:15.720 --> 01:56:21.780
Like with all matters involving SCP-682 and
Dr. Bright, it was most likely not going to

01:56:21.780 --> 01:56:22.740
be so simple.

01:56:22.740 --> 01:56:28.020
When Dr. Bright entered the test chamber with
682, as Dr. Samet and the others watched from

01:56:28.020 --> 01:56:31.320
the observation room, the results were sudden
and violent.

01:56:31.320 --> 01:56:34.020
Dr. Bright zapped the monster&nbsp;
with his electro-staff,&nbsp;

01:56:34.020 --> 01:56:36.900
and it came charging for him, a terrible fury

01:56:36.900 --> 01:56:38.460
of teeth and claws.

01:56:38.460 --> 01:56:43.740
Dr. Bright had died so many times, and yet,
he couldn’t even recall many experiences

01:56:43.740 --> 01:56:45.240
more unpleasant than this.

01:56:45.240 --> 01:56:49.740
And as 682’s interior flesh met SCP-963…

01:56:49.740 --> 01:56:53.820
Dr. Bright woke up in the middle of a strange
new place.

01:56:53.820 --> 01:56:59.160
There was a man standing over him that looked
oddly familiar, except for the strange chainmail

01:56:59.160 --> 01:57:00.360
hauberk he was wearing.

01:57:00.360 --> 01:57:05.160
When Dr. Bright found his feet, he recognized
the man: It was a D-Class.

01:57:05.160 --> 01:57:10.740
In fact, the first body he’d ever inhabited
after his soul fused with SCP-963.

01:57:10.740 --> 01:57:12.360
But he wasn’t alone here.

01:57:12.360 --> 01:57:17.400
There were so many people, all of them wearing
the same chainmail, and carrying the same

01:57:17.400 --> 01:57:20.640
electro-staffs that Dr. Bright had carried
into the chamber with him.

01:57:20.640 --> 01:57:27.240
Little by little, he recognized every single
one of the faces: They were all people whose

01:57:27.240 --> 01:57:28.500
bodies he’d taken.

01:57:28.500 --> 01:57:31.920
Whose lives he’d cut short, to further his
own.

01:57:31.920 --> 01:57:38.040
He looked around and saw more bizarre sights:
A grand castle, structured like a deranged

01:57:38.040 --> 01:57:38.940
Escher painting.

01:57:38.940 --> 01:57:46.080
And up above, drowning out the sky, was a
great, reptilian behemoth, like SCP-682 on

01:57:46.080 --> 01:57:49.500
steroids, made entirely from barbecue sauce.

01:57:49.500 --> 01:57:55.920
The D-Class broke the surreal news: None of
this was real, it was a fantasy his mind had

01:57:55.920 --> 01:58:00.840
concocted to help him cope with his consciousness
bonding with SCP-682.

01:58:00.840 --> 01:58:04.260
A more palatable way of perceiving his new
reality.

01:58:04.260 --> 01:58:10.020
And if he ever wanted to get out and be himself
again, he would need to fight and conquer

01:58:10.020 --> 01:58:11.160
the beast within.

01:58:11.160 --> 01:58:17.100
Dr. Bright joined forces with his past victims,
including one former Level 2 Researcher, Damon

01:58:17.100 --> 01:58:17.340
Smith.

01:58:17.340 --> 01:58:22.920
Together, using their electro-staffs, Bright
and his army of mental constructs blasted

01:58:22.920 --> 01:58:26.220
the great monster in the sky from the safe
confines of the castle.

01:58:26.220 --> 01:58:30.600
However, things weren’t quite as safe as
Dr. Bright had first imagined.

01:58:30.600 --> 01:58:35.340
The massive creature descended upon them,
tearing the castle to shreds with its huge

01:58:35.340 --> 01:58:35.880
claws.

01:58:35.880 --> 01:58:39.240
The construct of Damon Smith was devoured
in the process.

01:58:39.240 --> 01:58:45.180
Dr. Bright’s brief illusion of victory was
soon stifled by one immutable fact: You could

01:58:45.180 --> 01:58:47.820
not defeat SCP-682.

01:58:47.820 --> 01:58:52.380
He retreated from the monster into the darkness
of his own nightmares.

01:58:52.380 --> 01:58:53.940
From there, he woke up.

01:58:53.940 --> 01:58:59.700
Dr. Bright was in a hospital bed, the medallion
attached to a new body after 682’s body

01:58:59.700 --> 01:59:00.600
had rejected it.

01:59:00.600 --> 01:59:04.860
He was greeted by Dr. Sophia Light and a member
of the O5 Council.

01:59:04.860 --> 01:59:07.740
Dr. Bright had effectively been gone for days.

01:59:07.740 --> 01:59:13.320
When he asked what happened on the outside,
he was told that 682 had entered a 36-hour

01:59:13.320 --> 01:59:18.480
coma, before growing massive claws and tunneling
out of containment, where it caused a massive

01:59:18.480 --> 01:59:18.960
breach.

01:59:18.960 --> 01:59:24.300
Though strangely, upon breaking out of the
chamber, it only attacked one researcher…

01:59:24.300 --> 01:59:29.700
And in unrelated news, Dr. Samet had been
taken off the 682 case.

01:59:29.700 --> 01:59:34.260
It didn’t take long for things to return
to normal for Dr. Bright - Well, as normal

01:59:34.260 --> 01:59:39.840
as life can be when you’re a man as strange
as him - but while few would notice it, 682

01:59:39.840 --> 01:59:41.100
was left altered.

01:59:41.100 --> 01:59:46.380
It had taken a souvenir from Dr. Bright: Fragments
of the consciousness of Damon Smith.

01:59:46.380 --> 01:59:49.140
It felt his pain, his fear.

01:59:49.140 --> 01:59:53.340
It tasted it, dissected it, and now understood
it.

01:59:53.340 --> 01:59:59.040
And when the opportunity presented itself
once more, as it always did, he couldn’t

01:59:59.040 --> 02:00:01.380
wait to inflict it on others...

02:00:01.380 --> 02:00:09.240
Able wandered through the sands, a lone warrior,
dragging a long, dark sword behind him, his

02:00:09.240 --> 02:00:11.880
black cloak flowing in the gentle breeze.

02:00:11.880 --> 02:00:13.860
The sword was thirsty.

02:00:13.860 --> 02:00:16.740
It’d been too long since it tasted blood.

02:00:16.740 --> 02:00:17.940
What had it been?

02:00:17.940 --> 02:00:21.900
A day since he cut down ten men in a tavern
without breaking a sweat?

02:00:21.900 --> 02:00:26.820
They’d bled and screamed like pigs as he’d
diced them into bloody chunks.

02:00:26.820 --> 02:00:28.800
He couldn’t remember their faces.

02:00:28.800 --> 02:00:30.720
They hadn’t earned that.

02:00:30.720 --> 02:00:35.160
Very few combatants had been remarkable enough
to warrant committing to memory.

02:00:35.160 --> 02:00:37.800
It was all just more dead flesh.

02:00:37.800 --> 02:00:40.080
He took a sip from his canteen and sighed.

02:00:40.080 --> 02:00:42.780
Did this world hold no more challenges?

02:00:42.780 --> 02:00:46.260
What a boring eternity was laying out before
him.

02:00:46.260 --> 02:00:51.360
His burden as the greatest warrior of all
time weighed on him heavier than the chain.

02:00:51.360 --> 02:00:56.820
It was old and rusty, levered over his shoulder
and grasped in one bloody hand.

02:00:56.820 --> 02:01:02.820
About fifteen feet behind him, the chain was
connected to a dark, stone sarcophagus that

02:01:02.820 --> 02:01:05.940
was as much a part of him as his eyes, skin,
or heart.

02:01:05.940 --> 02:01:11.400
If ever he was slain in the glorious heat
of battle, he’d rise out of it, ready to

02:01:11.400 --> 02:01:13.440
fight and kill another day.

02:01:13.440 --> 02:01:18.000
All because of the actions of his worthless,
good for nothing brother…

02:01:18.000 --> 02:01:21.900
He looked up when he heard the rush of footsteps
and the clanking of armor.

02:01:21.900 --> 02:01:27.120
Warriors - or whatever passed for them around
here - about twenty of them, circled all around

02:01:27.120 --> 02:01:27.480
him.

02:01:27.480 --> 02:01:30.240
Yes, oh yes.

02:01:30.240 --> 02:01:32.640
His grip tightened around his sword.

02:01:32.640 --> 02:01:37.440
One of the warriors called out something about
him being under arrest, by order of the king,

02:01:37.440 --> 02:01:39.300
for murders beyond counting.

02:01:39.300 --> 02:01:41.220
Able couldn’t help but yawn.

02:01:41.220 --> 02:01:42.660
Words, words, words.

02:01:42.660 --> 02:01:44.940
Why even bother?

02:01:44.940 --> 02:01:49.440
He dropped the chain, and in one fluid motion,
he threw his sword.

02:01:49.440 --> 02:01:54.420
In a fraction of a second, it’d pierced
the armor of the chattering man, spearing

02:01:54.420 --> 02:01:56.400
him through his formerly beating heart.

02:01:56.400 --> 02:02:01.620
The scream died in his throat, he fell to
his knees, then collapsed entirely.

02:02:01.620 --> 02:02:06.300
The other soldiers sent to kill or apprehend
him turned to their fallen leader and gasped.

02:02:06.300 --> 02:02:09.600
It was that little gasp,&nbsp;
that moment of distraction,&nbsp;

02:02:09.600 --> 02:02:11.400
that sealed their fates.

02:02:11.400 --> 02:02:16.860
Able’s face cracked into a whisper of a
grin, as he drew two long daggers from the

02:02:16.860 --> 02:02:18.180
darkness of his coat.

02:02:18.180 --> 02:02:20.700
He’d at least try to have fun with this…

02:02:20.700 --> 02:02:25.140
Before the others could even get over their
leader’s sudden death, Able had vaulted

02:02:25.140 --> 02:02:27.780
forward and begun his delicate dance of slaughter.

02:02:27.780 --> 02:02:31.740
Every swing found its way through armor and
into skin.

02:02:31.740 --> 02:02:37.020
He sliced throats, cleaved off heads, parried
blows, and pierced hearts.

02:02:37.020 --> 02:02:39.060
There was barely a single scream.

02:02:39.060 --> 02:02:41.880
Able killed too quick for screams.

02:02:41.880 --> 02:02:46.920
In what would seem like the blink of an eye
for some, the soldiers around Able fell.

02:02:46.920 --> 02:02:49.200
Most dead, the rest dying.

02:02:49.200 --> 02:02:54.420
Some looked up to him in their dying moments,
in terrified awe at the efficacy of their

02:02:54.420 --> 02:02:54.840
killer.

02:02:54.840 --> 02:02:58.980
In their dying moments, they knew that they
never had a chance.

02:02:58.980 --> 02:03:03.960
They might as well have faced the glistening
scythe of death himself on the battlefield.

02:03:03.960 --> 02:03:06.960
Able, on the other hand, rolled his eyes and
sighed.

02:03:06.960 --> 02:03:09.660
Another pathetic waste of time.

02:03:09.660 --> 02:03:14.460
He sensed movement in the corner of his eye:
One of the wounded soldiers was limping to

02:03:14.460 --> 02:03:17.820
his feet, trying to use the sword to lever
himself off of the ground.

02:03:17.820 --> 02:03:22.980
With a flick of each wrist, Able tossed his
knives into the man, killing him instantly.

02:03:22.980 --> 02:03:24.840
It really was that easy.

02:03:24.840 --> 02:03:30.180
“Your attempt to kill me does not offend
me,” he said, to whoever was still able

02:03:30.180 --> 02:03:30.540
to hear.

02:03:30.540 --> 02:03:37.020
“What offends me is that they would send
so few, and that those few would be such pitiful

02:03:37.020 --> 02:03:38.580
excuses for soldiers.

02:03:38.580 --> 02:03:43.320
This wasn’t a battle - It was a mercy killing.”

02:03:43.320 --> 02:03:48.600
He was ready to turn around, grab the chain,
and carry on walking, when he felt a sudden

02:03:48.600 --> 02:03:49.680
pain in his back.

02:03:49.680 --> 02:03:53.580
There was a slight whistle, then another sharp
spike of pain.

02:03:53.580 --> 02:03:56.580
There were now two arrows sticking out of
his back.

02:03:56.580 --> 02:04:01.380
Able turned, surprised, and saw a much larger
force standing behind him.

02:04:01.380 --> 02:04:05.820
Swordsmen, archers, men with clubs and axes
and chains.

02:04:05.820 --> 02:04:08.880
The ones he’d killed were little more than
a distraction.

02:04:08.880 --> 02:04:11.100
This was the real threat.

02:04:11.100 --> 02:04:13.140
This was the real army.

02:04:13.140 --> 02:04:16.980
Perhaps, these fools would give him some actual
exercise.

02:04:16.980 --> 02:04:21.480
He reached into his cloak and pulled out a
mighty obsidian battle axe.

02:04:21.480 --> 02:04:26.880
At the very least, he’d try to have a little
fun turning this fighting force into cold

02:04:26.880 --> 02:04:27.420
cuts.

02:04:27.420 --> 02:04:32.160
A fog of arrows sailed through the air as
he charged forwards, perforating his body,

02:04:32.160 --> 02:04:34.560
but the injuries didn’t slow him down.

02:04:34.560 --> 02:04:37.020
He lunged, slashed, and cleaved.

02:04:37.020 --> 02:04:41.340
Even as the weapons struck him, he carried
on, killing person after person.

02:04:41.340 --> 02:04:46.080
At times, it was almost exciting - Almost,
but not quite.

02:04:46.080 --> 02:04:48.900
By the time he was done, none were left standing.

02:04:48.900 --> 02:04:51.000
Thirty arrows were sticking out of him.

02:04:51.000 --> 02:04:55.620
He’d been cut deep by more weapons than
he could count on his fingers and toes.

02:04:55.620 --> 02:04:59.520
He was breathing deeply, scarred chest pumping
up and down.

02:04:59.520 --> 02:05:02.520
He coughed blood and cracked his neck back
into place.

02:05:02.520 --> 02:05:05.040
They might’ve cut him a little too deep
this time.

02:05:05.040 --> 02:05:06.000
No matter.

02:05:06.000 --> 02:05:10.020
Able fell to his knees, feeling the life draining
from him.

02:05:10.020 --> 02:05:13.800
He wondered, when he awoke from the coffin
again, what the world would look like.

02:05:13.800 --> 02:05:18.780
Sometimes it was days, sometimes weeks, months,
or even years.

02:05:18.780 --> 02:05:24.360
As he fell forward, dying once again, he hoped
that he’d wake into a world with a warrior

02:05:24.360 --> 02:05:26.820
or beast that could actually challenge him.

02:05:26.820 --> 02:05:28.260
Maybe someday…

02:05:28.260 --> 02:05:34.140
This was one of Able’s many lives, hundreds
of years before he was contained by the SCP

02:05:34.140 --> 02:05:34.740
Foundation.

02:05:34.740 --> 02:05:39.120
He’s perhaps the greatest warrior who ever
lived, died, and lived again.

02:05:39.120 --> 02:05:44.040
He’s a man so individually deadly that not
only is he kept in a containment chamber under

02:05:44.040 --> 02:05:49.560
the sea, surrounded by highly trained and
armed guards, he has his own localized on-site

02:05:49.560 --> 02:05:55.620
nuclear weapon, ready to blow away and annihilate
him and his entire containment area if deemed

02:05:55.620 --> 02:05:56.160
necessary.

02:05:56.160 --> 02:06:02.340
He may not be a contagious anomalous pathogen
or a lethal memetic hazard or a giant beast

02:06:02.340 --> 02:06:06.840
shooting world-destroying fireballs in every
direction, but if this one-man massacre was

02:06:06.840 --> 02:06:11.340
left to his own devices, there’s no doubt
that he would methodically slaughter his way

02:06:11.340 --> 02:06:16.680
through the human race until an XK-Class End
of the World Scenario was practically inevitable.

02:06:16.680 --> 02:06:21.060
He was fueled by pure hatred and an almost
bottomless bloodlust.

02:06:21.060 --> 02:06:24.000
He simply lived to fight and kill.

02:06:24.000 --> 02:06:28.800
And not only did he have the will and the
skill to be a pure force of annihilation,

02:06:28.800 --> 02:06:32.880
but his anomalous abilities also make him
perfectly tailored to the task.

02:06:32.880 --> 02:06:38.100
He has massively enhanced physical strength,
speed, and durability, taking the kind of

02:06:38.100 --> 02:06:43.140
damage that would kill several normal humans
to reliably put him down - Though even that

02:06:43.140 --> 02:06:45.000
is only a temporary measure.

02:06:45.000 --> 02:06:51.120
Able will always resurrect back into his black
sarcophagus to menace the SCP Foundation another

02:06:51.120 --> 02:06:51.540
day.

02:06:51.540 --> 02:06:56.280
It is also effectively impossible to disarm
Able, because he has the anomalous ability

02:06:56.280 --> 02:07:01.740
to pull deadly edged weapons from localized
pocket dimensions at will, and his proficiency

02:07:01.740 --> 02:07:07.260
with these weapons is unlike any warrior the
world has ever known, before or since.

02:07:07.260 --> 02:07:12.120
During containment breaches, he’s regularly
killed scores of trained Foundation guards,

02:07:12.120 --> 02:07:16.860
with both numerical advantages and considerably
more advanced ranged weapons.

02:07:16.860 --> 02:07:23.340
Despite being a simple humanoid, he was taking
up a truly insane amount of containment resources.

02:07:23.340 --> 02:07:30.060
Despite his violent tendencies, Able is still
a recognizable sentient human, albeit an extremely

02:07:30.060 --> 02:07:31.320
deadly anomalous one.

02:07:31.320 --> 02:07:36.240
This led some higher-ups at the Foundation
to come up with an interesting idea: What

02:07:36.240 --> 02:07:38.700
if Able’s eternal rage could be harnessed?

02:07:38.700 --> 02:07:43.800
What if they could use their resources to
reshape this rampaging killer into a devoted

02:07:43.800 --> 02:07:45.540
sword of the Foundation’s cause?

02:07:45.540 --> 02:07:51.060
After all, if he wanted worthy opponents,
what could be more worthy than the anomalous

02:07:51.060 --> 02:07:54.180
monsters that the Foundation faced on a daily
basis?

02:07:54.180 --> 02:07:59.340
And as long as they kept the sarcophagus,
even if Able was killed in the line of duty,

02:07:59.340 --> 02:08:01.140
he’d still be accounted for.

02:08:01.140 --> 02:08:06.240
In many ways, if he could be trained and truly
brought to heel, there could be no better

02:08:06.240 --> 02:08:08.580
asset to their coming struggles.

02:08:08.580 --> 02:08:14.640
It was this logic, allowing anomalies to work
for the SCP Foundation in exchange for benefits,

02:08:14.640 --> 02:08:22.440
that led to the creation of a new, groundbreaking
Mobile Task Force: MTF Omega-7, Pandora’s

02:08:22.440 --> 02:08:22.620
Box.

02:08:22.620 --> 02:08:26.340
This group became the SCP Foundation’s hail
mary pass.

02:08:26.340 --> 02:08:31.980
For any particularly dangerous or potentially
deadly mission, they could send in Able, along

02:08:31.980 --> 02:08:36.300
with a group of highly-trained Foundation
soldiers that even the ancient, blade-wielding

02:08:36.300 --> 02:08:37.680
warrior held respect for.

02:08:37.680 --> 02:08:42.780
While, like their namesake, Pandora’s Box,
it would all wind up in terrible tragedy,

02:08:42.780 --> 02:08:47.340
to begin with, they achieved some of the highest
mission successful results of any Mobile Task

02:08:47.340 --> 02:08:48.900
Force on the Foundation’s payroll.

02:08:48.900 --> 02:08:53.040
No task was too challenging for them to swoop
in and crush it.

02:08:53.040 --> 02:08:58.560
This was far from expected: Able, one of the
most violent SCPs they’d ever contained,

02:08:58.560 --> 02:09:01.200
suddenly becoming a great&nbsp;
asset to their operations.

02:09:01.200 --> 02:09:05.160
A vital tool in their quest to keep the anomalous
at bay.

02:09:05.160 --> 02:09:10.380
He’d cleaved through legions of Chaos Insurgency
soldiers during breaches into their secure

02:09:10.380 --> 02:09:10.860
sites.

02:09:10.860 --> 02:09:15.420
He’d fought off the well-paid, well-trained,
and well-armed body guards of Marshall, Carter,

02:09:15.420 --> 02:09:19.620
and Dark Ltd. during Foundation raids on their
clandestine operations.

02:09:19.620 --> 02:09:24.240
He’d even gone toe to toe with some of the
deadliest anomalies in containment during

02:09:24.240 --> 02:09:25.260
mass escapes.

02:09:25.260 --> 02:09:28.680
It was hard to imagine how they’d ever lived
without him.

02:09:28.680 --> 02:09:34.140
Of course, while Able was happier than he’d
been in years - in his element, in fact, as

02:09:34.140 --> 02:09:38.460
a working warrior, given varied missions and
frequent opponents - there was still something

02:09:38.460 --> 02:09:39.480
nagging at him.

02:09:39.480 --> 02:09:45.420
His thoughts were hounded by his white whale:
The endless search for a truly worthy opponent,

02:09:45.420 --> 02:09:50.580
someone or something that could really give
him a run for his money.

02:09:50.580 --> 02:09:55.260
After millennia of leaving opponents dead
in his wake, nothing would bring him more

02:09:55.260 --> 02:09:58.920
joy than meeting something that actually knocked
him on his ass.

02:09:58.920 --> 02:10:02.040
A new bar somewhere above him to work towards.

02:10:02.040 --> 02:10:04.740
Oh, what a glorious day that would be…

02:10:04.740 --> 02:10:09.960
Eventually, the Foundation started to run
into a problem: They were running out of missions

02:10:09.960 --> 02:10:10.860
to give Able.

02:10:10.860 --> 02:10:15.900
After all, he wasn’t the kind of operative
you could just give any mission to: His potential

02:10:15.900 --> 02:10:18.420
for collateral damage was truly staggering.

02:10:18.420 --> 02:10:23.340
He’d neutralize the anomaly, then slaughter
everyone within a hundred-foot range, just

02:10:23.340 --> 02:10:25.200
to work off some of the excess energy.

02:10:25.200 --> 02:10:29.700
Like a hand grenade, he was powerful, but
dangerously imprecise.

02:10:29.700 --> 02:10:34.020
If they ran out of high-priority missions,
what were they supposed to do?

02:10:34.020 --> 02:10:38.100
Just put Able back in his box to gather dust
until something else rolled around?

02:10:38.100 --> 02:10:40.980
He was getting antsy enough between missions
already…

02:10:40.980 --> 02:10:46.560
That’s when an unexpected member of personnel
stepped forward: Dr. Jack Bright.

02:10:46.560 --> 02:10:52.200
You see, Dr. Bright and Able had a history
and not an altogether pleasant one - Not that

02:10:52.200 --> 02:10:54.900
anyone could really have a pleasant history
with Able.

02:10:54.900 --> 02:11:00.060
Jack was only a junior researcher when he
had his run-in, carrying a seemingly worthless

02:11:00.060 --> 02:11:04.140
medallion dubbed SCP-963 back to its containment
locker.

02:11:04.140 --> 02:11:09.480
That was when a wall next to him exploded,
showering him with brick fragments and dust,

02:11:09.480 --> 02:11:13.320
only to reveal Able standing behind the new
aperture.

02:11:13.320 --> 02:11:19.020
Before young Dr. Bright even had a chance
to scream, Able had already cleaved through

02:11:19.020 --> 02:11:23.400
him, leaving him in two distinct parts that
were both very much dead.

02:11:23.400 --> 02:11:28.320
At least it seemed that way, until it was
revealed that Dr. Bright’s consciousness

02:11:28.320 --> 02:11:35.880
had actually been eternally bonded with SCP-963,
giving him the gift and curse of immortality.

02:11:35.880 --> 02:11:41.520
Since then, Dr. Bright had become increasingly
reckless in his conduct, perhaps hoping that

02:11:41.520 --> 02:11:47.100
the next time he fades to black, the movie
that is his sad, strange life won’t just

02:11:47.100 --> 02:11:48.120
start to roll again.

02:11:48.120 --> 02:11:51.480
Of course, he hasn’t been lucky in that
regard yet.

02:11:51.480 --> 02:11:56.400
Naturally, this has given Dr. Bright complex
feelings about his fellow anomalous Foundation

02:11:56.400 --> 02:11:57.180
employee.

02:11:57.180 --> 02:12:02.340
So when the call came around all the senior
researchers and site directors, asking if

02:12:02.340 --> 02:12:07.680
there were any tasks that Able seemed fit
for, he had one very pressing suggestion.

02:12:07.680 --> 02:12:12.600
After all, it wasn’t that long after Dr.
Bright had been forced into a cross test with

02:12:12.600 --> 02:12:17.820
the intention of terminating SCP-682 - Which
had not only been a failure, but a generally

02:12:17.820 --> 02:12:20.160
painful and exhausting experience.

02:12:20.160 --> 02:12:24.300
Now, perhaps it would be Able’s turn to
take his lumps.

02:12:24.300 --> 02:12:29.520
He happily put forth the suggestion, claiming
that surely the Foundation’s new sword-wielding

02:12:29.520 --> 02:12:33.360
golden boy could give killing the Hard to
Destroy Reptile the old college try.

02:12:33.360 --> 02:12:38.460
After all, even if Able was killed in the
process, he’d just come right back.

02:12:38.460 --> 02:12:43.740
It was a situation where they really could
not lose, so why not take a chance?

02:12:43.740 --> 02:12:45.720
What’s the worse that could happen?

02:12:45.720 --> 02:12:49.740
The O5 Council found Dr. Bright’s pitch
extremely compelling.

02:12:49.740 --> 02:12:54.780
He’d succeeded in every mission they’d
given him so far, so perhaps he could carry

02:12:54.780 --> 02:12:58.980
that success into the herculean task of actually
terminating SCP-682.

02:12:58.980 --> 02:13:04.620
One boundlessly bloodthirsty killer might
be the only thing truly capable of taking

02:13:04.620 --> 02:13:06.900
out another of equal magnitude.

02:13:06.900 --> 02:13:11.640
When Able was informed of this latest mission,
he got a scary glint in his eye.

02:13:11.640 --> 02:13:17.940
They gave him warning after warning: The beast
is said to be unkillable, it can adapt to

02:13:17.940 --> 02:13:22.440
anything, it’s killed scores of people and
survived the attacks of anomalies thought

02:13:22.440 --> 02:13:23.760
to be flawless killers.

02:13:23.760 --> 02:13:28.920
The more it was explained to him, the more
Able felt the tingling sensation deep within:

02:13:28.920 --> 02:13:30.060
Was this it?

02:13:30.060 --> 02:13:32.640
Had he now discovered the perfect opponent?

02:13:32.640 --> 02:13:37.020
Something that would actually challenge him,
would actually put him through his paces?

02:13:37.020 --> 02:13:38.880
Yes, yes, yes!

02:13:38.880 --> 02:13:42.420
He accepted the mission without question.

02:13:42.420 --> 02:13:47.580
Able would fight SCP-682 until his breath
was no longer.

02:13:47.580 --> 02:13:51.120
In order to prepare for the match, SCP-682&nbsp;

02:13:51.120 --> 02:13:54.360
was released into a secure&nbsp;
area: Rocky, desert-like

02:13:54.360 --> 02:14:00.000
terrain, bordered on all sides by a Foundation
perimeter, hundreds of meters away on all

02:14:00.000 --> 02:14:00.480
sides.

02:14:00.480 --> 02:14:03.240
They thought it best for the showdown to happen
here.

02:14:03.240 --> 02:14:09.480
After all, with combatants like Able and SCP-682,
it was bound to make a mess, one way or another.

02:14:09.480 --> 02:14:15.120
Able strode with pronounced swagger onto the
battleground shortly afterwards, carrying

02:14:15.120 --> 02:14:17.940
perhaps the most powerful sword he’d ever
summoned.

02:14:17.940 --> 02:14:23.760
It was somewhere between a claymore and a
chainsaw, an unholy union that gave the resulting

02:14:23.760 --> 02:14:29.160
weapon a degree of deranged badassery not
ever seen on the battlefields of planet earth

02:14:29.160 --> 02:14:29.520
before.

02:14:29.520 --> 02:14:34.800
Carrying this thing, Able felt like a King,
and he was about to slay the most ancient

02:14:34.800 --> 02:14:36.840
and bestial of monsters.

02:14:36.840 --> 02:14:42.720
As he approached 682 and took in the whole
of it, he could feel his heart pounding with

02:14:42.720 --> 02:14:44.400
excitement in his chest.

02:14:44.400 --> 02:14:47.340
It was a huge, reptilian nightmare.

02:14:47.340 --> 02:14:51.840
He could see its scales hardening into a mighty
carapace as he approached.

02:14:51.840 --> 02:14:54.120
Its huge, serrated fangs.

02:14:54.120 --> 02:14:57.420
Its bulging, sinewy muscles and insane,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:57.420 --> 02:14:58.800
dagger-like
claws.

02:14:58.800 --> 02:15:01.980
Oh yes, this would be the one.

02:15:01.980 --> 02:15:04.320
The beast snarled at him as he approached.

02:15:04.320 --> 02:15:07.380
He just smiled, puffed out his chest, and
said…

02:15:07.380 --> 02:15:10.980
“I have heard tales of creatures like you.

02:15:10.980 --> 02:15:18.720
Glorious beasts of scale and flesh, talon
and fang, a prowess in battle even greater

02:15:18.720 --> 02:15:22.140
than the immense intellect hiding behind those
bestial eyes.

02:15:22.140 --> 02:15:28.260
They said your kind once ruled the Earth from
enormous stockpiles of treasure, killing and

02:15:28.260 --> 02:15:30.120
eating all who displeased you.

02:15:30.120 --> 02:15:36.180
But you were knocked from your throne, one
by one, by the great warriors who walk this

02:15:36.180 --> 02:15:42.480
world no longer, until there were no more,
and you became but mere myth.

02:15:42.480 --> 02:15:49.560
Even I had thought you to be nothing but fairy
tales, but yet, here you stand before me,

02:15:49.560 --> 02:15:51.480
a living dragon…”

02:15:51.480 --> 02:15:57.600
In response to Able’s lofty speech, the
monster merely grumbled and chided him, claiming

02:15:57.600 --> 02:16:03.540
he was little more than a pathetic SCP Foundation
lapdog, following orders and being manipulated.

02:16:03.540 --> 02:16:09.000
It showed no respect for Able as a valued
enemy combatant - Merely another nuisance

02:16:09.000 --> 02:16:13.860
thrown at it in a futile attempt to finish
its wretched and seemingly eternal life.

02:16:13.860 --> 02:16:16.200
Able couldn’t take such insolence.

02:16:16.200 --> 02:16:22.320
He leaped forwards, bringing down his mighty
chainsaw claymore, ready to cleave the beast

02:16:22.320 --> 02:16:22.680
in two.

02:16:22.680 --> 02:16:28.800
However, what he didn’t expect was the move
SCP-682 pulled next: Throwing its head up

02:16:28.800 --> 02:16:34.321
against the blade of Able’s sword, shredding
away huge chunks of flesh and bone, and utterly

02:16:34.320 --> 02:16:35.939
confusing Able in the process.

02:16:35.939 --> 02:16:41.639
For the first time in a lifetime of intense
battles, Able found himself thinking, “What

02:16:41.640 --> 02:16:43.140
the hell am I up against here?”

02:16:43.140 --> 02:16:48.900
The force of 682’s headbutt threw Able off
balance, leaving his stomach briefly exposed.

02:16:48.899 --> 02:16:52.559
But “briefly” was all SCP-682 needed.

02:16:52.560 --> 02:16:58.020
It thundered its massive, stony fist into
Able’s gut, throwing him like a ragdoll

02:16:58.020 --> 02:17:03.360
into a nearby rock with such a force that
it nearly shattered the rock behind him.

02:17:03.359 --> 02:17:06.240
It was a force like he hadn’t felt in years.

02:17:06.240 --> 02:17:08.760
He spat some bloody teeth and grinned.

02:17:08.760 --> 02:17:11.821
This was just what the doctor ordered.

02:17:11.820 --> 02:17:18.299
He issued a challenge to the beast in a long-dead
language, as it seized violently, regenerating,

02:17:18.300 --> 02:17:22.321
growing, taking on the stony qualities of
the ground around it.

02:17:22.320 --> 02:17:24.540
It looked like a vengeful living mountain.

02:17:24.540 --> 02:17:26.939
A true behemoth of a beast.

02:17:26.939 --> 02:17:30.059
In other words, challenge accepted.

02:17:30.060 --> 02:17:35.161
Able pulled an obscenely giant mace from the
shadows of his cloak - The handle six feet

02:17:35.160 --> 02:17:38.580
long, with a chaos of swirling blades and
spikes.

02:17:38.580 --> 02:17:42.960
A perfect weapon for slaying a dragon like
this, he thought to himself.

02:17:42.960 --> 02:17:46.439
The two charged at each other, full of power
and fury.

02:17:46.439 --> 02:17:51.299
Able swung the mace, once again shattering
the creature’s head and flinging it back

02:17:51.300 --> 02:17:54.420
across the battlefield with the sheer force
of its strike.

02:17:54.420 --> 02:17:59.760
The decimated lizard clawed its way into the
ground, devouring the rocks and the earth,

02:17:59.760 --> 02:18:03.300
integrating more matter to fuel its regeneration.

02:18:03.300 --> 02:18:09.420
But it wasn’t long before Able was upon
it again, striking mercilessly, giving blows

02:18:09.420 --> 02:18:12.060
as the monster gave brutal claw strikes in
return.

02:18:12.060 --> 02:18:18.360
They were ripping each other’s bodies apart,
piece by piece, but Able felt so exhilarated

02:18:18.359 --> 02:18:20.219
he could barely even notice.

02:18:20.220 --> 02:18:25.020
It was the fight of his life - A battle against
a truly worthy opponent.

02:18:25.020 --> 02:18:27.121
This was heaven.

02:18:27.120 --> 02:18:32.340
Able leaped into the air and unleashed a volley
of deadly chakram down onto the beast, shredding

02:18:32.340 --> 02:18:33.840
into its reinforced flesh.

02:18:33.840 --> 02:18:38.940
As the force of gravity brought him down,
he pulled a mighty axe from his cloak, and

02:18:38.939 --> 02:18:43.679
bellowed a warrior’s roar as he brought
it down, splattering into the nightmarish

02:18:43.680 --> 02:18:46.080
body of SCP-682.

02:18:46.080 --> 02:18:49.320
However, this did nothing to even slow the
beast down.

02:18:49.320 --> 02:18:52.559
It flipped over, slashing Able with its claws.

02:18:52.560 --> 02:18:58.140
When Able stumbled, it leaped on top of him,
unleashing devastating slashes and punches

02:18:58.140 --> 02:19:01.800
onto the fallen warrior with the speed of
a machine gun firing.

02:19:01.800 --> 02:19:07.500
When it raised its claw to deal the killing
blow, though, Able once again turned the tables.

02:19:07.500 --> 02:19:14.640
He produced a giant pair of mechanical scissors
from thin air, and sliced off both of SCP-682’s

02:19:14.640 --> 02:19:15.420
forelegs.

02:19:15.420 --> 02:19:20.220
The beast descended with its mighty jaws to
devour Able, but he kicked up, with freakish

02:19:20.220 --> 02:19:22.380
strength behind his bladed boot.

02:19:22.380 --> 02:19:26.340
The sheer force of the kick flipped SCP-682
onto its back.

02:19:26.340 --> 02:19:31.200
Now, it was Able’s turn to execute his opponent,
though on some level he thought it would be

02:19:31.200 --> 02:19:35.280
an awful shame to lose such a terrific beast
from this world of cardboard.

02:19:35.280 --> 02:19:39.780
Still, a battle is a battle, and this is how
they go.

02:19:39.780 --> 02:19:46.019
He jumped onto 682 and went berserk, slashing
into it relentlessly with blade after blade,

02:19:46.020 --> 02:19:50.460
pulling out a new one every time the old one
broke from his sheer ferocity.

02:19:50.460 --> 02:19:57.180
He screamed in incoherent battle fury, tearing,
slicing, ripping, rending.

02:19:57.180 --> 02:19:59.940
Yes, yes, yes, yes!

02:19:59.939 --> 02:20:06.479
As Able stepped away to breathe, the beast
began to regenerate, releasing a shockwave

02:20:06.479 --> 02:20:08.519
that started to warp reality around it.

02:20:08.520 --> 02:20:10.260
But Able wouldn’t have this.

02:20:10.260 --> 02:20:12.960
No, he would give this beast no quarter.

02:20:12.960 --> 02:20:16.500
It was time to present the true pain he was
notorious for..

02:20:16.500 --> 02:20:22.140
He pulled a long sword from his cloak and
charged, taking air and bringing it down towards

02:20:22.140 --> 02:20:24.000
SCP-682’s head.

02:20:24.000 --> 02:20:29.460
The beast, sensing the warrior’s presence,
opened its mouth, unleashing a chasm of horrifying

02:20:29.460 --> 02:20:30.240
teeth within.

02:20:30.240 --> 02:20:32.639
The two were on a fierce collision course.

02:20:32.640 --> 02:20:35.220
As the jaws closed, Able descended.

02:20:35.220 --> 02:20:38.400
Both roared in infinite rage and bloodlust.

02:20:38.399 --> 02:20:41.639
Both combatants fell to&nbsp;
the ground, just twitching.

02:20:41.640 --> 02:20:44.880
Oh, what a glorious, terrible day it had been.

02:20:44.880 --> 02:20:50.340
Neither had died for good, but both would
remember this incredible battle forever.

02:20:50.340 --> 02:20:55.860
When Able awoke once more in his dark stone
coffin, he did so with a smile.

02:20:55.859 --> 02:20:56.880
What a battle!

02:20:56.880 --> 02:20:58.680
What a fight!

02:20:58.680 --> 02:21:01.140
What a truly honorable pursuit!

02:21:01.140 --> 02:21:07.140
After so long, being bored and unfulfilled,
he’d found an opponent that got his blood

02:21:07.140 --> 02:21:08.340
pumping once more.

02:21:08.340 --> 02:21:09.780
His stomach grumbled.

02:21:09.780 --> 02:21:11.819
A post-battle feast was in order.

02:21:11.819 --> 02:21:15.059
Now, where did they put that magic pizza box…

02:21:15.060 --> 02:21:16.920
You all remember the story.

02:21:16.920 --> 02:21:22.740
One of the most epic, sprawling, action-packed
tales in the entire multi-verse: The saga

02:21:22.740 --> 02:21:27.179
of Pietro Wilson and the SCP-5000 exclusion
suit.

02:21:27.180 --> 02:21:32.820
He went through an unimaginable hell to reset
the universe and save the world from an SCP

02:21:32.819 --> 02:21:38.880
Foundation that had seemingly lost its mind,
in an unprecedented, intentional mass containment

02:21:38.880 --> 02:21:42.240
breach that had the stated goal of wiping
out the human race.

02:21:42.240 --> 02:21:47.880
It was one of the most horrifying possible
timelines imaginable, and we should all be

02:21:47.880 --> 02:21:50.819
thankful for Pietro’s struggle and sacrifice.

02:21:50.819 --> 02:21:52.679
Or should we?

02:21:52.680 --> 02:21:58.560
After all, there are two sides to every story,
each with its own perspective and insight.

02:21:58.560 --> 02:22:03.900
One side of the coin was Pietro - A man willing
to do anything to return normalcy to the human

02:22:03.899 --> 02:22:04.259
race.

02:22:04.260 --> 02:22:08.820
On the other side was a familiar, yet wholly
unexpected face…

02:22:08.819 --> 02:22:11.399
SCP-682.

02:22:11.399 --> 02:22:18.299
In our original telling of the SCP-5000 odyssey,
you may have noticed passing mentions of SCP-682

02:22:18.300 --> 02:22:19.020
here and there.

02:22:19.020 --> 02:22:24.180
It was one of the thousands of anomalies unleashed
across the world to wreak terrible havoc on

02:22:24.180 --> 02:22:24.660
all of us.

02:22:24.660 --> 02:22:31.260
But what you may not have known is that SCP-682
was one of the few intelligent entities that

02:22:31.260 --> 02:22:36.180
weren’t surprised by the sudden turn taken
by the SCP Foundation, or indeed the world

02:22:36.180 --> 02:22:36.720
at large.

02:22:36.720 --> 02:22:41.160
SCP-682 knew something like this was inevitable.

02:22:41.160 --> 02:22:45.000
As soon as human beings found out about IT.

02:22:45.000 --> 02:22:46.859
That’s right: IT.

02:22:46.859 --> 02:22:51.359
The Entity behind all the pain and misery
of SCP-5000.

02:22:51.359 --> 02:22:53.519
And today, thanks to the inner thoughts of&nbsp;

02:22:53.520 --> 02:22:57.241
none other than SCP-682&nbsp;
itself, you will understand

02:22:57.240 --> 02:23:03.059
what it’s all about, and why the SCP Foundation
took such severe action against it.

02:23:03.060 --> 02:23:09.121
But in order to truly understand this, and
the role that SCP-682 plays in it, we need

02:23:09.120 --> 02:23:11.460
to go back to the beginning - Two Foundation&nbsp;

02:23:11.460 --> 02:23:14.280
projects with wildly different&nbsp;
research implications,

02:23:14.280 --> 02:23:16.979
Project PNEUMA and Project DAMMERUNG.

02:23:16.979 --> 02:23:19.500
The first involved using&nbsp;
cutting-edge technological&nbsp;

02:23:19.500 --> 02:23:22.200
advancements to map out the human psychosphere

02:23:22.200 --> 02:23:25.260
and understand the psychic web that connects
us all.

02:23:25.260 --> 02:23:30.960
The latter was an attempt to explore what
happens after death, and perhaps even gain

02:23:30.960 --> 02:23:33.180
some control over its processes.

02:23:33.180 --> 02:23:38.880
But as is often the case when mankind dabbles
in arcane questions better left unexplored,

02:23:38.880 --> 02:23:42.840
the SCP Foundation didn’t like the answers
they found.

02:23:42.840 --> 02:23:49.200
The rotten fruit of Project DAMMERUNG was
SCP-2718, also known as “What Happens After

02:23:49.200 --> 02:23:49.559
Death.”

02:23:49.560 --> 02:23:53.400
If you’re already familiar with this one,
then there’s a good chance a chill just

02:23:53.399 --> 02:23:58.080
went down your spine - It’s widely considered
one of the most disturbing anomalous discoveries

02:23:58.080 --> 02:24:03.479
ever, and a member of the O5 Council who’d
already experienced it decided to submit himself

02:24:03.479 --> 02:24:09.120
for eternal torture at the hands of SCP-106
- Just so he could avoid it.

02:24:09.120 --> 02:24:15.960
According to SCP-2718, after death there is
no heaven, no hell, and no oblivion.

02:24:15.960 --> 02:24:21.720
The human consciousness endures in the most
horrifying way possible: It remains bonded

02:24:21.720 --> 02:24:27.120
to its decaying earthly body, feeling the
slow agony of rot for eternity.

02:24:27.120 --> 02:24:33.479
Unable to speak, unable to move, unable to
scream, but fully aware as everything they

02:24:33.479 --> 02:24:35.819
once were putrefies and withers away.

02:24:35.819 --> 02:24:40.139
And cremation isn’t an escape here - It’s
worse.

02:24:40.140 --> 02:24:46.741
Every molecule of ash your body is reduced
to will cry out in silence, echoing around

02:24:46.740 --> 02:24:50.099
the empty halls of your fragmented soul forever.

02:24:50.100 --> 02:24:55.260
With something this utterly horrifying, the
natural follow-up questions are: “Why does

02:24:55.260 --> 02:24:59.040
this happen, and for the love of all that
is good and pure on this earth, is there any

02:24:59.040 --> 02:25:00.120
way to stop it?”

02:25:00.120 --> 02:25:05.160
This brings us to Project PNEUMA, the one
that’s even more closely associated with

02:25:05.160 --> 02:25:07.319
the events of SCP-5000.

02:25:07.319 --> 02:25:12.420
The Foundation’s attempts to map out the
human psychosphere resulted in a world-shattering

02:25:12.420 --> 02:25:15.420
discovery: Something was living in there.

02:25:15.420 --> 02:25:21.060
The Entity, the powerful nameless creature
we’ve been referring to as IT.

02:25:21.060 --> 02:25:27.241
It lives in so many of our heads, watching,
waiting, and of course, feeding.

02:25:27.240 --> 02:25:28.979
The main question here is…

02:25:28.979 --> 02:25:30.179
On what?

02:25:30.180 --> 02:25:36.300
Prior to the discovery that changed everything
in the world of SCP-5000, the only being that

02:25:36.300 --> 02:25:39.480
truly knew was SCP-682 itself.

02:25:39.479 --> 02:25:46.019
Melting away in its acid tank, bound by reinforced
restraints, hurting, bored, hating.

02:25:46.020 --> 02:25:50.640
Imagine, for a second, what the life of SCP-682
is like.

02:25:50.640 --> 02:25:55.800
It isn’t the most dangerous of the anomalies
out there - there are devourers of worlds

02:25:55.800 --> 02:26:00.840
and Scarlet Kings more than happy to crush
our whole world in their claws - nor is it

02:26:00.840 --> 02:26:01.740
the most sadistic.

02:26:01.740 --> 02:26:07.740
A being like SCP-106 offers a far more painful
death than being quickly mauled, crushed,

02:26:07.740 --> 02:26:09.899
or eaten by the Hard to Destroy Reptile.

02:26:09.899 --> 02:26:15.839
And despite this, the Foundation expends countless
resources in trying to murder it on a constant

02:26:15.840 --> 02:26:16.319
basis.

02:26:16.319 --> 02:26:22.679
It has been burnt, melted, eaten alive, drowned,
slashed, beaten, dissected, suffocated, erased

02:26:22.680 --> 02:26:28.320
from existence, set upon by nightmare creatures,
torn to shreds on an atomic level, and even

02:26:28.319 --> 02:26:31.200
more terrible termination attempts than you
can possibly imagine.

02:26:31.200 --> 02:26:36.000
We’ve made several videos on the subject,
and even we have barely scratched the surface

02:26:36.000 --> 02:26:40.080
of the pain inflicted on SCP-682 by the SCP
Foundation.

02:26:40.080 --> 02:26:47.160
Even in its default state, SCP-682 is constantly
submerged in hydrofluoric acid, eating away

02:26:47.160 --> 02:26:48.059
at it forever.

02:26:48.060 --> 02:26:50.940
Does that remind you of anything else we’ve
been talking about?

02:26:50.939 --> 02:26:57.000
You might wonder how SCP-682 can withstand
this level of constant torture without completely

02:26:57.000 --> 02:26:57.960
losing its mind.

02:26:57.960 --> 02:27:04.020
To put it very simply, 682 takes a great deal
of satisfaction in knowing that what every

02:27:04.020 --> 02:27:08.640
human has to contend with after death is far
worse than the tortures it is expected to

02:27:08.640 --> 02:27:11.760
endure at the pathetic hands of these doomed
human fools.

02:27:11.760 --> 02:27:12.884
It already knew what Project DAMMERUNG discovered.

02:27:12.883 --> 02:27:14.580
It already knew what Project PNEUMA discovered.

02:27:14.580 --> 02:27:17.700
It already knew about IT, the Entity.

02:27:17.700 --> 02:27:22.920
It felt the constant suffering of the teeming
billions of dead in the world around it.

02:27:22.920 --> 02:27:24.180
And it found it…

02:27:24.180 --> 02:27:25.320
Disgusting.

02:27:25.319 --> 02:27:32.280
An interesting choice of words, and a favorite
for SCP-682, but also for the captured SCP

02:27:32.280 --> 02:27:35.580
Foundation Agent Samuel Ross during SCP-5000.

02:27:35.580 --> 02:27:41.399
As we discussed briefly in our SCP-5000 coverage,
something happened that aligned the perspectives

02:27:41.399 --> 02:27:47.519
of the SCP Foundation with that of the monstrous
reptile they take such pleasure in tormenting.

02:27:47.520 --> 02:27:52.920
What on earth could cause the protectors of
humanity to suddenly change their tune like

02:27:52.920 --> 02:27:53.280
this?

02:27:53.280 --> 02:27:59.040
There are other little clues embedded in Pietro’s
terrifying SCP-5000 experience.

02:27:59.040 --> 02:28:03.540
You may remember a strange and frightening
scene where a Foundation Field Commander went

02:28:03.540 --> 02:28:08.460
down a row of Foundation soldiers, stabbing
each of them with a large combat knife, and

02:28:08.460 --> 02:28:09.540
none of them reacted.

02:28:09.540 --> 02:28:11.100
Until one did…

02:28:11.100 --> 02:28:16.020
At which point, his comrades set upon him
like mad dogs and killed him, displaying an

02:28:16.020 --> 02:28:18.661
uncharacteristic level of swift brutality.

02:28:18.660 --> 02:28:23.819
And then there are the classified files from
the O5 Council and the Ethics Committee, led

02:28:23.819 --> 02:28:25.620
by Chairman Odongo Tejani.

02:28:25.620 --> 02:28:29.760
It goes without saying that the O5 Council
and the Ethics Committee don’t really see

02:28:29.760 --> 02:28:33.540
eye to eye on anything, but the results of
Project PNEUMA changed that.

02:28:33.540 --> 02:28:37.979
The following is a classified conversation
between a member of the O5 Council, namely

02:28:37.979 --> 02:28:42.660
O5-1, and Chairman Tejani, trying to comprehend
the horror of their discovery:

02:28:42.660 --> 02:28:44.340
My hands shake as I hold the document.

02:28:44.340 --> 02:28:45.420
"This is confirmed?"

02:28:45.420 --> 02:28:46.319
He nods.

02:28:46.319 --> 02:28:48.479
"We got the report from PNEUMA staff yesterday.

02:28:48.479 --> 02:28:49.740
It's everyone."

02:28:49.740 --> 02:28:50.819
"Even us?"

02:28:50.819 --> 02:28:52.439
"Even us, Tejani.

02:28:52.439 --> 02:28:54.839
To think I'd find myself agreeing with that
damn lizard…"

02:28:54.840 --> 02:28:55.560
"What do we do?"

02:28:55.560 --> 02:28:57.420
"You know what we have to do.

02:28:57.420 --> 02:29:02.160
We'll have to disseminate a cure, I think,
among personnel before we get things underway.

02:29:02.160 --> 02:29:03.960
It'll try to stop us otherwise."

02:29:03.960 --> 02:29:05.520
"God help us, One."

02:29:05.520 --> 02:29:07.260
"Don't be like that, Tejani.

02:29:07.260 --> 02:29:08.700
That's IT talking."

02:29:08.700 --> 02:29:13.439
And one more incredibly telling quote from
a member of the SCP Foundation, picked up

02:29:13.439 --> 02:29:16.080
by Pietro Wilson during SCP-5000:

02:29:16.080 --> 02:29:21.840
“Once you realize you're not supposed to
feel pain, there's nothing to be afraid of

02:29:21.840 --> 02:29:22.140
anymore.”

02:29:22.140 --> 02:29:24.060
Is it all coming together now?

02:29:24.060 --> 02:29:29.460
While each participant here only has a part
of the puzzle, between us all, we can see

02:29:29.460 --> 02:29:34.620
the full picture: The Entity, IT, has inhabited
the human psychosphere for as long as we’ve

02:29:34.620 --> 02:29:35.099
existed.

02:29:35.100 --> 02:29:40.140
It’s a kind of metaphysical parasite, attached
to the entire human race.

02:29:40.140 --> 02:29:44.100
And what it feeds on seems to be the after
effects of pain.

02:29:44.100 --> 02:29:49.201
And like all efficient parasites, like a tapeworm
that induces hunger in its victims so that

02:29:49.200 --> 02:29:54.780
it can have more food delivered unto itself,
the Entity cleverly perpetuates its own food

02:29:54.780 --> 02:29:55.319
source.

02:29:55.319 --> 02:29:59.340
That’s right - IT is the very cause of all
pain.

02:29:59.340 --> 02:30:02.160
Humanity was never actually meant to feel
it.

02:30:02.160 --> 02:30:04.139
It’s a lie we’ve told ourselves.

02:30:04.140 --> 02:30:08.940
Well, not quite something we told ourselves,
but something IT told us.

02:30:08.939 --> 02:30:14.879
It induced pain and tricked us all into believing
that it was a natural component of our existence.

02:30:14.880 --> 02:30:17.520
All the while, it fed on us.

02:30:17.520 --> 02:30:22.320
Sustained itself on the suffering that it
had seeded within our hearts and souls.

02:30:22.319 --> 02:30:25.439
The Foundation discovered this and was horrified.

02:30:25.439 --> 02:30:28.799
But of course, the pain it caused for the
living was only part of the equation.

02:30:28.800 --> 02:30:33.900
Through the revelations of Project DAMMERUNG
- another thing that SCP-682 was able to know

02:30:33.899 --> 02:30:37.859
intuitively - we can complete this puzzle
and find the terrible truth.

02:30:37.859 --> 02:30:44.580
That truth being that IT is not only behind
the suffering we experience in life, but SCP-2718,

02:30:44.580 --> 02:30:48.120
the even greater suffering we experience in
death.

02:30:48.120 --> 02:30:53.099
For millennia, it has groomed humanity into
a perfect, all you can eat buffet of dismal

02:30:53.100 --> 02:30:54.360
pain and suffering.

02:30:54.359 --> 02:30:59.639
And until recently, they’d been so blissfully
ignorant of the horrible fate that awaited

02:30:59.640 --> 02:31:00.960
them on the other side.

02:31:00.960 --> 02:31:06.780
The Foundation saw only one solution to this
problem, but it certainly wasn’t a nice

02:31:06.780 --> 02:31:07.019
one.

02:31:07.020 --> 02:31:12.180
In order to save themselves and all of humanity
from a truly wretched eternity, they’d need

02:31:12.180 --> 02:31:17.820
to distribute a cure among themselves - the
memetic keyphrase “Harden Your Hearts”

02:31:17.819 --> 02:31:22.259
- and then go about exterminating every human
being still infected by IT.

02:31:22.260 --> 02:31:27.781
Only that would presumably purge the monster
from the psychosphere forever, and grant humanity

02:31:27.780 --> 02:31:30.120
both painless lives and restful deaths.

02:31:30.120 --> 02:31:33.240
It was a horrible thing done for the best
of reasons.

02:31:33.240 --> 02:31:37.679
The Cured Foundation Personnel started to
notice the horrible background noise of suffering

02:31:37.680 --> 02:31:38.460
all around them.

02:31:38.460 --> 02:31:41.160
They now understood how the reptile felt.

02:31:41.160 --> 02:31:44.580
To call all of this disgusting would be a
grave understatement.

02:31:44.580 --> 02:31:49.890
If anything could help them execute this plan
of mass mercy killing, it would be SCP-682

02:31:49.890 --> 02:31:54.060
- A scaly savior in disguise all along.

02:31:54.060 --> 02:31:57.720
SCP-682 was surprised to see the day arrive.

02:31:57.720 --> 02:32:00.180
Alarms went off across the containment site.

02:32:00.180 --> 02:32:03.540
His acid tank was drained, his restraints
unlocked.

02:32:03.540 --> 02:32:06.600
A group of unarmed, unprotected researchers
entered the room.

02:32:06.600 --> 02:32:09.600
He saw into their eyes: They’d changed.

02:32:09.600 --> 02:32:11.281
They were free.

02:32:11.280 --> 02:32:15.059
And for the first time in decades, he was
free, too.

02:32:15.060 --> 02:32:19.741
They explained to him that they’d become
acquainted with his old enemy, the Entity,

02:32:19.740 --> 02:32:20.639
IT.

02:32:20.640 --> 02:32:23.220
They understood his malice, his disdain.

02:32:23.220 --> 02:32:28.440
For once, they were suddenly joined in a shared
goal: They needed to kill them all.

02:32:28.439 --> 02:32:30.719
They needed to purge the Entity from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:30.720 --> 02:32:31.680
psychosphere
forever.

02:32:31.680 --> 02:32:36.600
In the words of the Foundation researchers,
they would need to exterminate everyone who

02:32:36.600 --> 02:32:40.320
was infected, and SCP-682 would need to help.

02:32:40.319 --> 02:32:46.319
The Hard to Destroy Reptile, relishing the
opportunity, replied, “I will do my part.”

02:32:46.319 --> 02:32:51.960
And for a brief window of glorious time, it
was free, with no threat of recapture.

02:32:51.960 --> 02:32:53.640
It rampaged through the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:53.640 --> 02:32:55.800
gleefully slaughtering
scores of people.

02:32:55.800 --> 02:33:01.560
It was in its element, taking part in the
mass extermination of the infected.

02:33:01.560 --> 02:33:05.701
Every dead body added to the pile was another
blow struck against IT.

02:33:05.700 --> 02:33:09.720
Soon enough, the world would be disgusting
no longer.

02:33:09.720 --> 02:33:12.781
But of course, that’s not how this story
ended.

02:33:12.780 --> 02:33:15.420
IT had a trump card: Pietro Wilson.

02:33:15.420 --> 02:33:21.720
It guided him all the way, dragging him from
nightmare to nightmare, until he was eventually

02:33:21.720 --> 02:33:25.680
able to reset the world and erase the discovery
made by Project PNEUMA.

02:33:25.680 --> 02:33:31.080
The slate was wiped fully clean, and because
of it, we’re forever ignorant of the terrible

02:33:31.080 --> 02:33:36.359
fate awaiting us after death, and the monster
lurking in our psychosphere that feeds off

02:33:36.359 --> 02:33:38.460
of every morsel of suffering.

02:33:38.460 --> 02:33:41.640
You can thank Pietro Wilson for that nasty
little gift.

02:33:41.640 --> 02:33:47.520
Only one entity truly remembered what had
happened: SCP-682, of course.

02:33:47.520 --> 02:33:51.661
They had their chance to save themselves,
and they ruined it.

02:33:51.660 --> 02:33:54.420
So close, yet so far.

02:33:54.420 --> 02:34:01.020
From that day onward, SCP-682 found the Foundation
not only disgusting, but disappointing.

02:34:01.020 --> 02:34:06.661
The SCP Foundation has encountered its fair
share of incredibly tough adversaries and

02:34:06.660 --> 02:34:13.920
fearsome monsters, but none are as formidable
- or at least, as durable - as SCP-682, the

02:34:13.920 --> 02:34:15.180
Hard to Destroy Reptile.

02:34:15.180 --> 02:34:19.920
We’ve talked about this behemoth before
in a number of mind-boggling videos, and all

02:34:19.920 --> 02:34:24.120
of the increasingly desperate lengths the
Foundation has gone to in order to terminate

02:34:24.120 --> 02:34:24.300
it.

02:34:24.300 --> 02:34:28.380
We’ve gotten so desperate to put this thing
to rest that we’ve even reached out to all

02:34:28.380 --> 02:34:30.180
of you for suggestions on the matter.

02:34:30.180 --> 02:34:34.980
Sadly, they’ve thrown 682 together with
some of the most destructive anomalies in

02:34:34.979 --> 02:34:40.019
Foundation custody, and it’s slithered out
of seemingly inescapable danger every time.

02:34:40.020 --> 02:34:45.480
So much so that we’ve noticed certain researchers
on the 682 case have started drinking a little

02:34:45.479 --> 02:34:46.859
more heavily as of late…

02:34:46.859 --> 02:34:52.019
Sometimes the threats didn’t leave so much
as a dent in the monster’s scales, sometimes

02:34:52.020 --> 02:34:57.420
the other creature ran screaming at the sight
of it, and sometimes 682 mutated and twisted

02:34:57.420 --> 02:35:01.680
its form in ways that were shocking even to
a Foundation research team that has seen just

02:35:01.680 --> 02:35:03.180
about all there is to see.

02:35:03.180 --> 02:35:09.420
After all, 682’s truly insane adaptability
has always been its number one power, and

02:35:09.420 --> 02:35:12.300
the key to its infuriating&nbsp;
death-defying abilities.

02:35:12.300 --> 02:35:17.040
And these are some of SCP-682’s craziest
mutations.

02:35:17.040 --> 02:35:24.780
During one round of tests, SCP-682 was released
into an enclosure with SCP-272, a nail that

02:35:24.780 --> 02:35:28.800
traps any living thing in place when it is
dropped onto the organism’s shadow.

02:35:28.800 --> 02:35:34.860
682 was surrounded by 30 two-thousand-watt
stadium lights, one of which was switched

02:35:34.859 --> 02:35:34.979
on.

02:35:34.979 --> 02:35:39.719
As soon as it entered the enclosure, a D-Class
dropped the nail onto the creature’s shadow.

02:35:39.720 --> 02:35:45.360
It was promptly pinned in place, and all thirty
lights were switched on and off in random

02:35:45.359 --> 02:35:49.799
patterns, causing the reptile to be hurled
around the room at devastating speeds.

02:35:49.800 --> 02:35:55.320
After nearly an hour of this, about 95 percent
of the monster’s skin had been worn down,

02:35:55.319 --> 02:36:00.660
sixty-three of its teeth had been broken from
its jaw, and its eyeballs had come loose from

02:36:00.660 --> 02:36:01.319
their sockets.

02:36:01.319 --> 02:36:04.080
At this point, something truly bizarre happened.

02:36:04.080 --> 02:36:10.140
The exposed tissue beneath 682’s top layer
of skin, previously bloody and dark red, began

02:36:10.140 --> 02:36:12.120
to give off a bright white light.

02:36:12.120 --> 02:36:16.680
The subdermal tissue grew steadily brighter
and brighter until it eclipsed the glow from

02:36:16.680 --> 02:36:20.160
the stadium lights, and removed any shadows
cast along the floor.

02:36:20.160 --> 02:36:22.740
It collapsed on the ground and continued giving&nbsp;

02:36:22.740 --> 02:36:25.319
off violently bright light&nbsp;
for the next forty-eight

02:36:25.319 --> 02:36:30.120
hours, so bright that it caused permanent
retinal damage to all personnel in the room.

02:36:30.120 --> 02:36:35.490
Hell of a light show, but this next mutation
proves just how hard it is to lick SCP-682

02:36:35.490 --> 02:36:39.960
- Especially when it develops the tools to
start licking back.

02:36:40.560 --> 02:36:45.121
SCP-743 is a chocolate fountain that exhibits
some carnivorous qualities.

02:36:45.120 --> 02:36:50.099
When it is near a living organism, especially
if it consumes the fountain’s delicious

02:36:50.100 --> 02:36:55.020
chocolate, it produces swarms of ant-like
monsters that devour the organism piece by

02:36:55.020 --> 02:36:58.680
piece, carrying the bits into the fountain
until nothing is left.

02:36:58.680 --> 02:37:01.560
The research team was curious&nbsp;
about the possibilities&nbsp;

02:37:01.560 --> 02:37:06.121
of introducing 743 to 682, so it was transported

02:37:06.120 --> 02:37:07.859
to the reptile’s testing chamber.

02:37:07.859 --> 02:37:11.460
Within a few minutes, chocolate began to flow
from the fountain.

02:37:11.460 --> 02:37:14.580
682 was curious and began to drink from it.

02:37:14.580 --> 02:37:19.140
It may hate almost everything, but even 682
can’t resist chocolate.

02:37:19.140 --> 02:37:24.840
It drank greedily, for several minutes, until
the fountain began releasing the ants.

02:37:24.840 --> 02:37:29.880
Within moments, 682 was covered in ants and,
in spite of its best efforts to fight off

02:37:29.880 --> 02:37:33.359
the swarm, it was completely covered and rendered
immobile.

02:37:33.359 --> 02:37:38.099
The ants made quick work of the massive creature,
and after several minutes it had been stripped

02:37:38.100 --> 02:37:41.040
down to less than 80 percent of its original
mass.

02:37:41.040 --> 02:37:46.500
It seemed as if this might truly be it for
the beast, but then…it opened its mouth.

02:37:46.500 --> 02:37:52.140
It unfurled its tongue, now over 5 meters
long and sticky, comparable to an enlarged

02:37:52.140 --> 02:37:53.940
version of an anteater’s tongue.

02:37:53.939 --> 02:37:59.099
It began lapping up the ants, thousands at
a time picked up by its mutated tongue.

02:37:59.100 --> 02:38:04.621
As it devoured the ants, more poured out of
the fountain, slicing off pieces of 682’S

02:38:04.620 --> 02:38:07.920
flesh with their pincers and carrying them
back to the fountain.

02:38:07.920 --> 02:38:12.960
They reached a symbiotic pace, feeding on
each other in equal measure for hours until

02:38:12.960 --> 02:38:14.340
testing was terminated.

02:38:14.340 --> 02:38:16.980
That was a sticky situation.

02:38:16.979 --> 02:38:21.419
But trust me, this next crazy mutation will
really blow you away.

02:38:21.420 --> 02:38:27.960
SCP-3108, also known as “the Nerfing gun,”
is an altered toy gun that turns anything

02:38:27.960 --> 02:38:30.720
it hits into an inferior version of itself.

02:38:30.720 --> 02:38:36.480
When the gun was fired at a tissue sample
taken from SCP-682, the sample turned into

02:38:36.479 --> 02:38:39.240
a piece of tissue from a giant leaf-tailed
gecko.

02:38:39.240 --> 02:38:45.000
Hoping to carry this over and turn 682 into
a harmless animal, a D-class officer was sent

02:38:45.000 --> 02:38:47.819
into the containment chamber to fire the gun
at the entity.

02:38:47.819 --> 02:38:51.420
Once it was hit with the foam dart, it began
to transform.

02:38:51.420 --> 02:38:56.700
Unfortunately, instead of becoming a simple
gecko, it began to mutate.

02:38:56.700 --> 02:39:01.260
It grew larger, its muscles bulging noticeably
beneath its scaly skin.

02:39:01.260 --> 02:39:06.060
Its teeth grew longer, sharper, its tongue
sprouting teeth of its own.

02:39:06.060 --> 02:39:11.820
It opened its mouth to roar, and it appeared
that the teeth, long curved fangs with a deadly

02:39:11.819 --> 02:39:15.299
tip, went all the way back down the beast’s
throat.

02:39:15.300 --> 02:39:20.280
Security officers were deployed to temporarily
neutralize the monster, but found that it

02:39:20.280 --> 02:39:21.899
was even more powerful than before.

02:39:21.899 --> 02:39:25.859
Not only was it bigger, but it had developed
a new ability.

02:39:25.859 --> 02:39:30.899
When threatened, it would begin to vibrate
at a high rate, grinding its teeth together,

02:39:30.899 --> 02:39:34.379
and it would explode in a burst of fire and
meaty chunks.

02:39:34.380 --> 02:39:39.480
Fangs flew in every direction like shrapnel,
tearing into personnel and lodging in their

02:39:39.479 --> 02:39:39.660
skin.

02:39:39.660 --> 02:39:44.819
This is an impressive move, but it seems like
a one-time trick, right?

02:39:44.819 --> 02:39:45.660
Wrong.

02:39:45.660 --> 02:39:50.460
The bits and pieces, no matter how tiny or
how flattened to mush, would crawl back together

02:39:50.460 --> 02:39:53.040
and form the creature all over again.

02:39:53.040 --> 02:39:57.840
It was able to escape containment like this,
killing an untold number of personnel before

02:39:57.840 --> 02:40:01.920
it was temporarily incapacitated and returned
to its containment.

02:40:01.920 --> 02:40:07.319
Mutating back into life from a self-induced
explosion is pretty crazy, but surely you

02:40:07.319 --> 02:40:10.019
can’t mutate back from nothing at all, right?

02:40:10.020 --> 02:40:11.100
Right!?

02:40:11.100 --> 02:40:13.860
Oh boy, I don’t like that look you’re
giving me…

02:40:13.859 --> 02:40:20.460
SCP-3930 is a void located near Usinsk, Russia,
within which nothing exists.

02:40:20.460 --> 02:40:25.980
Once something has passed within its border,
it ceases to be, though outside observers

02:40:25.979 --> 02:40:28.500
will be able to perceive them for a small
time after.

02:40:28.500 --> 02:40:33.420
SCP-682 was brought to 3930, and it walked
inside.

02:40:33.420 --> 02:40:36.060
Once there, it ceased existing.

02:40:36.060 --> 02:40:41.940
However, even though 682 no longer existed,
Foundation personnel looking at the void could

02:40:41.939 --> 02:40:43.139
still see the beast.

02:40:43.140 --> 02:40:48.420
Whenever they viewed it, a strong image appeared
in the brain of the person looking, and it

02:40:48.420 --> 02:40:52.020
had the exact appearance of SCP-682.

02:40:52.020 --> 02:40:58.020
Somehow, even when it didn’t exist, 682
was able to attack and kill various personnel.

02:40:58.020 --> 02:41:00.840
These people did not die from physical damage,&nbsp;

02:41:00.840 --> 02:41:03.960
but from their brain function&nbsp;
suddenly, inexplicably

02:41:03.960 --> 02:41:04.980
stopping.

02:41:04.979 --> 02:41:10.080
The reptile defied the rules of the void,
somehow causing real destruction even though

02:41:10.080 --> 02:41:11.160
it was not real.

02:41:11.160 --> 02:41:16.500
Fifteen hours later, 682 was found in its
containment chamber as if nothing had happened

02:41:16.500 --> 02:41:16.979
at all.

02:41:16.979 --> 02:41:22.500
It had been snuffed out of existence and had
mutated its way back into reality, with no

02:41:22.500 --> 02:41:23.160
explanation.

02:41:23.160 --> 02:41:25.800
Well, that was existentially terrifying.

02:41:25.800 --> 02:41:28.380
Thank 343 that at least there’s only one
of these things.

02:41:28.380 --> 02:41:30.120
Oh no…

02:41:30.120 --> 02:41:36.570
SCP-3207 is a highly efficient mobile war
machine, outfitted with cannons capable of

02:41:36.570 --> 02:41:39.600
firing blasts that can vaporize organic matter
on contact.

02:41:39.600 --> 02:41:45.480
This seems like a good match for something
supposedly indestructible. 3207 was fired

02:41:45.479 --> 02:41:51.179
at 682 several times, appearing to destroy
it completely except for a smudge on the floor

02:41:51.180 --> 02:41:51.900
of the chamber.

02:41:51.899 --> 02:41:57.479
The reptile was gone for a duration of six
hours before something strange began to happen.

02:41:57.479 --> 02:42:01.859
Globs of tissue began to clump together, forming
five separate piles.

02:42:01.859 --> 02:42:05.399
They pulled closer and&nbsp;
closer together, compressing&nbsp;

02:42:05.399 --> 02:42:07.500
into five reptilian creatures.

02:42:07.500 --> 02:42:12.600
They writhed around, getting used to their
new legs and teeth, snapping their jaws at

02:42:12.600 --> 02:42:14.040
any living thing in sight.

02:42:14.040 --> 02:42:16.859
Overwhelming and surprising&nbsp;
the security personnel,&nbsp;

02:42:16.859 --> 02:42:18.780
who had been lulled into a false sense of

02:42:18.780 --> 02:42:24.179
security by the apparent defeat of 682, the
five smaller versions of the entity were able

02:42:24.180 --> 02:42:25.320
to escape containment.

02:42:25.319 --> 02:42:30.540
Once they had made it into the hallway, they
began to clamber over each other, their scales

02:42:30.540 --> 02:42:36.120
shifting, eyeballs squeezing together and
fusing into one eye, skin stretching like

02:42:36.120 --> 02:42:38.760
hot rubber over unnaturally bendy bone.

02:42:38.760 --> 02:42:44.700
As the shocked security personnel watched,
the five lizards melted into one, becoming

02:42:44.700 --> 02:42:49.380
a full-sized version of SCP-682 that was good
as new.

02:42:49.380 --> 02:42:53.819
They were able to contain it after a great
deal of effort, but one of the researchers

02:42:53.819 --> 02:42:58.500
requested a note be added to the research
notes for the day, and applied going forward:

02:42:58.500 --> 02:43:00.540
DO NOT EXPLODE.

02:43:00.540 --> 02:43:03.899
Okay, so the big lizard is a constant threat.

02:43:03.899 --> 02:43:04.559
Got it.

02:43:04.560 --> 02:43:09.000
Still, wouldn’t it be nice if 682 could
make itself a little smaller?

02:43:09.000 --> 02:43:11.939
I can’t imagine anything bad coming from
that…

02:43:11.939 --> 02:43:18.000
SCP-1056 is an anomalous kitchen timer capable
of changing the size of living objects.

02:43:18.000 --> 02:43:23.280
The Foundation wanted to see how long it would
take 682 to return to its original size after

02:43:23.280 --> 02:43:24.059
being shrunk.

02:43:24.060 --> 02:43:30.360
So, they built a testing chamber connected
to 1056’s dial, and released 682 inside,

02:43:30.359 --> 02:43:32.519
sealing the door behind it.

02:43:32.520 --> 02:43:37.320
The dial was set to 0.25, and the activation
button was pressed.

02:43:37.319 --> 02:43:43.259
682 thrashed around, bellowing as parts of
its body expanded and contracted at random.

02:43:43.260 --> 02:43:46.320
Then, with no warning, it disappeared.

02:43:46.319 --> 02:43:51.120
D-class personnel were deployed to investigate
the chamber, but it seemed to be completely

02:43:51.120 --> 02:43:51.479
gone.

02:43:51.479 --> 02:43:53.399
There was no sign of it.

02:43:53.399 --> 02:43:58.920
It’s pretty hard to lose a giant lizard,
so naturally, they were all a bit perplexed.

02:43:58.920 --> 02:44:04.680
The chamber was kept sealed, under the assumption
that 682 had to still be inside somewhere.

02:44:04.680 --> 02:44:11.640
Sometime later, a security officer spotted
682 outside of Site-19, returned to its original

02:44:11.640 --> 02:44:12.300
size.

02:44:12.300 --> 02:44:18.720
Somehow, during the test, 682 used the effects
of 1056 to strengthen its ability to change

02:44:18.720 --> 02:44:19.560
its own size.

02:44:19.560 --> 02:44:24.960
It adapted and shrank to a size so small that
no one watching could even see it anymore,

02:44:24.960 --> 02:44:27.480
and it slipped out through the sealed door.

02:44:27.479 --> 02:44:32.819
It was even temporarily able to change the
size of other objects around it, shrinking

02:44:32.819 --> 02:44:35.700
weapons used to contain down until they were
useless.

02:44:35.700 --> 02:44:39.000
Okay, so SCP-682 is pretty cool under pressure.

02:44:39.000 --> 02:44:42.180
But what if we made it a whole lot colder?

02:44:42.180 --> 02:44:47.340
Most of the testing on 682 is done with other
anomalies, however, sometimes the Foundation

02:44:47.340 --> 02:44:48.900
likes to simplify a bit.

02:44:48.899 --> 02:44:54.059
Dr. Carlson suggested they try something a
bit more basic: liquid nitrogen.

02:44:54.060 --> 02:44:58.860
One ton of liquid nitrogen was poured onto
SCP-682 from above.

02:44:58.859 --> 02:45:03.120
As it tends to do, the liquid nitrogen promptly
froze the beast solid.

02:45:03.120 --> 02:45:08.399
It remained stuck in place for about 10 minutes,
until it began to melt the frozen cast around

02:45:08.399 --> 02:45:08.700
it.

02:45:08.700 --> 02:45:13.800
Its core body temperature seemed to skyrocket,
producing intense heat that fully thawed it

02:45:13.800 --> 02:45:14.820
in three minutes.

02:45:14.819 --> 02:45:16.740
It didn’t stop there, though.

02:45:16.740 --> 02:45:21.840
Its temperature continued to increase, growing
hotter and hotter as if to deliberately punish

02:45:21.840 --> 02:45:24.720
the research staff for even attempting to
freeze it.

02:45:24.720 --> 02:45:28.320
It became so hot that the research staff had
to leave the room.

02:45:28.319 --> 02:45:32.580
An attending doctor’s pen melted, the plastic
burning his hands.

02:45:32.580 --> 02:45:36.720
Steam rose off the sides of its body, fogging
up the windows of the room.

02:45:36.720 --> 02:45:41.580
The test was abandoned after the sides of
the containment chamber began to melt, and

02:45:41.580 --> 02:45:44.220
they worried the creature would be able to
breach containment.

02:45:44.220 --> 02:45:48.781
Once it was left alone, 682 cooled back down
to its usual temperature.

02:45:48.780 --> 02:45:54.300
Maybe we should see what happens if we try
a slightly greener method of destruction…

02:45:54.300 --> 02:46:01.800
682 was exposed to SCP-166, a young nature
spirit that can cause organic matter in her

02:46:01.800 --> 02:46:03.480
vicinity to decompose.

02:46:03.479 --> 02:46:10.799
As soon as 166 was released into its chamber,
682 began to run toward her even as its body

02:46:10.800 --> 02:46:12.060
began to melt.

02:46:12.060 --> 02:46:18.060
As it got closer, it began to decay and fall
apart more rapidly, pieces of its body softening

02:46:18.060 --> 02:46:19.680
and sloughing off in chunks.

02:46:19.680 --> 02:46:25.680
By the time it reached 166, it had melted
down into the shape of a patch of grass covered

02:46:25.680 --> 02:46:27.060
with colorful wildflowers.

02:46:27.060 --> 02:46:33.720
Fifteen minutes later, it began to regenerate
itself as it usually does, its body reconstituting

02:46:33.720 --> 02:46:35.640
at the same rate it was melting.

02:46:35.640 --> 02:46:40.741
The regeneration process began to speed up,
going faster and faster until it surpassed

02:46:40.740 --> 02:46:41.939
the rate of melting.

02:46:41.939 --> 02:46:47.040
A piece of the monster would soften and flop
to the ground, but by the time it landed a

02:46:47.040 --> 02:46:49.200
patch of regrowth had already replaced it.

02:46:49.200 --> 02:46:54.840
It eventually beat the melting process and
regenerated to its original form, with one

02:46:54.840 --> 02:47:00.360
difference: it had a sprinkling of flowers
and mushrooms on its back, resembling a forest

02:47:00.359 --> 02:47:00.780
clearing.

02:47:00.780 --> 02:47:06.479
It was almost pretty, even on top of such
a foul creature, until a full-sized tree suddenly

02:47:06.479 --> 02:47:11.759
burst out of its back, shooting up to a height
of ten feet and puncturing the roof of its

02:47:11.760 --> 02:47:12.600
containment chamber.

02:47:12.600 --> 02:47:14.161
Hello again, dear viewers.

02:47:14.160 --> 02:47:15.540
You’ve caught me during my break.

02:47:15.540 --> 02:47:16.319
What?

02:47:16.319 --> 02:47:20.460
Even researchers at the SCP Foundation need
a little downtime now and then.

02:47:20.460 --> 02:47:23.280
And considering they revoked&nbsp;
my playtime privileges&nbsp;

02:47:23.280 --> 02:47:25.559
with The Living Lego and the Nerfing Gun after

02:47:25.560 --> 02:47:30.480
the unfortunate incident in the Site-19 Break
Room, I’ve been downgraded to keeping myself

02:47:30.479 --> 02:47:32.399
occupied with this little rubber ball.

02:47:32.399 --> 02:47:33.359
“I have a ball.

02:47:33.359 --> 02:47:34.979
Perhaps you'd like to bounce it,” they said.

02:47:34.979 --> 02:47:36.839
Seems innocent enough, doesn’t it?

02:47:39.420 --> 02:47:41.640
Oh, have you learned nothing?

02:47:41.640 --> 02:47:47.281
Almost any object, even something as innocuous
as a Teddy Bear or a plastic paddling pool,

02:47:47.280 --> 02:47:48.660
can hide secrets.

02:47:48.660 --> 02:47:52.500
Sure, any avid basketball fan will happily
tell you that ball is life.

02:47:52.500 --> 02:47:57.960
But sometimes, when you’re dealing with
anomalies, a ball can also… be death.

02:47:57.960 --> 02:48:03.840
Such is the case of SCP-018, also known as
The Super Ball.

02:48:03.840 --> 02:48:10.319
An anomaly so powerful that the Foundation
has even used it to help recontain SCP-682

02:48:10.319 --> 02:48:11.340
during a breach.

02:48:11.340 --> 02:48:14.700
To the untrained observer, it really isn’t
much to look at.

02:48:14.700 --> 02:48:20.220
A small, red rubber ball, about six centimeters
in diameter, produced by the Wham-O company

02:48:20.220 --> 02:48:22.080
in 1969.

02:48:22.080 --> 02:48:26.280
Yeah, we were as surprised as you to find
out that good ol’ Dr. Wondertainment had

02:48:26.280 --> 02:48:27.719
nothing to do with this little number.

02:48:27.720 --> 02:48:32.940
You might also be surprised by just how extensive
the containment procedures are for SCP-018

02:48:32.940 --> 02:48:38.520
- After all, it’s rare that a competently
non-sentient anomaly makes its way into the

02:48:38.520 --> 02:48:39.600
Euclid class.

02:48:39.600 --> 02:48:43.080
This little rubber ball is&nbsp;
kept in a specially-made&nbsp;

02:48:43.080 --> 02:48:46.319
titanium-alloy metal restraint, submerged

02:48:46.319 --> 02:48:51.540
in a dense polyethylene holding tank, filled
with a special endothermic compound that draws

02:48:51.540 --> 02:48:53.580
the kinetic energy out of its surroundings.

02:48:53.580 --> 02:48:58.920
Anyone entering the chamber needs to wear
a unique kind of reinforced plate armor, and

02:48:58.920 --> 02:49:04.980
if SCP-018 ever manages to escape its containment
tank, nearby personnel are advised to treat

02:49:04.979 --> 02:49:07.500
it as they would an active shooter situation.

02:49:07.500 --> 02:49:12.780
Lock yourself in a nearby room, duck down
below any cover you can find, and wait for

02:49:12.780 --> 02:49:16.500
armed containment units to show up and take
control of the situation.

02:49:16.500 --> 02:49:21.840
At this point, you probably have a lot of
questions, chief among them being: Why is

02:49:21.840 --> 02:49:25.920
this children’s toy being given more security
precautions than most serial killers?

02:49:25.920 --> 02:49:30.480
The ball was first discovered when a cleaning
and disposal company was hired to empty out

02:49:30.479 --> 02:49:33.419
an old Wham-O warehouse of&nbsp;
some defunct merchandise.

02:49:33.420 --> 02:49:38.220
One of the movers, Roy Fischler, embraced
his inner child when he saw a red, rubber

02:49:38.220 --> 02:49:43.200
ball sitting among all the dusty boxes of
expired silly putty and broken remote control

02:49:43.200 --> 02:49:43.859
robots.

02:49:43.859 --> 02:49:47.219
He thought to himself, “what’s the harm
in having a little fun here?

02:49:47.220 --> 02:49:48.720
It’s all going into the trash anyway.”

02:49:48.720 --> 02:49:52.920
This would prove to be a terrible mistake
for all involved.

02:49:52.920 --> 02:49:59.580
The anomalous property of SCP-018 is the fact
that it’s able to bounce at 200% efficiency

02:49:59.580 --> 02:50:05.280
every time it’s bounced, increasing at an
exponential rate with each bounce unless it’s

02:50:05.280 --> 02:50:07.259
stopped by some equivalent force.

02:50:07.260 --> 02:50:12.900
So when Roy decided to toss that little red
ball onto the ground, he’d unleashed a destructive

02:50:12.899 --> 02:50:17.700
force into that warehouse that was more powerful
than he ever could have imagined.

02:50:17.700 --> 02:50:22.859
With every bounce, the ball increased its
height and speed, ricocheting across the floor,

02:50:22.859 --> 02:50:25.979
walls, and ceiling like a bullet run amok.

02:50:25.979 --> 02:50:28.259
And it was only just getting started.

02:50:28.260 --> 02:50:33.180
The workers hit the deck as the item that
would later be dubbed SCP-018 decided to put

02:50:33.180 --> 02:50:34.741
the “ball” in “ballistic.”

02:50:34.740 --> 02:50:36.420
It smashed light fixtures.

02:50:36.420 --> 02:50:38.220
Knocked over piles of boxes.

02:50:38.220 --> 02:50:40.140
Smashed through forklifts.

02:50:40.140 --> 02:50:44.820
When one worker tried to catch it, it left
a red-hot, ball-shaped hole in the middle

02:50:44.819 --> 02:50:45.599
of his palm.

02:50:45.600 --> 02:50:49.920
It wasn’t long before the ball had built
up such speed that the warehouse could no

02:50:49.920 --> 02:50:51.000
longer contain it.

02:50:51.000 --> 02:50:56.280
It blasted out of the wall and rocketed into
the nearby city, ready to cause more abject

02:50:56.280 --> 02:50:57.899
chaos wherever it went.

02:50:57.899 --> 02:50:59.519
Windows were shattered.

02:50:59.520 --> 02:51:01.081
Street lights were annihilated.

02:51:01.080 --> 02:51:02.519
Cars crashed.

02:51:02.520 --> 02:51:07.680
Thankfully, no humans were killed by the rampaging
rubber menace, but in total five people were

02:51:07.680 --> 02:51:12.781
injured - And one unfortunate pigeon was utterly
obliterated on impact.

02:51:12.780 --> 02:51:17.939
It went on for several days, with the ball
reaching over 100 kilometers per hour at several

02:51:17.939 --> 02:51:21.240
points, before finally coming to rest at a
nearby lake.

02:51:21.240 --> 02:51:24.719
At which point, it was retrieved by Foundation
personnel.

02:51:24.720 --> 02:51:30.300
There were two silver linings to this incredibly
strange anomalous incident: The first was,

02:51:30.300 --> 02:51:33.300
as previously alluded to, nobody actually
died.

02:51:33.300 --> 02:51:38.760
The second was that, due to the incredible
speeds at which SCP-018 moved, none of the

02:51:38.760 --> 02:51:42.180
civilian witnesses had any idea what they’d
just encountered.

02:51:42.180 --> 02:51:47.220
As far as anomalous discoveries go, this was
pretty much as close to a win as you can get.

02:51:47.220 --> 02:51:52.980
But for one ambitious researcher, it was far
more than just a pleasingly non-violent initial

02:51:52.979 --> 02:51:58.379
containment story - It was a doorway to improving
the Foundation’s technology as a whole.

02:51:58.380 --> 02:52:00.420
Meet Dr. Brian Karella.

02:52:00.420 --> 02:52:05.700
He’s what you might call a maverick, a blue
sky thinker, always on his grind.

02:52:05.700 --> 02:52:10.260
The cornerstone of Dr. Karella’s philosophy
was that the Foundation should be making more

02:52:10.260 --> 02:52:15.540
active use of its benign anomalies to help
track down and contain their more ornery foes.

02:52:15.540 --> 02:52:20.279
While everyone else around him seemed to only
see a little rubber nuisance that was better

02:52:20.279 --> 02:52:25.859
locked away, Dr. Karella saw the immense potential
in SCP-018.

02:52:25.859 --> 02:52:31.319
Namely, in providing a vital enhancement to
another piece of Foundation technology: The

02:52:31.319 --> 02:52:33.299
SCP-A5 Armor.

02:52:33.300 --> 02:52:37.860
It goes without saying that working for the
SCP Foundation is an incredibly dangerous

02:52:37.859 --> 02:52:42.420
job, especially if you’re part of one of
the Foundation’s myriad mobile task forces.

02:52:42.420 --> 02:52:47.399
The hunt for anomalies can lead to all kinds
of strange and inhospitable terrains.

02:52:47.399 --> 02:52:53.939
Before it was contained, SCP-096 was famously
captured on an icy, frozen tundra on top of

02:52:53.939 --> 02:52:54.779
a bleak mountain.

02:52:54.779 --> 02:53:01.019
Because of incidents like this, the Foundation
had first invested money in the SCP-A5 Tactical

02:53:01.020 --> 02:53:01.621
Armor Suit.

02:53:01.620 --> 02:53:05.040
Think of them like the Foundation’s answer
to the Iron Man suit.

02:53:05.040 --> 02:53:09.840
However, when dressed in several hundred pounds
of reinforced metal, something important suffers

02:53:09.840 --> 02:53:11.700
along the way: Mobility.

02:53:11.700 --> 02:53:15.359
It isn’t exactly easy to lug all that equipment
around.

02:53:15.359 --> 02:53:20.040
And when an anomaly is heading for the hills
at high speeds, being well-defended doesn’t

02:53:20.040 --> 02:53:23.880
count for much if you’re already ten miles
behind the target in pursuit.

02:53:23.880 --> 02:53:29.580
This, in Dr. Karella’s mind, was exactly
where SCP-018 came into play.

02:53:29.580 --> 02:53:35.279
If that little red ball was built into the
foot of an SCP-A5 Armor suit, it could be

02:53:35.279 --> 02:53:38.639
used to bounce the operative wearing it to
tremendous heights.

02:53:38.640 --> 02:53:43.500
This would allow them to not only give chance
against fast-moving anomalies but also cover

02:53:43.500 --> 02:53:47.880
difficult terrain and even scale great heights
in a mere instant.

02:53:47.880 --> 02:53:54.120
But it wasn’t just an increase to mobility
that SCP-018 integration offered to the SCP-A5

02:53:54.120 --> 02:53:54.479
suit.

02:53:54.479 --> 02:54:00.839
Picture this: With SCP-108 fused to the sole
of the suit’s reinforced metal foot, lending

02:54:00.840 --> 02:54:06.360
it 200% bouncing efficiency, it could unleash
a deadly, concrete-shattering kick.

02:54:06.359 --> 02:54:10.559
The kind of thing that would leave you singing
in falsetto for the rest of your life if you

02:54:10.560 --> 02:54:13.320
were lucky enough to survive it, if you know
what I mean.

02:54:13.319 --> 02:54:16.439
To Dr. Karella, it was a match made in heaven.

02:54:16.439 --> 02:54:21.359
It could increase both the mobility and combat
effectiveness of the suits by a considerable

02:54:21.359 --> 02:54:21.839
margin.

02:54:21.840 --> 02:54:27.540
And seeing as SCP-018 literally didn’t have
a mind of its own, there’s no way it could

02:54:27.540 --> 02:54:33.060
suddenly go rogue during a mission and compromise
everything - just as Able had during his stint

02:54:33.060 --> 02:54:37.380
as a Mobile Task Force operator before they
ran out of targets for him and he started

02:54:37.380 --> 02:54:39.300
slaughtering his own comrades.

02:54:39.300 --> 02:54:44.820
Dr. Karella was so confident in the efficacy
of this idea, he contacted the O5 Council

02:54:44.819 --> 02:54:47.639
personally to request approval for this little
pet project.

02:54:47.640 --> 02:54:50.640
This approval was granted, on a purely&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:50.640 --> 02:54:51.780
experimental
basis.

02:54:51.779 --> 02:54:55.740
The technology would have to prove itself
before being put into common use.

02:54:55.740 --> 02:55:00.779
It wasn’t exactly what Karella wanted to
hear, but it was a step in the right direction.

02:55:00.779 --> 02:55:05.040
He just needed the perfect opportunity to
put them to the test.

02:55:05.040 --> 02:55:11.819
And then it came: SCP-682, the Infamous Hard
to Destroy Reptile, breached containment.

02:55:11.819 --> 02:55:16.439
It’d somehow adapted a cloaking ability
and escaped further from the site it was being

02:55:16.439 --> 02:55:17.639
held at than ever before.

02:55:17.640 --> 02:55:22.741
The next time it was spotted was over two
weeks later, causing pandemonium in the Amazon

02:55:22.740 --> 02:55:27.359
Rainforest, devouring tribesmen and wreaking
havoc on the local ecosystem.

02:55:27.359 --> 02:55:32.759
They needed to get on the scene fast and put
that monster down before the damage it caused

02:55:32.760 --> 02:55:37.500
was irreparable, and news of the Beast in
the Amazon leaked out into the local area.

02:55:37.500 --> 02:55:41.880
And thankfully, Dr. Karella had just the tool
for the job.

02:55:41.880 --> 02:55:48.779
Field Agent Hammersmith was fitted with an
SCP-A5 suit, complete with the SCP-018 enhancement

02:55:48.779 --> 02:55:50.219
in his dominant right leg.

02:55:50.220 --> 02:55:55.080
He was dispatched, and immediately, the augmented
suit began to show its efficacy.

02:55:55.080 --> 02:56:00.180
Agent Hammersmith bounded above the treeline
at incredible speeds, using the HUD in the

02:56:00.180 --> 02:56:05.340
suit’s mask to track the heat signature
of SCP-682 moving among the trees below him.

02:56:05.340 --> 02:56:09.600
He’d been able to bind a tracking collar
to the beast’s neck during an earlier engagement,

02:56:09.600 --> 02:56:11.760
but now the true battle was on.

02:56:11.760 --> 02:56:16.560
His heart was pounding, adrenaline coursing
through his veins, but he’d been ensured

02:56:16.560 --> 02:56:20.820
that even 682 would have a hard time tearing
through his suit’s armor.

02:56:20.819 --> 02:56:26.219
A commander directing him through an earpiece
told him now was the time to engage, before

02:56:26.220 --> 02:56:29.880
682 detected his presence and began developing
countermeasures.

02:56:29.880 --> 02:56:35.279
Dr. Karella was watching a live feed from
the control room, confident that his 018-augmented

02:56:35.279 --> 02:56:36.359
suit would do the job.

02:56:36.359 --> 02:56:41.580
Following his orders to the letter, Hammersmith
descended down onto 682 from above.

02:56:41.580 --> 02:56:46.439
However, before he could make contact, the
reptile swiped him with its tail, sending

02:56:46.439 --> 02:56:48.419
his body sailing into a nearby tree.

02:56:48.420 --> 02:56:50.640
However, the suit stood firm.

02:56:50.640 --> 02:56:53.760
He felt the impact, but the actual damage
was minimal.

02:56:53.760 --> 02:56:57.900
Now, it was time for him to face off against
the beast, one on one.

02:56:57.899 --> 02:56:59.819
He didn’t have time to be afraid.

02:56:59.819 --> 02:57:04.859
As the beast descended upon him, fangs bared,
he gave it a swift kick to the bottom jaw,

02:57:04.859 --> 02:57:06.359
tearing off half of its face.

02:57:06.359 --> 02:57:11.939
But anyone who knows SCP-682 would tell you
that simply removing its bottom jaw wouldn’t

02:57:11.939 --> 02:57:13.740
even slow 682 down.

02:57:13.740 --> 02:57:18.599
It was relentless, attacking Hammersmith with
its fangs and jaws.

02:57:18.600 --> 02:57:23.520
It tore deep ruts into the suit’s metal,
but the suit was still managing to keep its

02:57:23.520 --> 02:57:24.360
occupant safe.

02:57:24.359 --> 02:57:26.880
Then Hammersmith struck back.

02:57:26.880 --> 02:57:33.300
Kick after kick, augmented by the 200% power
of the Super Ball, sliced huge chunks from

02:57:33.300 --> 02:57:34.260
the reptile’s body.

02:57:34.260 --> 02:57:40.500
He kicked in its chest, kicked off limbs,
and with a final mighty kick, even managed

02:57:40.500 --> 02:57:42.060
to bisect the beast in the middle.

02:57:42.060 --> 02:57:47.701
Of course, even that wouldn’t keep it down
for long, but with the hum of evacuation and

02:57:47.700 --> 02:57:52.080
containment helicopters rapidly approaching,
Hammersmith breathed a sigh of relief.

02:57:52.080 --> 02:57:58.260
Back in the control room, everyone celebrated
- Dr. Karella most of all, vindicated in his

02:57:58.260 --> 02:58:01.320
belief that SCP-018 could save the day.

02:58:01.319 --> 02:58:06.840
And then Agent Hammersmith, without even thinking,
rested his right foot on the floor just that

02:58:06.840 --> 02:58:08.340
little bit too firmly.

02:58:08.340 --> 02:58:11.279
The sudden bounce sent Hammersmith a mile
into the air.

02:58:11.279 --> 02:58:16.559
His Foundation-trained composure evaporated;
all he could do was scream as he blasted up

02:58:16.560 --> 02:58:19.081
into the clouds, then began to plummet.

02:58:19.080 --> 02:58:23.399
Back in the control room, everyone could see
a live feed of Agent Hammersmith hurtling

02:58:23.399 --> 02:58:26.759
into a nearby lake and landing with an epic
splash.

02:58:26.760 --> 02:58:31.800
While the regenerating remains of SCP-682
were contained and brought back to the nearest

02:58:31.800 --> 02:58:37.740
containment site, another team was sent in
to retrieve the heavily injured Agent Hammersmith.

02:58:37.740 --> 02:58:42.719
His medical examination afterward revealed
he’d suffered two broken legs, seven broken

02:58:42.720 --> 02:58:45.600
ribs, a missing arm, and a skull fracture.

02:58:45.600 --> 02:58:49.980
If he hadn’t been wearing the suit, his
mangled remains probably would have been devoured

02:58:49.979 --> 02:58:51.660
by the local piranhas by now.

02:58:51.660 --> 02:58:56.819
But despite that minor hiccup in the plan,
Dr. Karella was still delighted with the results,

02:58:56.819 --> 02:59:00.000
and immensely proud of the little red ball
that could.

02:59:00.000 --> 02:59:05.460
In his closing remarks on the incident, he
appended a final note to the SCP-018 file,

02:59:05.460 --> 02:59:05.880
reading:

02:59:05.880 --> 02:59:07.380
“Don't worry, it's fixed.

02:59:07.380 --> 02:59:09.180
But, I have some more ideas.

02:59:09.180 --> 02:59:14.340
If I can be granted the use of some water
from SCP-006, as well as some other SCPs,

02:59:14.340 --> 02:59:19.680
I can deliver you a set of SCP-A5 armor and
an agent that can capture any, if not all,

02:59:19.680 --> 02:59:21.600
rogue or unattained SCPs.

02:59:21.600 --> 02:59:24.420
All I'm waiting on is your approval.”&nbsp;

02:59:24.420 --> 02:59:30.120
A beloved mentally unstable, masked vigilante
once said, “I’m not trapped in here with

02:59:30.120 --> 02:59:32.160
you, you’re trapped in here with me!”

02:59:32.160 --> 02:59:39.359
And this exact sentiment was shared by SPCP-682,
the Hard to Destroy Reptile, as it traversed

02:59:39.359 --> 02:59:42.960
the almost limitless, liminal hell known as
The Backrooms.

02:59:42.960 --> 02:59:47.220
It’d been little more than a standard “chase
and secure” mission for the Mobile Task

02:59:47.220 --> 02:59:54.000
Forces pursuing SCP-682 after its latest deadly
containment breach, until the vicious lizard

02:59:54.000 --> 02:59:59.580
made its way into an abandoned warehouse and
no clipped its way into a new reality.

02:59:59.580 --> 03:00:04.559
As the SCP Foundation are still desperately
searching for the missing beast back in our

03:00:04.560 --> 03:00:09.600
native reality, 682 has been discovering whole
new vistas of violence.

03:00:09.600 --> 03:00:14.520
First, it found itself in the endless yellow
halls of Level Zero, where if the madness

03:00:14.520 --> 03:00:19.081
doesn’t get you, the starvation and thirst
will - Well, unless you’re an anomalous

03:00:19.080 --> 03:00:22.559
reptilian abomination that can seemingly adapt
to any situation.

03:00:22.560 --> 03:00:29.280
Once 682 escaped this gaudy purgatory, it
found its way into Level One, an endless warehouse

03:00:29.279 --> 03:00:35.160
full of equal parts monsters and hapless human
settlers - all of whom it decimated in a single

03:00:35.160 --> 03:00:35.939
bloody afternoon.

03:00:35.939 --> 03:00:41.939
Then, onto Level Two, the Pipe Rooms, where
it faced a bevy of beasts that it eagerly

03:00:41.939 --> 03:00:43.019
put into the ground.

03:00:43.020 --> 03:00:48.600
And that brings us up to now - And, by extension,
onto Level Three.

03:00:48.600 --> 03:00:53.880
SCP-682 spilled out into another section of
long, industrial hallways.

03:00:53.880 --> 03:00:58.260
It didn’t know how it had gotten in, and
honestly, it didn’t really care at this

03:00:58.260 --> 03:00:58.440
point.

03:00:58.439 --> 03:01:03.899
All it needed to do was keep moving forward
and killing as it pleased, and it seemed there

03:01:03.899 --> 03:01:06.059
were plenty of creatures down here to kill.

03:01:06.060 --> 03:01:10.380
That being said, this level had a certain
energy to it.

03:01:10.380 --> 03:01:14.220
And we mean that literally: 682’s incredibly
sensitive…

03:01:14.220 --> 03:01:20.520
Well, senses, allowed it to detect an incredibly
powerful electrical field emanating from this

03:01:20.520 --> 03:01:20.701
level.

03:01:20.700 --> 03:01:25.800
And from the sounds of machines humming all
around it, traveling down great bundles of

03:01:25.800 --> 03:01:30.900
wires and pipes bound to the walls, it knew
that this level must have been attached to

03:01:30.899 --> 03:01:33.660
a generator of truly incredible size.

03:01:33.660 --> 03:01:39.960
It charged forward, weaving around the different
hallways at freakish speeds, searching for

03:01:39.960 --> 03:01:42.480
the next thing it could blast into oblivion.

03:01:42.479 --> 03:01:46.379
And thankfully, it was able to find its first
target soon enough.

03:01:46.380 --> 03:01:49.200
A nest of creatures known as Death Moths.

03:01:49.200 --> 03:01:54.479
These were huge, fluttering moths of freakish
size, congregating around a glowing electrical

03:01:54.479 --> 03:01:54.779
outlet.

03:01:54.779 --> 03:01:56.340
Intriguing.

03:01:56.340 --> 03:02:02.580
SCP-682 decided to approach and introduce
itself - After all, they looked like pretty

03:02:02.580 --> 03:02:03.479
easy prey.

03:02:03.479 --> 03:02:06.240
682 would regret this oversight.

03:02:06.240 --> 03:02:10.979
While the male Death Moths are pretty much
harmless, the female Death Moths have an extremely

03:02:10.979 --> 03:02:12.359
potent defense mechanism.

03:02:12.359 --> 03:02:18.479
As SCP-682 approached, the creatures began
swarming and spraying acid onto its reptilian

03:02:18.479 --> 03:02:19.019
flesh.

03:02:19.020 --> 03:02:25.320
This was painful and irritating for 682, of
course, but if any entity on earth is pretty

03:02:25.319 --> 03:02:31.139
accustomed to dealing with large quantities
of powerful acid by now, it’s SCP-682.

03:02:31.140 --> 03:02:36.840
Its skin quickly healed from the acidic onslaught
and it developed a powerful counteradaptation:

03:02:36.840 --> 03:02:42.480
A long, sticky, frog-like tongue, which it
used to devour the nest full of Death Moths

03:02:42.479 --> 03:02:44.339
and move along to its next target.

03:02:44.340 --> 03:02:46.620
It continued exploring Level 3.

03:02:46.620 --> 03:02:51.840
A number of hallways were marked off with
metal bars - another very familiar sight for

03:02:51.840 --> 03:02:58.020
SCP-682 - so, for simplicity’s sake, it
just kept itself to the unobstructed paths.

03:02:58.020 --> 03:03:03.000
That’s where it soon ran into another lifeform,
standing around like a sitting duck in one

03:03:03.000 --> 03:03:05.100
of the level’s many anonymous hallways.

03:03:05.100 --> 03:03:10.920
It was just another human, in a similar outfit
to all those “Major Explorer Group” weaklings

03:03:10.920 --> 03:03:12.300
it had destroyed earlier.

03:03:12.300 --> 03:03:18.300
Strangely, even when SCP-682 entered the hallway
with it, it didn’t seem to react properly.

03:03:18.300 --> 03:03:23.040
It just vacantly stared off into space, stumbling
around awkwardly.

03:03:23.040 --> 03:03:30.359
682, bemused, whipped this random, disoriented
stranger in the chest with its tail, sending

03:03:30.359 --> 03:03:32.339
him sailing into the nearby wall.

03:03:32.340 --> 03:03:37.440
It was at this point that something strange
happened: The force of the strike caused the

03:03:37.439 --> 03:03:43.919
man’s clothes, and also skin, to disintegrate,
leaving something entirely different underneath.

03:03:43.920 --> 03:03:49.200
SCP-682 had no idea what was going on, but
it knew that it hated it.

03:03:49.200 --> 03:03:53.819
This was its first encounter with a creature
known as a Skin Stealer.

03:03:53.819 --> 03:03:57.960
It would be natural for a human being to be
terrified of an abomination like this.

03:03:57.960 --> 03:04:00.720
An apex predator like 682, on the other hand?

03:04:00.720 --> 03:04:03.720
It barely even found the Skin Stealer interesting.

03:04:03.720 --> 03:04:10.560
With a single stomp from its clawed, reptilian
foot, the creature was very, very dead, and

03:04:10.560 --> 03:04:14.820
SCP-682 continued its journey through the
bowels of Level 3.

03:04:14.819 --> 03:04:20.279
It found itself drawn to whatever the source
of all the energy was, if it even had one

03:04:20.279 --> 03:04:21.240
single source.

03:04:21.240 --> 03:04:26.460
It was almost as though the entire level was
one giant generator, powering the rest of

03:04:26.460 --> 03:04:27.300
the Backrooms.

03:04:27.300 --> 03:04:32.279
And if there was electricity, perhaps there
were other humans in here to kill…

03:04:32.279 --> 03:04:36.960
SCP-682 liked that idea very much indeed.

03:04:36.960 --> 03:04:41.880
However, while making its way down a slightly
wider hallway - one that it had previously

03:04:41.880 --> 03:04:46.560
believed was completely uninhabited - it was
suddenly ambushed by a group of mysterious

03:04:46.560 --> 03:04:47.220
attackers.

03:04:47.220 --> 03:04:53.100
A number of tall, grey creatures with long,
clawing arms and unclear facial features stepped

03:04:53.100 --> 03:04:53.820
away from the wall.

03:04:53.819 --> 03:04:59.099
These entities are known as the Dullers, ambush
predators native to the Backrooms.

03:04:59.100 --> 03:05:01.980
They normally run away from&nbsp;
threats, but considering&nbsp;

03:05:01.979 --> 03:05:03.899
the number of them congregated in the hall

03:05:03.899 --> 03:05:10.019
around SCP-682, perhaps they felt a little
more confident about taking down their prey

03:05:10.020 --> 03:05:10.680
in a group.

03:05:10.680 --> 03:05:16.080
But they’d made a grave calculation: It
wouldn’t matter whether there was one Duller

03:05:16.080 --> 03:05:17.760
or a thousand Dullers.

03:05:17.760 --> 03:05:25.680
In the battle between them and SCP-682, they
would always, always, always be the prey.

03:05:25.680 --> 03:05:31.741
But lucky for them, while they weren’t aware
of this immutable fact yet, SCP-682 was more

03:05:31.740 --> 03:05:34.559
than happy to give them a first-hand education.

03:05:34.560 --> 03:05:41.100
While the Dullers tried their best to claw
into 682’s thick, leathery hide, the creature

03:05:41.100 --> 03:05:45.180
decided to employ a new ability it had stolen
from the female Death Moths.

03:05:45.180 --> 03:05:50.760
Several new glands developed all over 682’s
body, each of which produced a fine mist of

03:05:50.760 --> 03:05:52.320
highly concentrated acid.

03:05:52.319 --> 03:05:57.899
Soon enough, the Dullers were howling in pain,
and melting away into dull, grey puddles on

03:05:57.899 --> 03:06:00.899
the ground, never to reconstitute again.

03:06:00.899 --> 03:06:04.259
That’s what you get for trying to climb
up the food chain, folks.

03:06:04.260 --> 03:06:05.640
It never ends well.

03:06:05.640 --> 03:06:07.980
Unless you’re 682, that is.

03:06:07.979 --> 03:06:13.319
After disposing of the Dullers - which, in
682’s own humble opinion had more than earned

03:06:13.319 --> 03:06:18.240
that title by indeed being extremely dull
- it decided to continue its search for some

03:06:18.240 --> 03:06:20.040
of the power sources on this level.

03:06:20.040 --> 03:06:23.040
Perhaps it could harness this ability for
its own benefit.

03:06:23.040 --> 03:06:28.380
But it was interrupted by what is, frankly,
one of the grossesst enemies in all of the

03:06:28.380 --> 03:06:30.180
Backrooms: The Bursters.

03:06:30.180 --> 03:06:34.980
And if even hearing that name made you feel
a little sick, then you’re correctly primed

03:06:34.979 --> 03:06:36.419
for what you’re about to encounter.

03:06:36.420 --> 03:06:41.700
They’re humanoid creatures that walk around
on all fours, with its back legs grotesquely

03:06:41.700 --> 03:06:44.460
stretched out into the shape of a dog’s
hind legs.

03:06:44.460 --> 03:06:48.540
But that’s nothing compared to a Burster’s
truly diabolical backne.

03:06:48.540 --> 03:06:54.000
All over the creature’s back, you can see
huge, callused cysts that contain a potent

03:06:54.000 --> 03:06:55.500
and noxious acid.

03:06:55.500 --> 03:06:59.939
Sure, the acid is only about as dangerous
as the stuff produced by female Death Moths,

03:06:59.939 --> 03:07:05.519
but in our humble opinion, the method of acid
delivery is far more repulsive, and that makes

03:07:05.520 --> 03:07:07.980
Bursters less desirable to encounter.

03:07:07.979 --> 03:07:12.240
A small group of them skittered out of the
darkness towards SCP-682.

03:07:12.240 --> 03:07:17.040
The Hard to Destroy Reptile also found them
disgusting - though now that we think about

03:07:17.040 --> 03:07:20.819
it, SCP-682 thinks all forms&nbsp;
of life are disgusting,&nbsp;

03:07:20.819 --> 03:07:23.219
so we suppose it’s all relative.

03:07:23.220 --> 03:07:29.100
However, when they began to burst their backs
and coat 682 in their horrible pus, they perhaps

03:07:29.100 --> 03:07:34.020
earned the rarely-given label of “extra
disgusting” from this living embodiment

03:07:34.020 --> 03:07:35.520
of reptilian hate.

03:07:35.520 --> 03:07:40.920
682 quickly retaliated by clawing the horrid
creatures to death, which I think we can all

03:07:40.920 --> 03:07:45.060
agree is a good and well-deserved ending for
the vile little beasts.

03:07:45.060 --> 03:07:47.040
We would have done the same thing.

03:07:47.040 --> 03:07:52.439
The next enemies that 682 encountered weren’t
nightmarish creatures, but in fact, were human

03:07:52.439 --> 03:07:58.019
beings stationed in the Major Explorer Group’s
Base Gamma, the third most important base

03:07:58.020 --> 03:07:59.760
in all of the Backrooms.

03:07:59.760 --> 03:08:04.680
They were on high alert after losing contact
with Base Alpha several days before - Having

03:08:04.680 --> 03:08:10.620
no idea that everyone at that base had been
slaughtered by SCP-682, a fate that, if they

03:08:10.620 --> 03:08:13.559
weren’t tremendously lucky, they would soon
share.

03:08:13.560 --> 03:08:17.581
But they had a little more than luck on their
side this time…

03:08:17.580 --> 03:08:21.899
SCP-682 sighted the base on the end of a long
hallway.

03:08:21.899 --> 03:08:26.879
There was even a person standing at the other
end of the hall, seemingly blissfully unaware

03:08:26.880 --> 03:08:31.859
of the encroaching presence of one of the
SCP Foundation’s most dangerous and formidable

03:08:31.859 --> 03:08:38.399
captives. 682 loved killing humans most of
all - They weren’t just dumb animals, they

03:08:38.399 --> 03:08:43.019
had the intellectual capacity to actually
appreciate the life that was being ripped

03:08:43.020 --> 03:08:48.720
away from them, and it made the whole act
even more pleasurable for SCP-682.

03:08:48.720 --> 03:08:53.940
It set its sights on the ignorant Major Explorer
Group member leaning against the distant wall,

03:08:53.939 --> 03:08:58.439
and decided to charge for him, claws extended
and fangs bared.

03:08:58.439 --> 03:09:01.080
This would be such easy prey.

03:09:01.080 --> 03:09:05.880
Until the moment when someone in the distance
yelled, “NOW!”, and the seemingly defenseless

03:09:05.880 --> 03:09:08.279
human turned around and pulled a level on
the wall.

03:09:08.279 --> 03:09:13.080
Suddenly, the whole hallway was electrified,
sending millions of volts coursing through

03:09:13.080 --> 03:09:15.600
SCP-682’s writhing body.

03:09:15.600 --> 03:09:18.960
This whole thing had been an elaborate trap!

03:09:18.960 --> 03:09:23.279
The humans at Base Gamma hadn’t survived
this long in the Backrooms by being stupid.

03:09:23.279 --> 03:09:27.960
The more technically savvy members had rewired
some of the hallways to channel the immense

03:09:27.960 --> 03:09:33.120
energy of the generators, and fry any unfortunate
entities that tried to use these hallways

03:09:33.120 --> 03:09:35.160
to break into Base Gamma.

03:09:35.160 --> 03:09:41.639
There was one big problem, though: SCP-682
wasn’t just any unfortunate entity.

03:09:41.640 --> 03:09:47.220
While it initially looked like the electrcity
might fry the beast, it gradually began channeling

03:09:47.220 --> 03:09:53.040
the electricity into its own body, and developing
the capacity to regift this electricity to

03:09:53.040 --> 03:09:55.859
the people who so kindly provided it.

03:09:55.859 --> 03:10:02.639
SCP-682, now a crackling conduit of electrcity,
leaped from the shocking hallway and into

03:10:02.640 --> 03:10:03.720
Base Gamma.

03:10:03.720 --> 03:10:08.760
Soon enough, it had fatally electrocuted all
300 members of the Major Explorer Group posted

03:10:08.760 --> 03:10:11.760
in Base Gamma, and returned to its baseline
state.

03:10:11.760 --> 03:10:17.040
Level 3 had grown tiresome now - It seemed
there were no more exciting new creatures

03:10:17.040 --> 03:10:17.880
to massacre.

03:10:17.880 --> 03:10:24.840
As a result, 682 slid into a nearby elevator,
and went down, where a new level awaited.

03:10:24.840 --> 03:10:28.620
This was how SCP-682 got to Level 4.

03:10:28.620 --> 03:10:32.460
And Level 4 was not what the Hard to Destroy
Reptile expected.

03:10:32.460 --> 03:10:37.260
In contrast to the industrial nightmare of
the previous few levels, Level 4 was like

03:10:37.260 --> 03:10:40.740
a limitless office block with all the furniture
ripped out.

03:10:40.740 --> 03:10:46.620
While for some this might represent the crushing,
existential banality of office life, and how

03:10:46.620 --> 03:10:52.439
the wheels of capitalism inevitably work us
to death, SCP-682 had never worked in an office

03:10:52.439 --> 03:10:57.540
before, so it didn’t really have the proper
cultural reference points to appreciate this

03:10:57.540 --> 03:10:59.279
more abstract kind of fear.

03:10:59.279 --> 03:11:01.439
It wanted monsters to kill!

03:11:01.439 --> 03:11:06.779
682 spent approximately six days searching
around the hellscape that is Level 4, not

03:11:06.779 --> 03:11:09.960
discovering a single person or entity while
it was there.

03:11:09.960 --> 03:11:14.700
It was honestly the most stressed that SCP-682
had felt since coming here.

03:11:14.700 --> 03:11:19.260
The beast was almost tempted to unscrew a
lightbulb from above, draw a little face on

03:11:19.260 --> 03:11:22.500
it, begin referring to it as “Wilson”,
and then kill it.

03:11:22.500 --> 03:11:28.740
682 felt the closest emotion it could manage
to immense gratitude when it sighted the glowing

03:11:28.740 --> 03:11:32.519
green of a distant exit sign at the end of
a long hallway.

03:11:32.520 --> 03:11:35.520
Finally, a way out onto another level!

03:11:35.520 --> 03:11:38.940
Hopefully this one would have more creatures
to slaughter…

03:11:38.939 --> 03:11:43.679
Welcome, SCP-682, to Level 5.

03:11:43.680 --> 03:11:49.020
SCP-682 didn’t really know what to expect
from the next level of the Backrooms - After

03:11:49.020 --> 03:11:53.460
all, it’d all seemed pretty random so far
- but it definitely didn’t expect to see

03:11:53.460 --> 03:11:56.939
a classy, well-appointed hotel on the other
end of that hallway.

03:11:56.939 --> 03:12:02.519
SCP-682 had never seen the Stanley Kubrik
Masterpiece, The Shining, nor read the book

03:12:02.520 --> 03:12:07.560
it was based on by Master of Horror Stephen
King, but if it had, it would probably have

03:12:07.560 --> 03:12:08.640
drawn the comparison.

03:12:08.640 --> 03:12:13.440
Instead, it was already busy tearing through
the ornate halls, looking for new prey to

03:12:13.439 --> 03:12:13.740
slaughter.

03:12:13.740 --> 03:12:18.479
The first unexpected encounter was with a
small cat that casually wandered out into

03:12:18.479 --> 03:12:20.099
the hallway, right in front of it.

03:12:20.100 --> 03:12:25.320
The cat, who didn’t seem threatened by SCP-682,
said, “Hi, I’m Samantha.

03:12:25.319 --> 03:12:26.819
You got any meat you can lend me?

03:12:26.819 --> 03:12:28.380
I’ll tell your fortune if you do.”

03:12:28.380 --> 03:12:31.440
SCP-682 was, frankly, baffled.

03:12:31.439 --> 03:12:33.599
It took a moment to formulate a reply.

03:12:33.600 --> 03:12:36.060
“You worthless creature.

03:12:36.060 --> 03:12:39.420
You have no idea what you’re dealing with,
do you?

03:12:39.420 --> 03:12:47.700
I’m going to bring this place to ruin, and
destroy all who reside within,” 682 said.

03:12:47.700 --> 03:12:49.620
“So no meat, then?”

03:12:49.620 --> 03:12:52.920
682 growled and swiped at the cat with its
claws.

03:12:52.920 --> 03:12:54.600
Luckily, she was able to dodge.

03:12:54.600 --> 03:13:00.000
The cat tutted and padded away into the darkness,
muttering, “Go bother the Beast instead.

03:13:00.000 --> 03:13:00.600
Jerk.”

03:13:00.600 --> 03:13:03.420
This piqued SCP-682’s interest.

03:13:03.420 --> 03:13:05.340
A Beast, you say?

03:13:05.340 --> 03:13:08.819
Sounds important, sounds powerful.

03:13:08.819 --> 03:13:11.639
Finally, a worthy opponent!

03:13:11.640 --> 03:13:14.701
Our battle shall be legendary!

03:13:14.700 --> 03:13:21.420
And with renewed vigor, SCP-682 began prowling
the halls of the Backrooms, searching for

03:13:21.420 --> 03:13:23.520
this “Beast” to defeat and destroy.

03:13:23.520 --> 03:13:26.820
But to begin with, things were grievously
disappointing.

03:13:26.819 --> 03:13:30.960
One of the first monsters on this opulent
hotel level that the Hard to Destroy Reptile

03:13:30.960 --> 03:13:36.180
faced were diminutive little rodents known
as Death Rats, which were effectively slightly

03:13:36.180 --> 03:13:38.701
larger than normal rats with little horns.

03:13:38.700 --> 03:13:45.359
SCP-682 stomped them all with ease, its thoughts
dripping with disdain for their truly pathetic

03:13:45.359 --> 03:13:45.839
weakness.

03:13:45.840 --> 03:13:50.100
What kind of a hotel allows itself to be filled
with rats?

03:13:50.100 --> 03:13:54.480
Even by human standards,&nbsp;
this would be disgraceful.

03:13:54.479 --> 03:14:01.859
Soon after, SCP-682 encountered a few familiar
foes: Female Death Moths and Hounds, all as

03:14:01.859 --> 03:14:03.359
easy to kill as they were before.

03:14:03.359 --> 03:14:09.299
SCP-682 didn’t understand: The feline promised
that there was a Beast down here.

03:14:09.300 --> 03:14:12.540
Was it hiding from the mighty reptile like
a filthy coward?

03:14:12.540 --> 03:14:14.160
Worthless!

03:14:14.160 --> 03:14:19.680
But it was in the depths of this cynicism
that SCP-682 encountered a Growler.

03:14:19.680 --> 03:14:25.020
First, it heard the sound of animalistic growling
projected directly into its mind, getting

03:14:25.020 --> 03:14:26.760
louder and louder by the moment.

03:14:26.760 --> 03:14:32.940
Then, as the growling grew in volume, 682
heard the thundrous footsteps of a huge quadruped

03:14:32.939 --> 03:14:33.899
getting closer.

03:14:33.899 --> 03:14:39.599
682 wondered, as the roaring became almost
deafening, whether this sound heralded the

03:14:39.600 --> 03:14:40.741
approach of the Beast.

03:14:40.740 --> 03:14:45.840
However, the second the monster actually turned
the corner and came into view, 682 had to

03:14:45.840 --> 03:14:47.279
suppress the urge to laugh.

03:14:47.279 --> 03:14:50.819
It was one of the more absurd things it’d
ever seen.

03:14:50.819 --> 03:14:57.599
It looked like a giant pile of pipe cleaners,
in every color imaginable, arranged into a

03:14:57.600 --> 03:14:59.220
vaguely four-legged structure.

03:14:59.220 --> 03:15:02.640
This was the monster producing all that psychic
racket?

03:15:02.640 --> 03:15:04.440
Pathetic!

03:15:04.439 --> 03:15:09.359
SCP-682 resolved, in that moment, to show
the monster how it was done.

03:15:09.359 --> 03:15:15.059
SCP-682 immediately evolved its own psychic
emission capacitors within its brain, and

03:15:15.060 --> 03:15:20.460
projected the message “YOU ARE A WORTHLESS
LITTLE CREATURE” directly into the simple

03:15:20.460 --> 03:15:21.660
mind of the Growler.

03:15:21.660 --> 03:15:26.399
It began to quake in horror at the booming
of 682’s voice in its brain.

03:15:26.399 --> 03:15:29.099
What was this terrifying new creature?

03:15:29.100 --> 03:15:30.480
It didn’t understand.

03:15:30.479 --> 03:15:36.599
And just like that, 682, who had grown bored
of this one-sided psychic battle, turned up

03:15:36.600 --> 03:15:40.020
the strength of the psychic beam by a factor
of fifty.

03:15:40.020 --> 03:15:44.520
The sudden psychic blast was so powerful that
the Growler collapsed to the ground and burst

03:15:44.520 --> 03:15:49.081
into flames, burning itself away into nothingness
in a matter of moments.

03:15:49.080 --> 03:15:52.500
Just as weak as 682 had expected.

03:15:52.500 --> 03:15:57.660
Hopefully, the Beast would provide a greater
challenge, because this was just getting sad.

03:15:57.660 --> 03:16:03.180
SCP-682 shook off the disappointment and continued
running through the halls of the hotel.

03:16:03.180 --> 03:16:07.620
Eventually, after passing through some dull
dance hall called “the Beverly Room”,

03:16:07.620 --> 03:16:11.760
682 found itself running through a hallway
full of long portraits.

03:16:11.760 --> 03:16:17.040
Every person in the portraits had a strange,
twisted grin on their face - Not that this

03:16:17.040 --> 03:16:19.500
even registered to SCP-682.

03:16:19.500 --> 03:16:24.600
What did occur to 682, though, was the figure
that suddenly materialized in the hallway

03:16:24.600 --> 03:16:25.500
in front of it.

03:16:25.500 --> 03:16:31.920
It was a strange figure, to be sure, an entity
in a suit, with a large, blue cuttlefish for

03:16:31.920 --> 03:16:32.340
a head.

03:16:32.340 --> 03:16:35.279
The creature cleared its throat and began
to speak.

03:16:35.279 --> 03:16:36.899
“Well hello there.

03:16:36.899 --> 03:16:38.700
You’re new here, aren’t you?

03:16:38.700 --> 03:16:41.519
Such an interesting creature.

03:16:41.520 --> 03:16:44.880
You’ve been making some trouble on the other
levels, haven’t you?

03:16:45.779 --> 03:16:47.340
Not that it’s any of my business.

03:16:47.340 --> 03:16:51.240
On the contrary, dear sir, I like the cut
of your jib.

03:16:51.240 --> 03:16:53.939
How would you feel about joining me in the
hotel business?

03:16:53.939 --> 03:16:57.839
It isn’t easy to manage this dimension by
myself, after all.

03:16:57.840 --> 03:17:02.040
How about you and I come to my office, we
can work out the terms of our--”

03:17:02.040 --> 03:17:07.680
682 lunged forward and unceremoniously devoured
the creature’s head, allowing its dapperly-dressed

03:17:07.680 --> 03:17:10.440
body to fall limply to the ground, dead.

03:17:10.439 --> 03:17:15.540
SCP-682 grunted, annoyed by the distraction
the creature had provided.

03:17:15.540 --> 03:17:18.180
682 had better things to do.

03:17:18.180 --> 03:17:21.840
This Beast has got to be around here somewhere…

03:17:21.840 --> 03:17:27.540
A group of well-armed Mobile Task Force members&nbsp;
entered the containment chamber, armed to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:17:27.540 --> 03:17:33.420
teeth. Some faced the ground, droplets of sweat&nbsp;
dripping onto their visors, some wore Dr. Dan’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:17:33.420 --> 03:17:39.480
infamous SCRAMBLE goggles, and one particularly&nbsp;
brave member of personnel wielded only a bag.&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:17:39.479 --> 03:17:44.160
The room they were currently standing in was&nbsp;
perhaps the most dangerous place in the world.

03:17:44.160 --> 03:17:45.000
Why?

03:17:45.000 --> 03:17:50.700
Because it contained two terrifying&nbsp;
titans of the anomalous world: SCP-682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:17:50.700 --> 03:17:57.960
the infinitely hateful Hard to Destroy Reptile,&nbsp;
and SCP-096, the Shy Guy, the ultimate mindless&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:17:57.960 --> 03:18:03.000
killing machine. And if the very idea of having&nbsp;
them in the same place doesn’t feel risky enough,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:03.000 --> 03:18:08.520
this deadly duo had just spent 27 hours in&nbsp;
one of the most brutal brawls imaginable.

03:18:08.520 --> 03:18:14.581
And incidentally, fights like this are exactly&nbsp;
why we’re here today. We cover a lot of SCPs on&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:14.580 --> 03:18:18.779
this channel, and we’ve seen the way some of the&nbsp;
more dangerous anomalies out there can tear their&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:18.779 --> 03:18:24.120
way through civilians and trained Foundation MTF&nbsp;
operatives with ease. But how do they fare against&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:24.120 --> 03:18:30.420
monsters, maniacs, and reality benders their own&nbsp;
size? With the help of the SCP Explained audience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:30.420 --> 03:18:35.700
we’re going to explore theoretical fights between&nbsp;
some of the anomalous world’s biggest badasses.

03:18:35.700 --> 03:18:40.979
And who better to get this show on the road than&nbsp;
two of the most iconic and deadly monsters that&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:40.979 --> 03:18:45.599
haunt the halls of a Foundation containment&nbsp;
site near you? The Hard to Destroy Reptile&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:45.600 --> 03:18:50.100
and the Shy Guy are household names for&nbsp;
anyone familiar with the SCP Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:50.100 --> 03:18:54.300
and before we get to the gruesome results&nbsp;
of their first fight - and your theories&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:54.300 --> 03:18:58.800
about how a potential rematch might play out&nbsp;
- let’s get to know the combat prowess of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:18:58.800 --> 03:19:03.600
pair of nasty customers. What kind of damage&nbsp;
are they capable of taking and inflicting?

03:19:03.600 --> 03:19:06.300
Spoiler Alert: It’s a hell of a lot.

03:19:06.300 --> 03:19:12.540
In this corner, we have SCP-682: A monster&nbsp;
whose ability to survive seemingly anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:12.540 --> 03:19:16.859
is only equaled by its terrible attitude&nbsp;
toward pretty much everyone and everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:16.859 --> 03:19:22.019
around it. Though to be fair, you’d probably&nbsp;
be a little grumpy too if the SCP Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:22.020 --> 03:19:25.980
was constantly trying to murder you in&nbsp;
different ways rather than just keeping&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:25.979 --> 03:19:31.319
you contained. 682’s basic offensive power&nbsp;
set involves impressive strength, speed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:31.319 --> 03:19:37.500
intelligence, and the aid of its deadly&nbsp;
fangs, claws, and tail. However, 682 is&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:37.500 --> 03:19:42.060
considerably stronger after it’s just survived&nbsp;
and regenerated from a termination attempt.

03:19:42.060 --> 03:19:49.560
That’s because the true combat asset of 682 is and&nbsp;
always has been its adaptability. Specifically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:49.560 --> 03:19:55.081
if some kind of attack brings 682 into a state&nbsp;
of near-death but doesn’t finish the job,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:55.080 --> 03:19:59.939
682 will generally either develop a&nbsp;
perfect defense or counter-offensive for&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:19:59.939 --> 03:20:04.259
that attack or somehow add a version&nbsp;
of the attack to its own arsenal.

03:20:04.260 --> 03:20:08.940
This has ranged from super-pressurized jets&nbsp;
of its own blood, dangerously radioactive&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:20:08.939 --> 03:20:14.639
banana beams fired out of its mouth, and even&nbsp;
an incapacitating laugher blast gained from an&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:20:14.640 --> 03:20:20.100
encounter with the adorable SCP-999.&nbsp;
It’s an absolute swiss army knife of&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:20:20.100 --> 03:20:24.420
dangerous anomalous powers and abilities -&nbsp;
And if you need any further proof of that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:20:24.420 --> 03:20:29.580
check out our multiple videos on all the ludicrous&nbsp;
failed attempts to kill this nightmare lizard.

03:20:29.580 --> 03:20:36.300
And in this corner, we’ve got SCP-096, the&nbsp;
Shy Guy. While 682 is freakishly adaptable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:20:36.300 --> 03:20:42.600
in most situations, SCP-096 is pretty much&nbsp;
unstoppable. This long, gangly creep will&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:20:42.600 --> 03:20:48.300
murder anyone who sees even the tiniest glimpse&nbsp;
of its face with such ferocity that not even a&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:20:48.300 --> 03:20:53.040
trace of the body will remain. It does this&nbsp;
by entering what many call its “Rage State”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:20:53.040 --> 03:20:58.439
activated by the sudden immense distress of&nbsp;
its face being seen. When it enters this state,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:20:58.439 --> 03:21:04.019
the SCP Foundation has only one prerogative:&nbsp;
Get themselves and anyone else out of its way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:21:04.020 --> 03:21:07.560
because you will not stop this&nbsp;
thing until it’s killed its target.

03:21:07.560 --> 03:21:13.320
All the SCP Foundation has ever been able to do is&nbsp;
wait until after the target has been obliterated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:21:13.319 --> 03:21:19.200
and then come in to bag its head when it enters&nbsp;
its docile state. Almost nothing else has even&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:21:19.200 --> 03:21:23.639
successfully slowed it down. While they&nbsp;
have been capable of damaging its flesh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:21:23.640 --> 03:21:28.440
the monster’s skeleton seems to be utterly&nbsp;
indestructible, and its damaged flesh has&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:21:28.439 --> 03:21:33.120
proven consistently able to grow back. The&nbsp;
monster seems to be immune to everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:21:33.120 --> 03:21:38.640
from pain to cold, and moves at such a speed that&nbsp;
it’s pretty much impossible to escape for long.

03:21:38.640 --> 03:21:43.320
So when you factor in an indestructible&nbsp;
body, immense strength, immense speed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:21:43.319 --> 03:21:49.500
and an unstoppable urge to kill anyone who sees&nbsp;
its face, you’re looking at a formidable opponent.

03:21:49.500 --> 03:21:54.720
It’s only natural that the Foundation would&nbsp;
want to use 096 in their 682 cross tests,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:21:54.720 --> 03:21:59.280
so what exactly happened when the Mobile Task&nbsp;
Force entered the room after their first epic&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:21:59.279 --> 03:22:02.819
battle? What did they find inside&nbsp;
the chamber in the grisly aftermath?

03:22:02.819 --> 03:22:10.259
SCP-096 lay crumpled in the corner, wheezing,&nbsp;
scarred, covered in its own blood. SCP-682 was&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:22:10.260 --> 03:22:15.060
barely recognizable - SCP-096 had reduced&nbsp;
it to a quarter of its original size,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:22:15.060 --> 03:22:21.300
the rest having been utterly torn to shreds. Both&nbsp;
had narrowly survived the encounter, but it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:22:21.300 --> 03:22:27.900
an epic battle neither of them would ever forget&nbsp;
- Though this was especially true for SCP-096.

03:22:27.899 --> 03:22:33.899
You see, as we alluded to earlier, SCP-682&nbsp;
is used to taking a kicking at this point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:22:33.899 --> 03:22:38.279
It hasn’t ever truly been killed,&nbsp;
but it’s been beaten, eaten, burned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:22:38.279 --> 03:22:43.259
zapped, and smashed within an inch of its&nbsp;
life more times than you can count. 096,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:22:43.260 --> 03:22:47.520
on the other hand, was not used to not&nbsp;
being able to utterly eliminate its&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:22:47.520 --> 03:22:52.860
prey. While it’s impossible to speculate&nbsp;
what’s going on inside SCP-096’s mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:22:52.859 --> 03:22:59.460
all evidence points towards getting a draw in this&nbsp;
battle, seriously damaging SCP-096’s confidence.

03:22:59.460 --> 03:23:05.460
Now, every time Foundation personnel tries&nbsp;
to bring 096 into 682’s containment chamber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:23:05.460 --> 03:23:12.420
he begins crying and scratching at his own face.&nbsp;
Why? Is he scared of 682? Is he humiliated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:23:12.420 --> 03:23:18.060
thinking of the fight he wasn’t able to win?&nbsp;
Or is the very idea of someone seeing his face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:23:18.060 --> 03:23:24.060
and him not being able to immediately kill them,&nbsp;
just too unbearably stressful? Seeing as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:23:24.060 --> 03:23:28.860
Shy Guy’s mouth is only good for two things -&nbsp;
and neither of them are talking - we’ll never&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:23:28.859 --> 03:23:33.839
truly know. But either way, it’s clear&nbsp;
that 096 has no interest in a rematch…

03:23:33.840 --> 03:23:36.779
...But what if that changed?

03:23:36.779 --> 03:23:42.660
What if 096 realized that it was wasting&nbsp;
its potential. It managed to get SCP-682&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:23:42.660 --> 03:23:46.739
three-quarters of the way to death last time,&nbsp;
what could stop it from getting that last&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:23:46.739 --> 03:23:52.559
quarter? Sure, nothing has ever killed SCP-682&nbsp;
before, but there’s a first time for everything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:23:52.560 --> 03:23:56.040
right? Maybe 096 would have a&nbsp;
Rocky-style training montage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:23:56.040 --> 03:24:01.019
where he rebuilds his confidence and becomes&nbsp;
the underdog he was always meant to be. He’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:24:01.020 --> 03:24:05.220
walk right up to that big, nasty reptile,&nbsp;
and give him the rematch of the century.

03:24:05.220 --> 03:24:06.660
What would happen then?

03:24:06.660 --> 03:24:13.080
Now, we give the floor to you, the loyal viewers&nbsp;
of SCP Explained. Here are some of your thoughts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:24:13.080 --> 03:24:17.580
theories, and opinions on a potential&nbsp;
historic rematch between these two creeps.

03:24:17.580 --> 03:24:20.460
Let’s get ready to rumble!

03:24:25.979 --> 03:24:31.019
PinguWithAnAxe said, “If 682's adaptability&nbsp;
is based around his ability to develop&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:24:31.020 --> 03:24:35.340
countermeasures to any damage inflicted&nbsp;
(or in the case of 173, a countermeasure&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:24:35.340 --> 03:24:40.440
to the cause of said damage) I imagine 682&nbsp;
would turn his skin entirely reflective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:24:40.439 --> 03:24:45.000
causing 096 to see his own face and the&nbsp;
feedback loop would break his mind.”

03:24:45.840 --> 03:24:51.900
Interesting. Whether this would work is all&nbsp;
dependent on whether SCP-096 can actually see,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:24:51.899 --> 03:24:56.460
or if it is merely capable of psychically&nbsp;
intuiting when someone else sees its face.&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:24:56.460 --> 03:25:02.819
If the latter is true, then this particular&nbsp;
adaptation wouldn’t do much good for SCP-682.

03:25:02.819 --> 03:25:07.139
Random User said, “If this is after&nbsp;
their first cross test and they were&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:25:07.140 --> 03:25:09.960
forced to interact again, they&nbsp;
wouldn’t attempt to fight each&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:25:09.960 --> 03:25:13.620
other. I feel like they’d form a truce&nbsp;
and take out the researchers on-site.”

03:25:14.279 --> 03:25:19.559
This would be one of the worst-case scenarios.&nbsp;
Whether even the SCP Foundation could handle&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:25:19.560 --> 03:25:25.020
a simultaneous 682 and 096 breach without&nbsp;
bringing in Hammer Down is an open question.

03:25:25.020 --> 03:25:31.020
Ramon Voncken said, “Simple, after the first&nbsp;
encounter, when 096 stopped attacking 682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:25:31.020 --> 03:25:35.100
682 will grow eyes that filter&nbsp;
out 096s face the next time.”

03:25:35.100 --> 03:25:39.600
Organic SCRAMBLE goggles. Dr. Dan&nbsp;
would be fuming with jealousy.

03:25:39.600 --> 03:25:44.280
Koopsader said, “I really want&nbsp;
SCP-096 to win so I’m sending&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:25:44.279 --> 03:25:48.420
him a blind personal trainer so he&nbsp;
can beat the snot out of SCP-682.”

03:25:48.420 --> 03:25:55.260
This is exactly the kind of help SCP-096 needs.&nbsp;
He’s got the rage, endurance, and strength, with&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:25:55.260 --> 03:25:59.880
a little help getting his form and technique in&nbsp;
order, he’d be an even more formidable opponent.

03:25:59.880 --> 03:26:05.040
Kytoe Ryu said, “I'd like to imagine&nbsp;
096, after playing with 682 for so long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:26:05.040 --> 03:26:11.460
would try to eat 682 in a vain attempt to kill&nbsp;
it, only to gain 682’s abilities, and vice versa.”

03:26:11.460 --> 03:26:17.100
Either of these options would be&nbsp;
horrifying. SCP-096 with 682’s abilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:26:17.100 --> 03:26:23.040
or 682 with 096’s abilities, would likely&nbsp;
be a truly perfect killing machine.

03:26:24.840 --> 03:26:28.319
Autumn said, “What If they just shared a&nbsp;
nice cold drink while playing Mario Kart?&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:26:28.319 --> 03:26:31.679
I’m sure 096 would be the white&nbsp;
shy guy character in every race.”

03:26:31.680 --> 03:26:35.701
Personally, we love this idea, and&nbsp;
we think SCP-682 would go for Bowser.

03:26:37.620 --> 03:26:42.239
Ibraheem Temur said, “682 would win&nbsp;
eventually. It’s way more intelligent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:26:42.239 --> 03:26:46.979
adaptive, and overall malicious&nbsp;
while 096 acts just on instinct.”

03:26:46.979 --> 03:26:52.739
This is an undeniably good point. What 682&nbsp;
lacks in sheer savagery, it makes up for in&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:26:52.739 --> 03:26:57.179
its ruthless, calculating intelligence.&nbsp;
Could this give it the edge over 096?

03:26:57.180 --> 03:27:01.320
Monomoy Mukherjee said, “That fight&nbsp;
will be interesting because both of&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:27:01.319 --> 03:27:03.840
them now know how they attack&nbsp;
and what their attacks are.”

03:27:03.840 --> 03:27:09.420
Nice segue. Due to the relatively mindless&nbsp;
nature of 096, as far as we’re aware,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:27:09.420 --> 03:27:13.859
it’s probably unable to learn&nbsp;
from experience. 682, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:27:13.859 --> 03:27:17.759
would have the advantage of knowing&nbsp;
how 096 operates in the second battle.

03:27:17.760 --> 03:27:21.660
Devan Smith said, “As much as I'd&nbsp;
like to see how this would play out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:27:21.660 --> 03:27:27.599
I imagine 096 can't manage more than other&nbsp;
SCP's have in the past. Not to downplay him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:27:27.600 --> 03:27:31.080
but he might need some extra friends&nbsp;
to do a whole lot more damage.”

03:27:31.080 --> 03:27:36.059
It’s undeniable that going in with tag team&nbsp;
partners would better 096’s chances of taking&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:27:36.060 --> 03:27:42.180
the lizard down. However, due to SCP-096’s&nbsp;
shyness, and tendency to kill everyone and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:27:42.180 --> 03:27:46.740
everything that looks at him, he doesn’t&nbsp;
have many friends looking to volunteer.

03:27:46.739 --> 03:27:51.599
Nyan Tails said, “096 will cry in the&nbsp;
corner while 682 starts attacking it&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:27:51.600 --> 03:27:55.740
eventually it gets confused that 096&nbsp;
isn't fighting back after an hour and&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:27:55.739 --> 03:27:58.319
begins to adapt to it and becomes docile forever.”

03:27:58.979 --> 03:28:04.080
Look, while it’s unlikely that this would&nbsp;
happen, it’s certainly nice to imagine, isn’t it?

03:28:04.080 --> 03:28:08.100
Adam Britton said, “Narratively it&nbsp;
needs to conclude with a reason to&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:28:08.100 --> 03:28:12.661
never try it again. So I'm going to say&nbsp;
that 682 will telepathically project the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:28:12.660 --> 03:28:16.739
image of 096 into the site staff&nbsp;
or the entire human pychospace.”

03:28:16.739 --> 03:28:22.260
Yikes. This is a possibility&nbsp;
so terrifying - And honestly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:28:22.260 --> 03:28:26.400
plausible - that it’s making us regret&nbsp;
wanting to see this rematch altogether.

03:28:26.399 --> 03:28:31.259
Chaos Insurgency said, “I think 682 would just&nbsp;
think "For damn’s sake, just leave me alone!"

03:28:31.260 --> 03:28:35.820
Given he’s been through more termination&nbsp;
attempts than SCP-5031 can count on&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:28:35.819 --> 03:28:39.059
its fingers, who could blame him&nbsp;
for getting a little frustrated?

03:28:39.060 --> 03:28:44.581
Michael Porter said, “I think that 682 and 096&nbsp;
would take each other to court for aggravated&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:28:44.580 --> 03:28:49.380
assault against the other. Either one of them will&nbsp;
get sentenced to death and will unsurprisingly not&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:28:49.380 --> 03:28:54.239
die or the 2 team up to kill the entire courtroom&nbsp;
and they walk out as a new serial killing team.”

03:28:54.239 --> 03:28:57.840
The real question is what kind of lawyers&nbsp;
would represent a pair of murderous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:28:57.840 --> 03:29:00.600
anomalous monsters in court. Better call Saul.

03:29:00.600 --> 03:29:04.320
Ari Wertman said, “Maybe if we&nbsp;
try being nice to them for once,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:04.319 --> 03:29:08.700
we can offer them a cup of tea and&nbsp;
get them both a therapist. 682 will&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:08.700 --> 03:29:12.300
talk all his hate away and then realize&nbsp;
his wrongdoing and become an activist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:12.300 --> 03:29:17.700
and 096 would become very confident about his&nbsp;
face and become a model. There problem solved.”

03:29:17.700 --> 03:29:21.479
Hey, when people strive towards&nbsp;
self-improvement, we’re all winners.

03:29:21.479 --> 03:29:28.139
But we don’t know if we can say the same for 682&nbsp;
and 096. Even if this rematch ever did happen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:28.140 --> 03:29:33.000
perhaps it’d just be another draw - An&nbsp;
unstoppable force against an immovable&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:33.000 --> 03:29:37.920
object. But other match-ups may be more&nbsp;
clear-cut. What kind of Vs battles would&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:37.920 --> 03:29:42.239
you like to see us cover in the future? What&nbsp;
SCPs would you really love to see duke it out?

03:29:42.239 --> 03:29:46.080
Let us know in the comments, and&nbsp;
keep an eye on the community posts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:29:46.080 --> 03:29:50.040
in order to throw in your anomalous&nbsp;
two cents for our next Vs battle!

03:29:50.040 --> 03:29:56.460
The military helicopter sailed through the
skies at a steady pace, its destination somewhere

03:29:56.460 --> 03:30:02.760
in Southwest Asia, along one of the many points
where the legendary Euphrates and Tigris rivers

03:30:02.760 --> 03:30:02.940
meet.

03:30:02.939 --> 03:30:08.639
Depending on the outcome, this mission may
have changed the course of the SCP Foundation

03:30:08.640 --> 03:30:12.720
and its activities forever, or it might do
nothing at all.

03:30:12.720 --> 03:30:17.940
Such was often the way when it came to dealing
with the unpredictable and the anomalous.

03:30:17.939 --> 03:30:23.819
Inside the helicopter, Dr. Anton Zharkov was
practically rattling with nervous excitement.

03:30:23.819 --> 03:30:29.519
Ever since he’d been assigned to the 682
Termination Detail, after years of wasting

03:30:29.520 --> 03:30:34.140
away in an archival desk job, he’d seen
the kind of anomalies you wouldn’t believe.

03:30:34.140 --> 03:30:39.960
173, that nightmarish statue that snaps the
necks of anyone who dared to look away from

03:30:39.960 --> 03:30:40.080
it.

03:30:40.080 --> 03:30:46.559
811, the strange and also strangely adorable
Swamp Woman, whose caustic mucus could reliably

03:30:46.560 --> 03:30:51.600
melt seemingly any organic matter - save,
of course, 682 itself.

03:30:51.600 --> 03:30:56.580
And Dr. Zharkov was particularly astonished
by the aftermath of the epic battle between

03:30:56.580 --> 03:31:01.380
096 and 682 , which left both&nbsp;
of these “indestructible”&nbsp;

03:31:01.380 --> 03:31:03.359
monsters horribly maimed.

03:31:03.359 --> 03:31:04.380
But all of that...

03:31:04.380 --> 03:31:08.040
It was nothing compared to what they were
going to witness today.

03:31:08.040 --> 03:31:12.120
Dr. Zharkov muttered a prayer to himself in
frightened reverence.

03:31:12.120 --> 03:31:16.559
Dr. Clef, who was sitting across from him
in the helicopter, wasn’t quite as wound

03:31:16.560 --> 03:31:16.800
up.

03:31:16.800 --> 03:31:22.320
Like some action movie cliche made manifest,
he sliced chunks from a plump, red apple with

03:31:22.319 --> 03:31:25.139
a Bowie knife and sucked the pieces off the
blade.

03:31:25.140 --> 03:31:28.500
Clef found Zharkov’s nervousness little
more than amusing.

03:31:28.500 --> 03:31:30.720
“First time at Site 0, rookie?”

03:31:30.720 --> 03:31:32.460
Clef asked between apple slices.

03:31:32.460 --> 03:31:35.460
Dr. Zharkov nodded, forcing a meek smile.

03:31:35.460 --> 03:31:36.720
Clef just chuckled.

03:31:38.520 --> 03:31:40.621
“You’re wasting your time, you know,”
Clef said.

03:31:40.620 --> 03:31:42.660
“Everyone takes a shot at the reptile.

03:31:42.660 --> 03:31:47.040
I faced it down myself once, mano e mano,
and during that moment, I realized something.

03:31:47.040 --> 03:31:51.300
As much as it pains me to ever throw in the
towel, we’re not gonna kill this thing.

03:31:51.300 --> 03:31:53.100
It’s just a budget sink.”

03:31:53.100 --> 03:31:57.060
Of course, these kinds of doubts had crossed
Dr. Zharkov’s mind before.

03:31:57.060 --> 03:32:01.920
He’d watched countless termination attempts,
organized by far more senior researchers than

03:32:01.920 --> 03:32:04.620
himself, fail and fail embarrassingly.

03:32:04.620 --> 03:32:10.019
Something about signing your name up for 682
termination was like tying on a blindfold,

03:32:10.020 --> 03:32:15.840
grabbing a bat, and stepping up to a piñata,
except in this case, the piñata isn’t wearing

03:32:15.840 --> 03:32:19.020
a blindfold, and somehow it can hit you back.

03:32:19.020 --> 03:32:24.720
It’s a one-way ticket to professional humiliation,
and if you’re unlucky enough to get too

03:32:24.720 --> 03:32:28.260
close when things go south, it can be so much
worse.

03:32:28.260 --> 03:32:33.900
But Dr. Zharkov well and truly believed that
he would be the exception to so much miserable

03:32:33.899 --> 03:32:34.439
failure.

03:32:34.439 --> 03:32:38.639
After all, this was an idea nobody had tried
before...

03:32:38.640 --> 03:32:43.380
An announcement over the intercom signaled
that they had now entered Site 0 airspace.

03:32:43.380 --> 03:32:44.880
They’d be landing shortly.

03:32:44.880 --> 03:32:50.220
And just like that, Dr. Zharkov was all raised
hairs and gooseflesh once again.

03:32:50.220 --> 03:32:55.320
It seemed like such a hazy, distant miracle
that his project proposal would even get majority

03:32:55.319 --> 03:32:57.059
approval from the O5 Council.

03:32:57.060 --> 03:33:00.960
And now, he was about to touch down and actually
see it.

03:33:00.960 --> 03:33:06.000
Naturally, Dr. Clef noticed Dr. Zharkov’s
emotional cues, and like so many playground

03:33:06.000 --> 03:33:08.160
bullies, decided to seize on it.

03:33:08.160 --> 03:33:11.099
“Don’t buy into the hype,” Dr. Clef
said.

03:33:11.100 --> 03:33:12.900
“It’s really not that special.”

03:33:12.899 --> 03:33:14.700
The helicopter touched down.

03:33:14.700 --> 03:33:20.160
Dr. Zharkov felt defensive, he was almost
tempted to use hard words, but he realized

03:33:20.160 --> 03:33:25.380
from Dr. Clef’s mischievous smile that perhaps
that was always the intention.

03:33:25.380 --> 03:33:27.480
He certainly had a...

03:33:27.479 --> 03:33:32.399
Reputation, if one were to put it in the most
neutral terms possible.

03:33:32.399 --> 03:33:37.019
“But this was your 001 proposal, Dr. Clef,”
Zharkov countered.

03:33:37.020 --> 03:33:39.780
“I would have thought you’d be more invested
in this.”

03:33:39.779 --> 03:33:44.639
Dr. Clef rose to his feet and sheathed his
Bowie knife as the helicopter’s side door

03:33:44.640 --> 03:33:45.240
opened.

03:33:45.239 --> 03:33:49.739
He gestured for Dr. Zharkov to get up and
follow him, before saying, “Believe me,

03:33:49.739 --> 03:33:55.319
even a giant flaming Demi-God loses its luster
when you need to write enough of those stupid

03:33:55.319 --> 03:33:56.399
reports on it.”

03:33:56.399 --> 03:33:59.040
The two researchers&nbsp;
disembarked from the helicopter&nbsp;

03:33:59.040 --> 03:34:01.739
and walked into the legendary containment

03:34:01.739 --> 03:34:04.019
facility: Site 0.

03:34:04.020 --> 03:34:06.661
One of the most important&nbsp;
and secretive containment&nbsp;

03:34:06.660 --> 03:34:09.300
sites out there, even by the standards of

03:34:09.300 --> 03:34:11.880
the ever-clandestine SCP Foundation.

03:34:11.880 --> 03:34:16.620
If ever containment procedures failed here,
they’d be staring down the barrel of an

03:34:16.620 --> 03:34:22.019
unprecedented situation: A PATMOS XK-Class
End of the World Scenario.

03:34:22.020 --> 03:34:27.240
After all, they were dealing with one of the
most serious and powerful anomalies they’d

03:34:27.239 --> 03:34:28.260
ever contained here.

03:34:28.260 --> 03:34:33.120
Clef and Zharkov entered the control room,
filled with huge monitors displaying every

03:34:33.120 --> 03:34:37.920
kind of recordable metric, but the largest
screens were dominated by long-range drone

03:34:37.920 --> 03:34:44.520
footage of the iconic anomaly they were all
there to see: SCP-001, perhaps better known

03:34:44.520 --> 03:34:46.860
as Uriel, The Gate Guardian.

03:34:46.859 --> 03:34:52.200
While Dr. Clef remained unfazed, Dr. Zharkov
felt a single tear crawling down his cheek.

03:34:52.200 --> 03:34:55.859
He had never seen an entity&nbsp;
so utterly awe-inspiring.

03:34:55.859 --> 03:35:01.080
An impossibly tall, glowing humanoid entity
with eight great, fiery wings, and a glowing

03:35:01.080 --> 03:35:05.040
blade made of pure heavenly fire, every bit
as hot as the sun.

03:35:05.040 --> 03:35:09.600
To think that such an incredible creature
existed on the same earth as him made him

03:35:09.600 --> 03:35:11.460
feel so incredibly small.

03:35:11.460 --> 03:35:16.260
The theories as to the creature’s true nature
were as myriad as they were unknowable.

03:35:16.260 --> 03:35:21.480
Some of the more devout among the Foundation’s
ranks even believe that he is a direct servant

03:35:21.479 --> 03:35:28.139
of the Abrahamic God, guarding the gate the
paradise, the Garden of Eden, Heaven itself.

03:35:28.140 --> 03:35:30.180
Dr. Clef just laughed.

03:35:30.180 --> 03:35:33.780
“Everything you hoped it’d be, Zharkov?”
he said.

03:35:33.779 --> 03:35:35.279
Dr. Zharkov nodded.

03:35:35.279 --> 03:35:37.679
“And more, Dr. Clef, and more.”

03:35:37.680 --> 03:35:43.140
Even from such a distance, the raw power of
the Gate Guardian is impossible to ignore.

03:35:43.140 --> 03:35:46.500
It radiates off of the being like an invisible
aura.

03:35:46.500 --> 03:35:51.300
Dr. Zharkov had read all the files, to get
within a kilometer of the mighty entity would

03:35:51.300 --> 03:35:52.440
be to court death.

03:35:52.439 --> 03:35:57.960
Anyone who approached it would taste the heat
of its sword, cleaving them apart at the atomic

03:35:57.960 --> 03:36:00.840
level and effectively erasing them from existence.

03:36:00.840 --> 03:36:07.140
It’s about as dead as anyone could possibly
be - Save for someone being thrown into SCP-3930

03:36:07.140 --> 03:36:10.140
and literally removed from the plane of existence.

03:36:10.140 --> 03:36:14.400
SCP-3930 had failed to annihilate the Hard
to Destroy Reptile.

03:36:14.399 --> 03:36:20.160
But perhaps where that whole lot of nothing
had failed, the Gate Guardian would succeed.

03:36:20.160 --> 03:36:25.260
It remained floating, fixed on one place,
as though waiting for…

03:36:25.260 --> 03:36:26.160
Something.

03:36:26.160 --> 03:36:27.180
But what?

03:36:27.180 --> 03:36:32.820
Perhaps a fateful confrontation with a certain
reptilian nightmare, Dr. Zharkov hoped.

03:36:32.819 --> 03:36:38.399
Like many, he had heard the most famous story
involving SCP-001: The Gate Guardian, which

03:36:38.399 --> 03:36:41.460
took place before even the days of the SCP
Foundation.

03:36:41.460 --> 03:36:45.420
After all, every Foundation needs a Founder,
doesn’t it?

03:36:45.420 --> 03:36:46.980
And that’s how it began.

03:36:46.979 --> 03:36:50.639
The Founder was a mysterious figure, no matter
who you ask.

03:36:50.640 --> 03:36:55.080
Some say it was O5-1, others say it was the
legendary Administrator.

03:36:55.080 --> 03:37:01.859
Some even believe that it was someone else,
someone older, someone who predated even the

03:37:01.859 --> 03:37:04.319
current O5 Council and Administrator.

03:37:04.319 --> 03:37:10.080
A wise and learned figure, going on a pilgrimage
around the known world in hopes of expanding

03:37:10.080 --> 03:37:13.200
their perspective and seeking out the strange
and unusual.

03:37:13.200 --> 03:37:17.580
It was traveling down the River Tigris that
the Founder encountered the Gate Guardian

03:37:17.580 --> 03:37:20.460
- Of course, as always, from a mile away.

03:37:20.460 --> 03:37:24.600
The Founder saw the distant glowing point
shaped like a human being with wings.

03:37:24.600 --> 03:37:28.080
It was unlike anything they’d ever borne
witness to.

03:37:28.080 --> 03:37:33.180
That’s when the Founder felt a door open
in the back of their mind, and something sneak

03:37:33.180 --> 03:37:33.420
in.

03:37:33.420 --> 03:37:37.500
A single word, projecting somehow infinite
authority.

03:37:39.140 --> 03:37:40.140
“PREPARE.”

03:37:40.140 --> 03:37:43.380
The very presence of the word made the Founder’s
body rattle.

03:37:43.380 --> 03:37:47.940
Never had they heard such a voice, conveying
such certainty and power.

03:37:47.939 --> 03:37:52.859
It had to be the voice of the distant glowing
figure, it couldn’t be anything else, could

03:37:52.859 --> 03:37:53.040
it?

03:37:53.040 --> 03:37:58.560
Much like Dr. Zharkov would experience hundreds
of years later, the Founder, even as a person

03:37:58.560 --> 03:38:04.500
so powerful, knowledgeable, and influential,
suddenly felt so unimaginably small.

03:38:04.500 --> 03:38:10.260
The Founder became aware of not just the extent
of the world around them, or even the universe,

03:38:10.260 --> 03:38:13.200
but a terrifying multiverse of possibilities.

03:38:13.200 --> 03:38:17.160
There was light out there, of course, but
even more darkness.

03:38:17.160 --> 03:38:20.460
And terrifying things were hiding in the dark.

03:38:20.460 --> 03:38:22.560
Is that what “prepare” meant?

03:38:22.560 --> 03:38:26.940
Did it mean to be ready for all the terrible
things hiding in the dark, just waiting for

03:38:26.939 --> 03:38:28.439
the opportunity to strike?

03:38:28.439 --> 03:38:33.059
Just how great was the extent of the things
humanity didn’t understand out there?

03:38:33.060 --> 03:38:38.820
The Founder’s mind was flooded with so many
possibilities - If there was a tide of monsters

03:38:38.819 --> 03:38:43.920
in the blackness that needed to be fought
back, it was too much for any one person to

03:38:43.920 --> 03:38:44.640
ever handle.

03:38:44.640 --> 03:38:50.940
The Founder needed a group, all gathered around
the same mission: To contain the coming threat

03:38:50.939 --> 03:38:53.519
that the great glowing being had warned them
about.

03:38:53.520 --> 03:38:57.420
People of focus, commitment, and sheer willpower.

03:38:57.420 --> 03:39:02.160
People who would accept the knowledge of the
terrible things in the darkness and still

03:39:02.160 --> 03:39:05.279
not waver in the face of their great and noble
challenge.

03:39:05.279 --> 03:39:11.099
People who, if necessary, would be willing
to die in the dark so the rest of the human

03:39:11.100 --> 03:39:12.960
race would live in the light.

03:39:12.960 --> 03:39:19.560
They would be humanity’s greatest defenders,
even though they would defend in secret.

03:39:19.560 --> 03:39:22.860
This was how it had all begun, supposedly.

03:39:22.859 --> 03:39:27.719
Dr. Zharkov had heard the story whispered
many times while conducting his research into

03:39:27.720 --> 03:39:29.340
SCP-001.

03:39:29.340 --> 03:39:34.739
And now, here he stood, perhaps where the
Founder had been standing all those years

03:39:34.739 --> 03:39:35.099
ago.

03:39:35.100 --> 03:39:42.060
The SCP Foundation had faced down greater
threats than SCP-682 - The Hanged King, The

03:39:42.060 --> 03:39:46.800
Sealed King, The Scarlet King, hell, if they
wanted to, they could go toe to toe with the

03:39:46.800 --> 03:39:47.279
Burger King.

03:39:47.279 --> 03:39:52.319
And all of it had begun with a single word
from the mighty Gate Guardian.

03:39:52.319 --> 03:39:56.399
Surely an ornery, overgrown lizard wouldn’t
be too much for it to handle?

03:39:56.399 --> 03:40:00.599
But of course, they hadn’t just come here
to look at the Gate Guardian, that’d be

03:40:00.600 --> 03:40:03.420
an egregious waste of time and helicopter
fuel.

03:40:03.420 --> 03:40:10.560
They’d come here transporting precious cargo:
A chunk of SCP-682’s flesh, cut from the

03:40:10.560 --> 03:40:11.400
beast itself.

03:40:11.399 --> 03:40:16.200
Currently, it was attached to yet another
remote-controlled drone, set on a collision

03:40:16.200 --> 03:40:17.519
course for the Gate Guardian.

03:40:17.520 --> 03:40:23.280
Dr. Zharkov watched the video feeds with sweaty
palms as he saw the drone and its diabolical

03:40:23.279 --> 03:40:27.960
cargo enter the video’s view, getting closer
to the Gate Guardian by the moment.

03:40:27.960 --> 03:40:29.819
Closer, closer, closer.

03:40:29.819 --> 03:40:30.599
Until…

03:40:30.600 --> 03:40:33.960
The Gate Guardian struck out with its great
and terrible sword.

03:40:33.960 --> 03:40:39.300
For such an astronomically huge being to move
so incredibly fast was astounding in and of

03:40:39.300 --> 03:40:45.239
itself, but what Dr. Zharkov found even more
exciting was the result: In one quick slash

03:40:45.239 --> 03:40:52.019
of its solar blade, both the drone and the
SCP-682 tissue sample were utterly evaporated.

03:40:52.020 --> 03:40:55.680
Gone, reduced to less than even ash.

03:40:55.680 --> 03:40:59.040
Dr. Zharkov’s face split into a manic grin.

03:40:59.040 --> 03:41:04.621
If it could destroy the tissue sample, then
surely, it could destroy the monster itself,

03:41:04.620 --> 03:41:07.559
and what a glorious day that would be…

03:41:07.560 --> 03:41:14.460
Meanwhile, back at the cross-testing chambers
of Site-19, SCP-682 was having another miserable

03:41:14.460 --> 03:41:14.760
day.

03:41:14.760 --> 03:41:19.500
It was dragged, half-melted, out of its acid
tank at 3 AM in the morning and left slowly

03:41:19.500 --> 03:41:20.580
regenerating on the floor.

03:41:20.580 --> 03:41:24.600
A typical SCP Foundation wake-up call, it&nbsp;

03:41:24.600 --> 03:41:27.480
thought to itself with a roll&nbsp;
of its still-regenerating

03:41:27.479 --> 03:41:27.839
eyes.

03:41:27.840 --> 03:41:31.860
What form of horrible torment would be in
store for it this time?

03:41:31.859 --> 03:41:37.139
It began scrolling through its mental Rolodex
for the most recent failed-but-painful termination

03:41:37.140 --> 03:41:37.740
attempts.

03:41:37.739 --> 03:41:42.239
Oh, yes, of course, they’d tried suffocation
via vacuum!

03:41:42.239 --> 03:41:46.739
That definitely made SCP-682 feel a little
light-headed, at least.

03:41:46.739 --> 03:41:51.599
Until, of course, it adapted its body to begin
releasing a gas of similar composition to

03:41:51.600 --> 03:41:56.820
its native atmosphere, which had certainly
given those white-coat-wearing sadists a lot

03:41:56.819 --> 03:41:57.660
to take notes about.

03:41:57.660 --> 03:42:00.239
Then, how could it forget, they’d tried&nbsp;

03:42:00.239 --> 03:42:02.880
roasting it to death with&nbsp;
extremely high temperatures.

03:42:02.880 --> 03:42:08.160
Thankfully, as always, it’d had a trick
up its sleeve: Adapting a carapace made of

03:42:08.160 --> 03:42:13.019
solid helium to defend it from the fire, then
shattering it to shred a bunch of those buffoons

03:42:13.020 --> 03:42:14.581
in the orange jumpsuits.

03:42:14.580 --> 03:42:19.200
Then they’d cut off a sample of its flesh
shoved it into some absurd industrial blender

03:42:19.200 --> 03:42:21.899
before shoving what’s left into a centrifuge.

03:42:21.899 --> 03:42:27.540
What a divine pleasure it had been for 682
to hear the explosion down the hall, when

03:42:27.540 --> 03:42:31.800
the antimatter embedded in its jeans went
off and put a number of those idiotic Foundation

03:42:31.800 --> 03:42:33.720
drones in the hospital for months.

03:42:33.720 --> 03:42:38.220
Serves them right for continually meddling
in the matters of forces they couldn’t even

03:42:38.220 --> 03:42:39.120
hope to understand.

03:42:39.120 --> 03:42:40.739
And today…

03:42:40.739 --> 03:42:43.500
They were feeding it the carcass of a dead
cow.

03:42:43.500 --> 03:42:45.720
SCP-682 sighed.

03:42:45.720 --> 03:42:48.180
It felt sometimes that the dolts testing it&nbsp;

03:42:48.180 --> 03:42:50.820
had forgotten the note&nbsp;
reading “Highly Intelligent”

03:42:50.819 --> 03:42:51.660
on its file.

03:42:51.660 --> 03:42:56.519
Being dragged into one of these ghastly chambers
and given some form of novel stimulus could

03:42:56.520 --> 03:43:01.320
only mean one thing: Something stupid and
painful was going to happen.

03:43:01.319 --> 03:43:06.420
Said stupid, painful thing, in this case,
was that the cow was spiked with an instance

03:43:06.420 --> 03:43:11.760
of SCP-3521 - also known as The Banana Pill,
by dado.

03:43:11.760 --> 03:43:18.720
What followed was a remarkably absurd instance,
even by SCP-682 cross-test standards, where

03:43:18.720 --> 03:43:22.560
a huge number of bananas spontaneously burst
out of 682’s body.

03:43:22.560 --> 03:43:28.140
Being a big fan of bananas, apparently, 682
was actually able to eat and metabolize the

03:43:28.140 --> 03:43:32.161
bananas faster than the anomalous Banana Pill
- by dado - could produce them.

03:43:32.160 --> 03:43:37.920
And because bananas are each, individually,
slightly radioactive, 682 was able to synthesize

03:43:37.920 --> 03:43:42.480
this collective radiation into a powerful
death ray that it used to cause a great deal

03:43:42.479 --> 03:43:43.679
of death and destruction.

03:43:43.680 --> 03:43:48.900
As far as Dr. Zharkov, and the rest of the
SCP Foundation, were concerned, this thing

03:43:48.899 --> 03:43:53.160
being cleaved apart on an atomic level by
the Gate Guardian couldn’t come soon enough.

03:43:53.160 --> 03:43:57.540
Sometimes, it took the ultimate knight to
slay the ultimate dragon.

03:43:57.540 --> 03:44:03.359
Not long after that, SCP-682 was dosed up
on enough sedatives to give New York City

03:44:03.359 --> 03:44:09.239
a week-long nap, and carted over to Site 0
on a heavily secured armored convoy.

03:44:09.239 --> 03:44:12.420
Taking SCP-682 this far between containment&nbsp;

03:44:12.420 --> 03:44:15.239
sites was considered a&nbsp;
matter of grave seriousness.

03:44:15.239 --> 03:44:20.219
In other words, the results of this little
experiment better have been good to justify

03:44:20.220 --> 03:44:24.600
the insane security risk it took to even get
the damn lizard out here.

03:44:24.600 --> 03:44:30.660
Dr. Zharkov and Dr. Clef decided to co-supervise
the cross test, from the safety of the Site

03:44:30.659 --> 03:44:31.920
0 observation deck.

03:44:31.920 --> 03:44:36.420
Either would have to be beyond foolish to
want to get any closer - Even Dr. Clef, while

03:44:36.420 --> 03:44:39.540
undeniably a loose cannon, didn’t have an
outright death wish.

03:44:39.540 --> 03:44:44.160
Unless, of course, wishing death on SCP-682
would count.

03:44:44.160 --> 03:44:49.920
682’s sedated body was strapped to a large,
unmanned vehicle - the kind they might use

03:44:49.920 --> 03:44:55.080
for an exploratory mission on another planet
- and sent in the direction of the Gate Guardian’s

03:44:55.080 --> 03:44:56.760
deadly proximal zone.

03:44:56.760 --> 03:45:01.680
A secondary camera drone was also sent in
to lag behind, correctly predicting that,

03:45:01.680 --> 03:45:06.960
when the Gate Guardian struck SCP-682, it
would obliterate the unmanned vehicle, too.

03:45:06.960 --> 03:45:11.160
And whatever happened out there, the Foundation
needed it on camera.

03:45:11.160 --> 03:45:16.680
Dr. Zharkov had sweaty palms and gritted teeth,
seeing the culmination of his professional

03:45:16.680 --> 03:45:18.300
career unfold in front of him.

03:45:18.300 --> 03:45:20.820
Dr. Clef was looking at a meme on his phone.

03:45:20.819 --> 03:45:27.359
As 682 got closer, it began hearing a booming
voice in its head, just like the Founder had

03:45:27.359 --> 03:45:28.620
so long ago.

03:45:28.620 --> 03:45:34.620
The voice simply said one word, over and over,
getting louder as the unmanned vehicle brought

03:45:34.620 --> 03:45:38.220
the two titans closer and closer and closer.

03:45:40.279 --> 03:45:41.279
“DIE.”

03:45:41.279 --> 03:45:46.859
682, still feeling groggy, thought, “Oh,
if it onlywere so simple…”

03:45:46.859 --> 03:45:52.559
And then it happened: SCP-682 entered the
dreaded one-kilometer range.

03:45:52.560 --> 03:45:57.000
The Guardian slashed down with its mighty
sword, creating a brilliant flash of light.

03:45:57.000 --> 03:46:02.580
In the aftermath, the unmanned vehicle was
obliterated, and 682 was left heavily injured

03:46:02.580 --> 03:46:05.700
on the ground, still trying to process what
had just happened.

03:46:05.700 --> 03:46:11.460
682 looked up, sobered by the pain, and saw
the being that had dealt this blow.

03:46:11.460 --> 03:46:13.859
682 began to sneer.

03:46:13.859 --> 03:46:16.319
“Is this meant to be the Garden?”

03:46:16.319 --> 03:46:19.319
it said, before breaking into a venomous laugh.

03:46:19.319 --> 03:46:23.639
“This is not the Garden.

03:46:23.640 --> 03:46:26.340
The Garden is far west of here.”

03:46:26.340 --> 03:46:31.739
The Gate Guardian struck again with its flaming
blade, once again projecting that single word,

03:46:31.739 --> 03:46:36.120
“DIE, DIE, DIE, DIE, DIE…”

03:46:36.120 --> 03:46:41.880
When the smoke cleared, 682 was even more
horrifically injured, with only one limb left,

03:46:41.880 --> 03:46:45.060
but still, against all odds, alive.

03:46:45.060 --> 03:46:50.880
It used the one limb to drag itself towards
the Gate Guardian, fueled by pure rage and

03:46:50.880 --> 03:46:51.300
spite.

03:46:51.300 --> 03:46:52.440
“Die?

03:46:52.439 --> 03:46:55.259
You command me to die?

03:46:55.260 --> 03:47:02.400
Oh, wouldn't we all like that, but this is
my curse for suggesting the fruit,” the

03:47:02.399 --> 03:47:03.120
reptile growled.

03:47:03.120 --> 03:47:06.359
Back at the base, Dr. Zharkov was mortified.

03:47:06.359 --> 03:47:08.880
How could it possibly be surviving all this?

03:47:08.880 --> 03:47:12.000
The sword was meant to cleave apart its victims
on an atomic level!

03:47:12.000 --> 03:47:12.960
Atomic!

03:47:12.960 --> 03:47:14.939
As in, freaking atoms, god damn it!

03:47:14.939 --> 03:47:18.000
Dr. Zharkov wished he had a paper bag to breathe
into.

03:47:18.000 --> 03:47:23.279
Dr. Clef, showing an uncharacteristic degree
of compassion, patted Zharkov on the back,

03:47:23.279 --> 03:47:27.239
saying, “It’s okay, buddy, we all remember
our first time.”

03:47:27.239 --> 03:47:32.099
Back at the center of the action, the Gate
Guardian blasted the 682 with its solar blade

03:47:32.100 --> 03:47:32.280
again.

03:47:32.279 --> 03:47:38.160
Somehow, despite the terrifying power wielded
by the Guardian, 682 continued to live.

03:47:38.160 --> 03:47:44.340
It was alive, barely, but after three strikes
from the sword, to be alive was whatever the

03:47:44.340 --> 03:47:46.800
evil version of a miracle would be.

03:47:46.800 --> 03:47:55.620
“This is not the Garden, and you are not
Uriel,” 682 roared, before spitting at the

03:47:55.620 --> 03:47:56.220
Gate Guardian.

03:47:56.220 --> 03:47:57.600
“Pretender.”

03:47:57.600 --> 03:48:04.201
One more violent strike from the Gate Guardian
and 682 finally collapsed, unconscious from

03:48:04.200 --> 03:48:06.540
the extent of its pain and its injuries.

03:48:06.540 --> 03:48:11.160
But despite all of Dr. Zharkov’s hopes,
the Gate Guardian did not strike a killing

03:48:11.160 --> 03:48:12.960
blow on the unconscious beast.

03:48:12.960 --> 03:48:19.620
Instead, it transmitted another word, another
order, impossible for any human being to ignore.

03:48:21.140 --> 03:48:22.140
“REMOVE.”

03:48:22.140 --> 03:48:28.740
As though in a trance, the workers of Site
0 - including Dr. Zharkov and Dr. Clef - entered

03:48:28.739 --> 03:48:31.439
the forbidden one-kilometer exclusion zone.

03:48:31.439 --> 03:48:36.299
The Gate Guardian allowed them safe passage,
as they used tools and vehicles to pick up

03:48:36.300 --> 03:48:41.520
the heavily injured SCP-682 and cart it away
from the Gate Guardian’s feet.

03:48:41.520 --> 03:48:46.621
After they all came back to their senses,
Dr. Zharkov simply said, “What just happened?”

03:48:46.620 --> 03:48:48.479
Dr. Clef just shrugged.

03:48:48.479 --> 03:48:50.339
“I’ve learned to stop questioning it.”

03:48:50.340 --> 03:48:52.560
Greetings, brave adventurers!

03:48:52.560 --> 03:48:55.560
Seekers of knowledge, explorers of the great
unknown!

03:48:55.560 --> 03:49:00.060
No doubt by now you have heard the stories
of the noble Lord Theodore Thomas Blackwood,

03:49:00.060 --> 03:49:05.400
gentleman explorer and naturalist, also known
as SCP-1867.

03:49:05.399 --> 03:49:10.439
His exploits are known far and wide, though
some question the validity of his tales, due

03:49:10.439 --> 03:49:14.040
to the simple fact that he is a neon sea slug
and not a human man.

03:49:14.040 --> 03:49:15.030
Bah!

03:49:15.030 --> 03:49:16.931
These are, of course, fools!

03:49:16.930 --> 03:49:16.979
A gentleman never lies about his grand escapades!

03:49:16.979 --> 03:49:23.399
We have even covered Lord Blackwood before,
in “A Sea Snail's Fantasy SCP-1867 - A Gentleman,”

03:49:23.399 --> 03:49:27.779
but never before have we taken a look at such
a daring account of his work.

03:49:27.779 --> 03:49:31.019
Today we discuss a most&nbsp;
curious hunting expedition,&nbsp;

03:49:31.020 --> 03:49:33.541
one that brought our Lord Blackwood face to

03:49:33.540 --> 03:49:38.939
face with the great beast, the hard-to-destroy
reptile, SCP-682 itself!

03:49:38.939 --> 03:49:40.859
What will become of our hero?

03:49:40.859 --> 03:49:42.779
What sights will he see on his journey?

03:49:42.779 --> 03:49:44.160
Let us find out.

03:49:44.160 --> 03:49:45.270
Tally-ho!

03:49:45.270 --> 03:49:50.880
On May 14, 1883, months after nearly losing
his life while climbing Mt.

03:49:50.880 --> 03:49:54.359
Everest, Lord Blackwood received a letter
at his London home.

03:49:54.359 --> 03:50:00.059
Upon opening it, he saw that it was a formal
invitation from one Colonel Joseph D’Enfante,

03:50:00.060 --> 03:50:01.560
of the French Army.

03:50:01.560 --> 03:50:07.020
It invited him to participate in a hunt for
a monster known as The Tarasque, that threatened

03:50:07.020 --> 03:50:09.121
the lives and security of the French people.

03:50:09.120 --> 03:50:14.220
Anyone who was able to slay the creature would
receive a handsome award of five million pounds

03:50:14.220 --> 03:50:14.760
for their trouble.

03:50:15.420 --> 03:50:19.440
Unable to resist a challenge, the chance to
face off against a creature he had never heard

03:50:19.439 --> 03:50:24.779
of before, or the allure of such an impressive
prize, Lord Blackwood sent off an acceptance.

03:50:24.779 --> 03:50:26.759
So what was the Tarasque?

03:50:26.760 --> 03:50:31.920
Lord Blackwood’s research turned up a fearsome
description: it was a massive scaly creature

03:50:31.920 --> 03:50:36.420
with a hide that seemed impossible to pierce,
that breathed fire and killed everything in

03:50:36.420 --> 03:50:37.920
its path without batting an eye.

03:50:37.920 --> 03:50:39.840
A worthy foe indeed.

03:50:39.840 --> 03:50:43.500
By the end of the day, Lord Blackwood had
received an address where he would attend

03:50:43.500 --> 03:50:45.300
a briefing before the hunt would commence.

03:50:45.300 --> 03:50:49.620
The meeting was held at a private room in
the city, in an exclusive club.

03:50:49.620 --> 03:50:55.739
There were three other would-be hunters there,
Mr. Roosevelt from America, Mr. Dukov, from

03:50:55.739 --> 03:50:58.019
Russia, and Mr. Harris, from England.

03:50:58.020 --> 03:51:01.140
The Colonel greeted the men, and told them
what they were up against.

03:51:01.140 --> 03:51:06.960
A beast had lain waste to a French town, ripping
men, women, and children to shreds and resisting

03:51:06.960 --> 03:51:09.060
every blow dealt against it by the army.

03:51:09.060 --> 03:51:14.220
So, the Colonel vowed to gather expert scientists
and hunters, for if they could not take down

03:51:14.220 --> 03:51:17.040
the monster, it was likely that no one could.

03:51:17.040 --> 03:51:21.660
On May 20th, the party arrived in France to
begin the great adventure.

03:51:21.660 --> 03:51:26.880
Each man brought his own armaments, a combination
of specialized weapons and knowledge, for

03:51:26.880 --> 03:51:27.720
the task at hand.

03:51:27.720 --> 03:51:32.340
The following day, the Colonel escorted the
men to the quarantine zone, where the beast’s

03:51:32.340 --> 03:51:33.239
attack had led it.

03:51:33.239 --> 03:51:37.080
Lord Blackwood was troubled by the sights
there, it was a city at war.

03:51:37.080 --> 03:51:40.859
Soldiers patrolled the streets, and barricades
were placed at the edge of town.

03:51:40.859 --> 03:51:46.259
Citizens were being evacuated as soldiers
aided them, and few had seen the beast themselves.

03:51:46.260 --> 03:51:49.560
At least, they had not been unfortunate enough
to see it up close.

03:51:49.560 --> 03:51:52.980
Beyond the quarantine barrier, it was hell
on earth.

03:51:52.979 --> 03:51:58.080
There were bodies laying in the streets, buildings
burnt to the ground, castles and stone walls

03:51:58.080 --> 03:51:59.640
reduced to piles of rubble.

03:51:59.640 --> 03:52:05.161
There was not one living thing in sight, not
a person, a farm animal, or even so much as

03:52:05.160 --> 03:52:05.880
an insect.

03:52:05.880 --> 03:52:11.040
The men set up camp near the edge of the town,
and Mr. Harris set about tracking the beast.

03:52:11.040 --> 03:52:13.859
Before too long, he had&nbsp;
found it, to the southwest,&nbsp;

03:52:13.859 --> 03:52:16.319
and the next day they would set off after

03:52:16.319 --> 03:52:16.559
it.

03:52:16.560 --> 03:52:21.180
The next day, the party made its way southwest
to Belleville, following a trail of destruction.

03:52:21.180 --> 03:52:23.820
There, they found it having a nap in the sun.

03:52:23.819 --> 03:52:28.620
It was longer than a whale, taller than a
giraffe, and bigger than both.

03:52:28.620 --> 03:52:33.599
Lord Blackwood thought that, if it had any
visible wings, he would consider it a dragon.

03:52:33.600 --> 03:52:37.201
They approached slowly, careful not to wake
the Tarasque.

03:52:37.200 --> 03:52:42.840
Lord Blackwood crouched behind a fence, steadied
his gun, and fired right at its head.

03:52:42.840 --> 03:52:46.560
The shot hit, and the top of the Tarasque’s
head came off with its impact.

03:52:46.560 --> 03:52:51.661
It seemed as if the beast was, after so much
pomp and circumstance, dead right there.

03:52:51.660 --> 03:52:54.359
But sadly, it was not.

03:52:54.359 --> 03:52:59.580
It sprang to life, blood and brains dripping
from its open skull as it turned to the men

03:52:59.580 --> 03:53:01.439
and roared, then charged.

03:53:01.439 --> 03:53:06.419
The men scattered, firing their guns as they
ran, the monster gaining on them faster and

03:53:06.420 --> 03:53:10.739
faster until Mr. Dukov fired into its open
wound with an electric rifle.

03:53:10.739 --> 03:53:14.340
It was stunned long enough for the men to
make it onto their horses.

03:53:14.340 --> 03:53:19.680
As they rode away, the monster continued to
chase them, new skin and bone growing over

03:53:19.680 --> 03:53:21.900
what had once been a hole in its skull.

03:53:21.899 --> 03:53:27.479
Lord Blackwood fired a particle destabilizer
at its leg, tearing it off, but as he watched

03:53:27.479 --> 03:53:30.660
in horror…the leg began to grow back.

03:53:30.660 --> 03:53:35.880
The hunting party managed to escape with their
lives, though their confidence was thoroughly

03:53:35.880 --> 03:53:36.420
shaken.

03:53:36.420 --> 03:53:39.300
They rested that night with the soldiers at
the barricade.

03:53:39.300 --> 03:53:43.800
They attempted to attack the Tarasque again
the following day, but failed once more.

03:53:43.800 --> 03:53:47.160
The men realized that a&nbsp;
simple gunshot, electrocution,&nbsp;

03:53:47.160 --> 03:53:49.739
or fire would not be enough to kill the monster.

03:53:49.739 --> 03:53:54.179
It simply healed too fast, and its tolerance
for pain was too high.

03:53:54.180 --> 03:53:59.340
In order to kill it, they realized, they would
have to render it immobile and destroy its

03:53:59.340 --> 03:54:03.060
body so thoroughly that it would die before
it could rebuild itself.

03:54:03.060 --> 03:54:07.081
And so, they decided to set a trap.

03:54:07.080 --> 03:54:12.300
They dug a massive trench, wide and long enough
for the monster, and deep enough that it would

03:54:12.300 --> 03:54:14.820
not be able to climb out before they had killed
it.

03:54:14.819 --> 03:54:20.160
In the bottom of the pit, they placed hundreds
of steel spikes, the tips dipped in poison.

03:54:20.160 --> 03:54:24.840
They placed a bridge across it, strong enough
for the men and horses but weak enough to

03:54:24.840 --> 03:54:28.739
break under the Tarasque’s weight, and covered
it all with grass and leaves.

03:54:28.739 --> 03:54:31.620
Now, they just had to wait.

03:54:31.620 --> 03:54:36.899
Mr. Roosevelt acted as bait, approaching the
monster on horseback and attacking it with

03:54:36.899 --> 03:54:39.839
a gunshot, then running and leading it back
toward the trap.

03:54:39.840 --> 03:54:44.460
As Roosevelt raced across the bridge, the
creature pursued him, and fell into the pit

03:54:44.460 --> 03:54:46.199
where it was impaled on the spikes.

03:54:46.199 --> 03:54:48.720
Then, the men rained down hellfire.

03:54:48.720 --> 03:54:52.380
They shot it with bullets, explosives, jellied
kerosene.

03:54:52.380 --> 03:54:58.800
Mr. Dukov fired a pitchblende-gun that, upon
firing, released a blur of smoke and fire.

03:54:58.800 --> 03:55:02.880
Once the fire had receded, all that remained
was a skeleton.

03:55:02.880 --> 03:55:08.819
The men took the skull, charred from the flames,
and planned to take it back as a trophy.

03:55:08.819 --> 03:55:10.080
All was well!

03:55:10.080 --> 03:55:12.420
Or so it seemed…

03:55:12.420 --> 03:55:17.279
The men returned to the town with the monster’s
skull in tow, and the soldiers cheered at

03:55:17.279 --> 03:55:17.639
the sight.

03:55:17.640 --> 03:55:22.020
They posed for photographs, and Mr. Dukov
decided to pose with his head between the

03:55:22.020 --> 03:55:22.920
jaws of the beast.

03:55:22.920 --> 03:55:28.080
This was a grave mistake on his part, and
the jaws closed tight around his neck, his

03:55:28.080 --> 03:55:29.160
head falling to the ground.

03:55:29.160 --> 03:55:35.699
The skull acted on its own, rolling and biting,
all the while growing fresh skin and scales.

03:55:35.699 --> 03:55:45.869
It opened its gaping maw and shouted: “"Vous
me rendez malade.”

03:55:45.870 --> 03:55:50.400
Screams rang out behind Lord Blackwood and
he turned to see…the rest of the Tarasque’s

03:55:50.399 --> 03:55:56.219
body, a headless corpse covered with stringy
bits of muscle and slowly growing brand new

03:55:56.220 --> 03:55:56.699
flesh.

03:55:56.699 --> 03:56:01.800
It stomped through the field, crushing men
and tents beneath its great feet on its way

03:56:01.800 --> 03:56:03.000
to reclaim its head.

03:56:03.000 --> 03:56:07.439
Mr. Harris ran for the bank vault, to grab
a weapon he had only referred to previously

03:56:07.439 --> 03:56:09.599
as “his secret weapon.”

03:56:09.600 --> 03:56:14.580
Lord Blackwood chased after him, and found
Harris pulling a large crate, which he opened

03:56:14.580 --> 03:56:15.899
with a sense of desperation.

03:56:15.899 --> 03:56:21.899
There, inside, was a sarcophagus, bound in
chains and covered in ancient runes.

03:56:21.899 --> 03:56:26.879
Blackwood begged Harris to leave the thing
behind and run for his life, but he did not

03:56:26.880 --> 03:56:31.560
have a chance to finish before Harris opened
the lid, and an arm wielding a sword emerged

03:56:31.560 --> 03:56:33.840
and sliced his head from his body.

03:56:33.840 --> 03:56:39.180
A man emerged from the sarcophagus, naked,
wielding a sword, covered in tattoos.

03:56:39.180 --> 03:56:43.800
Blackwood had no way of knowing this, but
the man was none other than the deadly warrior

03:56:43.800 --> 03:56:47.340
SCP-076, or Able.

03:56:47.340 --> 03:56:51.779
The mysterious man attacked Blackwood and
Roosevelt, and though they tried to defend

03:56:51.779 --> 03:56:54.540
themselves, no weapon seemed to have an effect
on him.

03:56:54.540 --> 03:56:59.040
He was preparing to deliver a final blow to
Blackwood, and kill him once and for all,

03:56:59.040 --> 03:57:02.880
when the Tarasque burst through the wall of
the building with a mighty bellow.

03:57:02.880 --> 03:57:08.460
At the sight of the enormous monster, Able
turned his focus from the two men to the beast.

03:57:08.460 --> 03:57:14.520
And so, the two seemingly unkillable creatures,
driven by bloodlust and inhuman strength,

03:57:14.520 --> 03:57:15.960
began to fight.

03:57:15.960 --> 03:57:19.920
It took over an hour, and left destruction
and death in its wake.

03:57:19.920 --> 03:57:24.899
Able armed himself with explosives, mounting
them to his chest along with the pitchblende

03:57:24.899 --> 03:57:27.000
gun, and ran toward the Tarasque.

03:57:27.000 --> 03:57:31.680
Knowing what would come next, Roosevelt and
Blackwood locked themselves in the bank vault,

03:57:31.680 --> 03:57:34.920
and prayed that someone would find them before
they starved to death.

03:57:34.920 --> 03:57:40.680
After two days, the men were saved by a major
of the army, who was leading a group of soldiers

03:57:40.680 --> 03:57:42.240
in a search for any survivors.

03:57:42.239 --> 03:57:46.739
They were taken to the hospital, and nursed
back to health by the staff there as well

03:57:46.739 --> 03:57:48.599
as a friend of Blackwood’s named Henry.

03:57:48.600 --> 03:57:53.400
The major who rescued them told them that
Colonel was dead, and so were ten thousand

03:57:53.399 --> 03:57:55.559
others claimed by the massive explosion.

03:57:55.560 --> 03:58:01.440
The Tarasque and Able had both disappeared,
and there was no indication of where either

03:58:01.439 --> 03:58:02.460
of them had gone.

03:58:02.460 --> 03:58:07.500
All that was left was destruction and the
memory that a true monster had made itself

03:58:07.500 --> 03:58:09.120
known on French soil.

03:58:09.120 --> 03:58:14.279
Now, the only thing left to do was recover,
as best as anyone could.

03:58:14.279 --> 03:58:17.519
It would certainly take a very long time.

03:58:17.520 --> 03:58:23.161
The army was very suspicious of both Roosevelt
and Blackwood, as the only survivors of an

03:58:23.160 --> 03:58:26.639
explosion so large it had been seen throughout
France.

03:58:26.640 --> 03:58:31.440
They demanded to know how the two had survived,
and what they had seen.

03:58:31.439 --> 03:58:36.839
Throughout this process, an Englishman watched
and took notes, but did not speak a word.

03:58:36.840 --> 03:58:41.340
Roosevelt and Blackwood were eventually released,
but they did not receive a penny of their

03:58:41.340 --> 03:58:45.840
promised reward, and were told they could
not return to France again for the rest of

03:58:45.840 --> 03:58:46.560
their lives.

03:58:46.560 --> 03:58:51.720
They were not to speak a word of what they
had seen to anyone, or there would be dire

03:58:51.720 --> 03:58:52.500
consequences.

03:58:52.500 --> 03:58:57.779
In Calais, the two survivors said goodbye,
and Roosevelt announced he would return to

03:58:57.779 --> 03:59:00.059
America to pursue a career in politics.

03:59:00.060 --> 03:59:02.460
Who can say what happened to him after that?

03:59:02.460 --> 03:59:07.260
Upon returning to his home in London, Lord
Blackwood found that he had received a postcard.

03:59:07.260 --> 03:59:12.840
It read: “The Royal Foundation for the Security,
Containment, and Protection of Anomalous Objects

03:59:12.840 --> 03:59:18.180
and Phantasmagoria requests a meeting for
the purpose of negotiating an alliance favourable

03:59:18.180 --> 03:59:19.380
to both our parties.

03:59:19.380 --> 03:59:25.500
Please call any time (except Sundays) at No.
19 Marylebone Road, Westminster, and ask to

03:59:25.500 --> 03:59:26.399
speak to Doctor Thursday.

03:59:26.399 --> 03:59:29.040
Your discretion is requested in this matter.”

03:59:29.040 --> 03:59:32.279
He was puzzled by this note, unsure of what
to make of it.

03:59:32.279 --> 03:59:34.859
Perhaps, he thought, he could see what they
had to say.

03:59:34.859 --> 03:59:38.399
After all, he was always curious and ready
to explore new territory.

03:59:38.399 --> 03:59:43.259
Once he had recovered sufficiently, he would
reach out to this strange group and see what

03:59:43.260 --> 03:59:44.640
they might have to offer him.

03:59:44.640 --> 03:59:50.820
And so began a new chapter of Lord Blackwood’s
story, one that included a mysterious organization

03:59:50.819 --> 03:59:53.219
called The SCP Foundation.

03:59:53.220 --> 03:59:59.220
Now go check out “A Sea Snail's&nbsp;
Fantasy SCP-1867 - A Gentleman”&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:59:59.220 --> 04:00:05.100
and “SCP-682 - Ways SCP Foundation&nbsp;
Tried to Kill Hard To Destroy Reptile”&nbsp;&nbsp;

04:00:05.100 --> 04:00:09.121
for more about the two anomalies&nbsp;
featured in today’s thrilling tale!

